\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-Russia likely to buy yuan on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in 2023 - sources\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2022\par 15:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This content was produced in Russia where the law restricts coverage of Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 By Elena Fabrichnaya\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 22 (Reuters) - Russia will start buying yuan on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market next year if oil and gas revenues meet expectations, two sources said, opening a new front in an accelerating dedollarisation drive designed to reduce its dependency on Western finance.\par \par \uc2 Western sanctions on Moscow over its actions in Ukraine have curbed its use of and access to dollars and euros, and the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's role in Russia's economy is growing fast.\par \par \uc2 Daily yuan-rouble trading volumes on the \uc2 Moscow Exchange\uc2  are already exceeding dollar-rouble trades on some days, according to Refinitiv data, a trend set be to accentuated in 2023 as an oil embargo and price cap squeeze Russia's traditional export routes.\par \par \uc2 Russia stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in February due to restrictions imposed on its use of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves after it sent tens of thousands of troops into \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume next year in yuan, the two sources told Reuters, provided that revenues from oil and gas exports exceed 8 trillion roubles as set out in budget plans.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can currently now buy yuan," a banking source close to monetary authorities told Reuters. But the bank would not do so while the government continued, as now, to spend its oil and gas revenues.\par \par \uc2 "(However), if next year budget revenues from the export of oil and gas exceed 8 trillion roubles, then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy yuan," that source added.\par \par \uc2 Under the budget rule, designed to replenish state reserves, oil and gas revenues above that figure are currently directed to the National Wealth Fund (\uc2 NWF\uc2 ), which Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  has said is equivalent to oil prices of $62-63 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Russia has for years adopted conservative fiscal policies and sought to run budget surpluses, but is on course for a deficit of 2% of GDP this year as Moscow ramps up spending to finance its military campaign in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Siluanov's ministry expects 900 billion roubles in additional hydrocarbon revenues next year, though analysts, wary of the impact of export restrictions, are sceptical.\par \par \uc2 'FRIENDLY' \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 A senior government source confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  next year would be in yuan.\par \par \uc2 "We have a lot of friendly \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On the exchange, the Chinese yuan is the most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is the friendliest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far," the source said.\par \par \uc2 Russia considers countries that have not joined in with Western sanctions as "friendly".\par \par \uc2 The banking source said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with yuan would be protected from sanctions and freezing. Russian government assets worth around $300 billion have been frozen since the conflict in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  began.\par \par \uc2 The government source said a decision about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the framework of the budget rule was needed in order to start accumulating reserves, and as soon as authorities adopted the plan, it would be announced.\par \par \uc2 At the start of this year, the yuan accounted for 17.1% of Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves, the most recent available data. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  last week said Russia has sufficient funds in yuan and gold.\par \par \uc2 The yuan, or renminbi, has already enjoyed a dramatic acceleration into Russia's markets and trade flows, with its share of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reaching 48% in November, MOEX Group said last week, up from less than 1% at the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 Moscow Exchange\uc2 , Russia's largest bourse, will expand the range of yuan instruments it offers next year, changes the exchange's head Yuri Denisov said would enable traders to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk and increase yuan liquidity.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya; additional reporting and writing by Alexander Marrow; editing by John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-22T15:25:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221222eicm02761\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
