\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Euro traded below the dollar for the first time in two decades\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 ? The EU \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to its worst level due to fears of economic recession in Europe and uncertainty in the supply of Russian gas.Photo Ap Clara Zepeda Peri\u243\'00\'F3dico La JornadaThursday, July 14, 2022, p. 17Theeuro broke the one dollar level for the first time in two decades, falling to 0.9998 dollars, before recovering to trade at 1.0061. This is the worst level for the continent's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since December 2002. The situation could worsen if the energy price shock triggered by the conflict in Ukraine pushes the bloc into a protracted economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 This comes as fears of an economic recession in Europe are growing in the markets, against a backdrop of high inflation and increasing uncertainty about the continuity of Russian gas supplies.\par \par \uc2 Gone are the years when the euro was so strong (1.6 times the dollar during the 2008 global financial crisis) that many Europeans went on vacation to the United States because of the low prices in hotels and food, and returned home with suitcases full of electronics and clothes. But now the situation is completely different, with Europe suffering the economic consequences of the war in Ukraine and the decision of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ) to maintain interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Thus, there is concern that this crisis could cause a recession with unsuspected consequences, a shadow that intensified on Monday with the reduction of Russian gas supplies and the concern that inflation will continue to rise.\par \par \uc2 According to analysts, the EU \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost ground against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2021, but this was accentuated after Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , taking into account the low economic growth in the euro zone and a less restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has also caused distrust in the euro.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220714ei7e005bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
