\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia.War Russia Ukraine day 65: Minute by minute what's happening live\b0\par\par\uc2 1,174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The war between Russia and Ukraine has reached its 65th day, since its beginning on February 24, when the Russian president sent military troops to carry out a "special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to liberate the Donbas region.\par \par \uc2 That he himself declared as independent territories Lugansk and Donetsk, part of this region.\par \par \uc2 On the 65th day of this war, just over two months, during the visit of \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2 , the Secretary General of the \uc2 United Nations\uc2  (\uc2 UN\uc2 ), Russia shelled Kiev on Thursday, April 28.\par \par \uc2 You can also readInternationalWorld War III: China calls for dialogue between Russia and Ukraine to avoid itInternationalRussia applies sanctions to 29 Americans, including Mark Zuckerberg and Kamala HarrisInternationalFor sinking of Russian Ship Moskova in the Black Sea, Russia launches attack on KievOnhis visit on Thursday, \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2  lamented the "failure" of the Security Council to avoid the conflict\par \par \uc2 .Also in other international support for Ukraine, U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  asked Congress for $33 billion in additional aid for Ukraine, of which more than $20 billion will go to military assistance.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , this aid is not to attack Russia, but to assist Ukraine in defending itself against Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , on Thursday criticized Russia for making "idle" claims about the possible use of nuclear weapons in the Ukrainian conflict, and said that such assertions showed "desperation" on the part of the country administered by \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite \uc2 UN\uc2  attempts to end this war and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , attacks continue between the two nations.\par \par \uc2 It is recorded that after withdrawing from the north and the vicinity of Kiev, the Russian offensive concentrated in the south and east of the country.\par \par \uc2 In addition, during the visit of \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2  it is reported that at least one person was killed in the Russian attack on Kiev, reported Friday the mayor of the city, \uc2 Vitali Klitschko\uc2 , on Telegram.\par \par \uc2 U.S.lower house approves \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to give more weapons to Ukraine with a law dating back to World War IITheU.S.lower house approved last Thursday a legislative measure that allows the country's president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , to use a law dating back to World War II to lend more weapons to Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .With 417 votes in favor and only 10 against, the measure was supported by both Democrats and Republicans, as was previously the case in the Senate, and allows \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to deliver weapons more quickly and with less bureaucracy to Kiev.\par \par \uc2 It is a type of legislation first used in 1941 during World War II - before the United States entered directly into that conflict - by then President \uc2 Franklin D. Roosevelt\uc2  to provide armaments to the United Kingdom Armed Forces in their fight against Germany.\par \par \uc2 That same Thursday, just hours before the House of Representatives voted in favor of the legislation, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  formally asked Congress for $33 billion in additional aid for Ukraine, of which more than $20 billion will be military assistance to defend against Russia, in the face of the possibility of a long war.\par \par \uc2 In a speech from the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  explained that it is "crucial" that Congress give the green light to this aid, because giving in to Russian aggression would be much more costly.\par \par \uc2 "Either we back the Ukrainian people to defend their country or we stand by as the Russians continue their atrocities and aggression against Ukraine. "\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  recalled that the assistance the United States has sent so far has made a difference on the battlefield and helped Ukraine "win the battle of Kiev," referring to the success of Ukrainian forces in repelling Russian advances toward the capital\par \par \uc2 .Joe Biden\uc2 's request for assistance includes, in addition to sending arms and ammunition to Ukraine, 8.5 billion in direct economic assistance and 3 billion in humanitarian aid.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian and Russian presidents invited to G20 summit: IndonesiaJokoWidodo, the president of Indonesia, informed on Friday that he invited his Ukrainian counterpart \uc2 Volodymir Zelenski\uc2  to the G20 summit in November in Indonesia, in which \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  confirmed his participation\par \par \uc2 . "I invited President Zelenski to participate in the G20\par \par \uc2 summit\u8243\'20\'33Despite Western pressure to exclude Russia, both nations were invited\par \par \uc2 .Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymir Zelenski\uc2  noted in a tweet on Wednesday that he had been invited to the summit following a telephone conversation with his Indonesian peer.\par \par \uc2 Joko Widodo\uc2  also spoke with the Russian leader on Thursday. According to the Indonesian president, at that time, President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  thanked Indonesia for the invitation to the G20 summit and said he would participate.\par \par \uc2 The G20 summit is scheduled to take place in Bali in November.\par \par \uc2 Two British humanitarian volunteers "captured" by Russian forces in Ukraine: NGOTwoBritish volunteers were "captured" by Russian soldiers in Ukraine, a non-profit organization called Presidium Network and the family of one of the imprisoned aid workers reported Friday\par \par \uc2 .Paul Urey and Dylan Healy were "captured" by Russian soldiers on Monday at a checkpoint south of the town of Zaporiyia in southwestern Ukraine, Presidium Network said.\par \par \uc2 The volunteers were operating independently to try to help Ukrainians flee and were arrested while assisting a woman and her two children in Zaporiyia.\par \par \uc2 The organization said it offered to help Urey and Healy after receiving reports of their work on the ground, but clarified that the volunteers were not affiliated with its network in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Presidium Ntework reported that Urey is a seasoned humanitarian worker who spent eight years in Afghanistan and reported that Healy, born in 2000, worked in the kitchen at a hotel chain in the UK.\par \par \uc2 The NGO confirmed that it is working with the British Foreign Office.\par \par \uc2 Russian economy to contract by 8-10% this year due to sanctionsTheRussian economy will contract by 8-10% this year due to Western sanctions imposed on Russia for its military campaign in Ukraine, marking the worst drop in Russian GDP since 1994, when the country's GDP contracted by 12.7%\par \par \uc2 .Despite this possible decline, the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its main interest rate this Friday, April 29, from 17% to 14%, as it estimated that "risks to prices and financial stability ceased to increase".\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had dramatically raised its rate to 20% following the first Western sanctions against Russia over the invasion of Ukraine in late February, had already cut the interest rate a first time to 17% on April 8.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, had also fallen to record lows against the dollar and the euro, but has recovered.\par \par \uc2 Also the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that current growth rates of consumer prices have slowed significantly after peaking in the first half of MarchAccording to\par \par \uc2 the bank, this is due to the "strengthening of the ruble and the cooling of consumer activity."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recorded year-on-year inflation of 16.5% in March, a level it has not seen since 2015.\par \par \uc2 The bank forecasts that this year inflation could reach 23%, before slowing in 2023\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220429ei4t00cv9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
