\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: Putin's government warns that alleged Ukrainian attack on its territory will affect negotiations\b0\par\par\uc2 12,193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 EN VIVONews in DevelopmentTheKremlin estimated on Friday that the attack perpetrated according to Moscow by Ukrainian helicopters on Russian territory against a fuel depot will affect bilateral negotiations to end the offensive in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 07:41\par \par \uc2 Russia considers that Ukrainian attack on its territory will affect negotiations According to the governor of the Belgorod region, the fire at the oil depot was caused by a Ukrainian airstrike. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin estimated Friday that the attack perpetrated according to Moscow by Ukrainian helicopters on Russian territory on a fuel depot will affect bilateral negotiations on ending the offensive in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "It is clear that this cannot be considered as something that will create appropriate conditions for the continuation of negotiations," Dmitry Peskov, spokesman for the Russian presidency, estimated after the dawn destruction of a depot in the Belgorod region bordering Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 07:30\par \par \uc2 Death toll rises to 28 in Russian attack on official headquarters inMikolaivRussian soldiers, in the instant before kicking in the door to enter the property they were to inspect in Mikolaiv\par \par \uc2 The death toll in Tuesday's attack on\par \par \uc2 the headquarters of the regional administration in the southern Ukrainian city of Mikolaiv\par \par \uc2 rose to 28, Ukraine's State Emergency Service (SES) reported today.Speaking to the Ukrainian news agency Ukrinform, Ilyana Patsyuk, spokeswoman for the SES, said that at 10:50 a.m. on April 1 the provisional toll of the Russian rocket attack that hit and destroyed the regional administration headquarters was 28 dead.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 07:39\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 05:29\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  and China launch virtual summit focusing on war in UkraineTheEuropean Union (EU) and China launched on Friday a summit via videoconference in which the war in Ukraine and economic relations between the two sides will take center stage, \uc2 EU\uc2  sources reported\par \par \uc2 .The first working session brought together the presidents of the European Council, \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2 , and of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , with the Chinese Premier, \uc2 Li Keqiang\uc2 , while for a second meeting is scheduled the participation of the President of China, \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , is also taking part in the summit.\par \par \uc2 The meeting is marked by the Russian invasion of Ukraine, as the \uc2 EU\uc2  expects "assurances" from Beijing that it "does not intend to offer economic lifeline or other support to Russia" during the strife.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 04:28\par \par \uc2 Already 153 Ukrainian children killed by the warTheUkrainian Prosecutor General's Office reported that 153 Ukrainian children have already been killed\par \par \uc2 by thewar with Russia. In addition, "more than 245" were injured by the armed conflict.\par \par \uc2 Most of the affected children resided in the regions of Kiev, where the Ukrainian capital is located; in Donetsk, self-proclaimed independent republic and close to the Russian border, and in the city of Kharkov, in the northeast and the region of Chernigov, in the north, all of them heavily hit by Russian bombardments.\par \par \uc2 The Prosecutor's Office reports that it is trying to collect data on the number of children killed and wounded in the besieged Mariupol, a port city in the south of the country, from which almost two-thirds of its population have fled.\par \par \uc2 According to the Prosecutor General's Office, Russian shelling and attacks damaged, so far, 859 educational establishments\par \par \uc2 in Ukraine.01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 03:55\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claims to have repelled seven attacks in Donetsk and LuganskTheUkrainian Army claimed in a report to have repelled seven attacks in Donetsk and Lugansk\par \par \uc2 . On theother hand, it was indicated that in the last 24 hours the resistance destroyed 3 tanks, 2 armored personnel carriers, 2 artillery systems and shot down an Orlan drone-10.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 03:45\par \par \uc2 Already 24 dead from attack on Mikolaiv administrationTheState Emergency Service reported that already 24 dead from the Russian attack on the Mikolaiv regional administration building\par \par \uc2 .Rescuers pulled out 23 bodies from the rubble and another person died in the hospital.\par \par \uc2 Inaddition, the number of wounded amounted to 33.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 03:12\par \par \uc2 Ukraine carried out the first attack on Russian soil, they claimAccording toRBC media, the governor of Belgorod, Vyacheslav Gladkov, claimed that Ukraine carried out the first attack on the territory of Russia.Through Telegram, he assured that two helicopters of the Ukrainian Armed Forces shelled during the early hours of Friday morning an oil depot in Belgorod, 40 kilometers from the Ukrainian border. As a result of the attack, part of the building caught fire and two people were reportedly injured. The flames have not yet been contained. Several videos of what would be the moment of the attack went viral on social networks.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 02:46\par \par \uc2 Ukraine accuses Belarus of using its territory to emplace missilesTheUkrainian government denounced that the territory of Belarus is being used by Russia to emplace and accumulate missile systems, as warned by the Deputy Minister of Defense, Hanna Maliar\par \par \uc2 . "Russian forces are actively using the territory of Belarus to carry out aggressive actions against Ukraine, relocating their missile systems in the Homel region," she specified.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 02:04\par \par \uc2 Ukraine assures Russia desists from invading Kiev and focuses onMariupolRussian troops have for the time being abandoned the occupation of Kiev and are now concentrating on the assault on the port of Mariupol, according to a report issued early this morning by the General Staff of the Ukrainian armed forces\par \par \uc2 ."The enemy, which has suffered significant losses in personnel and equipment, failed to blockade and capture the city of Kiev\par \par \uc2 . The occupants were forced to temporarily abandon this task," says the Ukrainian army's part, published at the end of the thirty-sixth day of the Russian invasion of Ukraine.The Russian army "focused on continuing the assault on the city of Mariupol\par \par \uc2 . " 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 01:26\par \par \uc2 UK reported that Russia is deploying troops in Georgia to join the invasion of Ukraine."Between 1,200 and 2,000 of these Russian troops are being reorganized into 3 battalion tactical groups," the \uc2 UK Ministry of Defense\uc2  reported. As it analyzed, "it is highly unlikely that Russia plans to generate reinforcements in this way and is indicative of the unexpected losses it suffered during the invasion."\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 00:59\par \par \uc2 Australia to send armored vehicles toUkraineAustralian Prime Minister Scott Morrison announced Friday that he will send Bushmaster armored vehicles to Ukraine after Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  specifically requested them during a video conference with Australian lawmakers\par \par \uc2 .Morrison reported that the vehicles will be sent on \uc2 Boeing\uc2  C-17 Globemaster transport aircraft, but did not specify how many vehicles it would send or when.\par \par \uc2 01.04.2022\par \par \uc2 00:21\par \par \uc2 Zelenski dismissed two generals for "disloyalty" to the UkrainianpeopleUkrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\par \par \uc2 reported that he dismissed two generals for violating the military oath of allegiance, based on the disciplinary statute of the Armed Forces of Ukraine.The head of the main internal security department of the \uc2 Security Service of Ukraine\uc2 , Naumov Andriy Olehovich, and the head of the office of the \uc2 Security Service of Ukraine\uc2  in the Kherson region, Krivoruchko Sergiy Oleksandrovich, were dismissed.\par \par \uc2 "Now I do not have time to deal with all traitors. But gradually they will all be punished," Zelensky assured during his usual evening speech, in which he has also thanked the "national heroes" for defending the state, Europa Press agency reported.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 23:49\par \par \uc2 Russian tanks destroyed on the outskirts ofKievWar\par \par \uc2 tanksdestroyed on the outskirts of Kiev. AP Photo/Rodrigo Abd.\par \par \uc2 Destroyed Russian tanks\par \par \uc2 line a road outside the Ukrainian capital, where Ukrainian soldiers pose for selfies on the frame of one of the vehicles after overrunning a Russian position.An 81-year-old man rides alone on a bicycle next to a charred tank on the muddy road.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 23:29\par \par \uc2 Russian troops blocked 45 buses evacuating civilians from MariupolTheUkrainian government said Russian forces blocked 45 buses sent to evacuate civilians from Mariupol, with only 631 people managing to leave the city\par \par \uc2 in private vehicles.Twelve Ukrainian trucks were able to transport humanitarian supplies to Mariupol, but were seized by Russian forces, said Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to Ukrainian officials, tens of thousands of people have left Mariupol in recent weeks along humanitarian corridors, reducing the number of inhabitants from 430,000 before the war to about 100,000 last week.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 23:02\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on fuel price hike due to "fault" of Vladimir PutinTheUS president, via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , said he knows that "gas prices hurt" and argued that the measures he will take will "ease the pain today and protect you tomorrow."\par \par \uc2 " I will continue to use every tool at my disposal to protect you from Putin's price hikes. And I am asking Congress to put partisanship aside. Let's face this moment together," the US president added.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 22:58\par \par \uc2 How a hospital protected wounded Ukrainian soldiers Anton Dovgopol, the director of the polyclinic in the city of Irpin, told how they protected Ukrainian soldiers who entered the medical center wounded by the attacks of Russian forces\par \par \uc2 ."The hospital staff dressed them in civilian clothes, gave them fake name tags and hid their IDs so that they would not become targets if the Russians broke in," he recounted.\par \par \uc2 "We put the policemen who guarded the hospital in white robes, otherwise they could be shot dead," he added in an interview with The Kiev Independent.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 22:10\par \par \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  also disbelieves Russian withdrawal: "There will be battles ahead"After Russian soldiers withdrew from the north and center of the country, the Ukrainian president assured that the situation has intensified in the southeast, where Russian forces "are preparing for new powerful attacks" and that this withdrawal is just another tactic\par \par \uc2 ."We must realize that this is also part of the tactics of the Russian Armed Forces. It is not occasional, we know their plans," he reiterated.\par \par \uc2 "We know they are moving away from those areas where we are attacking them to focus on other very important areas. Where it could be difficult for us," the president analyzed.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:55\par \par \uc2 At a FIFA congress, Ukraine called for an end to the warTheUkrainian soccer leader appeared dressed in an armored vest on the streets of Kiev, and referred to the impact of the war launched by Russia against his country, in a video shown on Thursday during the FIFA congress\par \par \uc2 ."We have regularly received sad news about the deaths of members of the Ukrainian soccer community, \uc2 Andriy Pavelko\par \par \uc2 said in his recorded message to the leaders gathered in Qatar, who included delegates from Russia."They have been killed by the rockets of the aggressors, one of the largest armies in the world. Soccer has taken a back seat in our country," he assured.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:40\par \par \uc2 Zelenski on Russians: 'They don't look like humans, they look like from another world; monsters that burn and plunder'President of Ukraine \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 . Reuters photo.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president said in a video on Telegram that the Russians "come with a lot of evil and thirst for destruction."\par \par \uc2 "They don't look like humans, they look like from another world. Monsters who burn and loot and try to murder," he described. "But when you're on your land, everything helps you: the land, the rivers, every inhabitant, even those you wouldn't have thought would," he assured.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:26\par \par \uc2 Julio Alga\u241\'00\'F1arazAnalysis\par \par \uc2 : \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's back and forth on gas raises tension in EuropeAnincredible back and forth by President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  about payment in euros and dollars or only in rubles from European countries for their gas purchases created an even more alarming climate on Thursday about the development of the crisis in the wake of Russia's invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .Read more\par \par \uc2 . 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:13\par \par \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  President is on her way to KievRobertaMetsola\par \par \uc2 announced Thursday that she is "on her way" to the Ukrainian capital, without specifying further details for security reasons."On my way to Kiev," tweeted the Maltese politician in a terse message in English and Ukrainian, accompanied by the hashtag #StandWithUkraine.\par \par \uc2 She also posted a photo of herself in the foreground staring at the camera, looking serious and wearing a black jacket, with the open door of a train carriage visible in the background from the platform.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 20:50\par \par \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 : "We endured much more than the enemy expected "In a post on his Telegram account, the Ukrainian president said, "We endured much more than the enemy expected."\par \par \uc2 "They said three to five days. They thought this would be enough for them to take over our entire state. And it's 36 now. And we are standing. And we will continue to fight," he assured.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 20:39\par \par \uc2 Russian opera canceled soprano over comments on Ukraine The Novosibirsk Opera in Siberia canceled a concert it had scheduled for June 2.\par \par \uc2 The cancellation was of a concert by Russian lyric star Anna Netrebko\par \par \uc2 over her comments on the military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched by Moscow in neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 20:22\par \par \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  pointed to Russia's impunity for the downing of MH17 and how it led to the invasion of UkraineTheUkrainian president recalled in his speech in the Parliament of Australia the Russian impunity in downing of \uc2 Malaysia Airlines\uc2  flight MH17, which occurred on July 17, 2014\par \par \uc2 .In addition, he insisted on the need to improve the capabilities of international institutions to hold war criminals accountable.\par \par \uc2 As compiled by Ukrinform agency, he spoke about the plane shot down by pro-Russian rebels from the Donbas region, in the Ukrainian sky that killed 298 people and stressed that the perpetrators of the tragedy have not yet been brought to justice.\par \par \uc2 "They are hiding in Russia. And, obviously, they received security guarantees from the Russian state. Did Russia pay compensation to the victims' relatives? No. It continues to deny its guilt in the tragedy," Zelenski said.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 20:06\par \par \uc2 Marie-Pierre\par \par \uc2 OlphandEconomicconsequences\par \par \uc2 : can Europe do without diamonds produced by Russia? " Asking diamond traders to do without Russian diamonds is a bit like telling them that drinking water is of Russian origin and that they should no longer drink it." With these almost drastic words, a Paris trader sums up how the gemstone trading sector depends on those coming from Russia.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the disputes over the gas that Moscow sells to much of Europe and which is in the midst of controversy and uncertainty in the context of the war in Ukraine, the diamond market is also suffering the consequences. And it is torn between what position to take in relation to international sanctions against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Read more\par \par \uc2 .31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 19:49\par \par \uc2 Canada opposes Russia's presence at the upcoming G20 Canada's Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 . Reuters photo.\par \par \uc2 Canada's Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  estimated that Russia should not be at the next G20 meeting because that country cannot be considered a "constructive partner".\par \par \uc2 "I don't think we can sit with Russia around the table" he explained and said he had discussed the issue with the Indonesian president, who is chairing the G20 this year.\par \par \uc2 "It doesn't make any sense to have a discussion about global economic growth if the country responsible for a large part of the downside is at the table," Trudeau added.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 19:31\par \par \uc2 Ukraine: more U.S. weapons, other materials arriveThe Pentagon said half a dozen shipments of weapons and other materials arrived in Ukraine as part of the $800 million aid package that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  approved on March 16.\par \par \uc2 John Kirby, a spokesman at U.S. Defense Department headquarters, said the shipments include Javelin anti-tank weapons, Stinger anti-aircraft missile systems, body armor, medical supplies and other materials. He added that the 100 Switchblade drones that Biden approved under the plan have not been delivered.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 19:13\par \par \uc2 Oil falls nearly 7%It cameafter U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced that he will allocate 180 million barrels of crude oil from the reserves\par \par \uc2 The U.S. market to alleviate the local market over a six-month period.Contracts for delivery in May of the WTI barrel fell 6.99% to 100.28 dollars, while in London the Brent barrel, also for May, fell 6.44% to 107.91 dollars.\par \par \uc2 Biden announced that in the next 180 days he will release one million barrels per day "to increase supply (...) until production accelerates at the end of the year".\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:30\par \par \uc2 Russian troops withdrew from the Chernobyl plantRussian troops left the Chernobyl power plant they had occupied since the beginning of the invasion of Ukraine on February 24, Ukrainian authorities announced Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 View of the protective arch over the damaged reactor 4 of Ukraine's Chernobyl nuclear power plant. Photo EFE/ Oleg Petrasyuk\par \par \uc2 "There are no outsiders of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant on this territory anymore," the Ukrainian state agency for the management of the power plant zone said on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:26\par \par \uc2 Biden orders unprecedented release of crude oil stocks to contain its price due to the war in UkraineU.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced today that the release of one million barrels of crude oil per day from its strategic reserves and for six months would "relieve" households in the face of rising fuel prices in that country as a result of the Russian invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  expects this release to serve as a "bridge" until the end of the year. AFP photo.\par \par \uc2 "This record release will provide a historic amount to serve as a bridge until the end of the year, when domestic production increases," added the note from the Presidency, which hopes that this release will serve as a "bridge" until the end of the year and that domestic production will manage to supply the demand.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:03\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  warned that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  would have fired or put under house arrest several of his advisersU.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said that his Russian counterpart, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , could be "isolated", and that he would have fired or put under "house arrest" some of his advisors, although he indicated that there is no irrefutable evidence of this.\par \par \uc2 Read more.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 16:50\par \par \uc2 With the war, Ukraine's grain harvest may be cut in halfDevastated or shelled fields, workers who left to fight, ruined logistics: the Russian invasion may halve the grain harvest in Ukraine, crucial for world food, warned the Ukrainian Minister of Agriculture in an interview with the AFP agency.\par \par \uc2 Although Ukraine harvested a record 106 million tons of grain last year, this year the figure will be "25% to 50%" lower, warns Minister Mykola Solsky. "And that is an optimistic forecast," he added.\par \par \uc2 31.03.2022\par \par \uc2 16:30\par \par \uc2 Paula Lugones\par \par \uc2 U.S. to rel