on.\par \par \uc2 "With all due respect, if there are to be no weapons, if there are to be no sanctions, if there are to be no restrictions on Russian companies, then please find another job,'' Zelenskyy said in his speech.?He added: "I am waiting for concrete results in the next few days on the work of our representatives in Latin America, the Middle East, Southeast Asia and Africa.''\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 22:07\par \par \uc2 Ukraine and Russia to resume negotiations on FridayNegotiations between Ukraine and Russia in search of a peace agreement will resume on Friday via videoconference, reported David Arakhamia, leader of the ruling party in the parliament. The two sides held a face-to-face meeting on Tuesday in Istanbul, after two weeks of negotiations via video, and the first outlines of a possible peace deal appeared to emerge.The Ukrainian delegation offered a framework under which the country would declare neutrality, dropping its aspirations to join \uc2 NATO\uc2  - something Moscow has long demanded - in exchange for security guarantees from third nations.?Russian diplomats responded positively to Ukraine's proposal.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:46\par \par \uc2 Russia is alleged to be using anti-personnel mines that are banned A Ukrainian serviceman searches for mines in the city of Kharkov. AFP photo.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian army technicians detected that Russian forces used anti-personnel mines in Kharkov.Russia is known to possess these recently deployed landmines, which can indiscriminately kill and maim people within a range of 16 meters. The 1997 International Mine Ban Treaty comprehensively prohibits the use, production, stockpiling and transfer of anti-personnel mines. Russia is not among the 164 countries that have acceded to the treaty.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 20:43\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian army's crude video: a recaptured city with destroyed houses, abandoned cars and corpses in the streetsThe official