\par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 19:25\par \par \uc2 U.S. believes Russia's peace talks are a strategy to buy timeUkrainian militiamen ready their weapons in the Kiev region. Reuters photo.\par \par \uc2 The United States doubts Russia's words. While different analysts maintain that this impasse is in fact a strategy to gain time and regroup. "Russia is not in a position to negotiate seriously because it has to do better in war," said \uc2 Fran\u231\'00\'E7ois Heisbourg\uc2 , a French defense analyst at the Foundation for Strategic Research. "This is an opportunity for the Russians to consolidate, to regroup, to withdraw from places outside their logistical reach, where they have already run out of food and ammunition." Some senior Western officials agreed, saying the Russians were very short of artillery shells and other ammunition and needed to resupply.Read more\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 19:00\par \par \uc2 Ukraine accuses Russian forces of firing phosphorus bombsOne of the images released by the mayor of Irpin, \uc2 Oleksandr Markushyn\uc2  when denouncing white phosphorus attacks.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian authorities again accused Russian forces of firing phosphorus bombs in the eastern Ukrainian town of Marinka."A dozen fires were localized and controlled by the personnel of the National Emergency Situations Service," said the head of the Donetsk region military administration, Pavel Kyrylenko, explaining that "the towns of Georgievka, Novokolinovo and Otcheretino were also shelled."White phosphorus is a yellowish or colorless translucent substance, with a waxy texture and a slight garlic odor, which ignites immediately on contact with oxygen in the air, thereby creating a bright plume of smoke. It cannot be extinguished with water and burns at up to 1,300 \u186\'00\'BAC.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 18:35\par \par \uc2 Six shipments of U.S. military aid arrive in UkraineThe U.S. Department of Defense announced that the first six shipments of "about 30" shipments with U.S. military aid arrived in Ukraine on Wednesday.These are, explained Pentagon spokesman John Kirby, "the materiel the Ukrainians need most, from anti-armor to anti-aircraft systems."Instead, Switchblade drones will be sent shortly, the so-called kamikaze drones that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  's administration has long announced its intention to send to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 18:11\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's popularity in Russia reaches 83%, the highest since the beginning of the conflictVladimir Putin is in one of his best moments in terms of popularity in his country.\par \par \uc2 A poll by the independent statistics institute Levada measured Putin's popularity in Russia and showed that it stands at 83 percent, the highest number in recent years, after the start of the war in Ukraine.In February the approval rating for Putin was 71 percent.?Although many independent media have been banned since the beginning of the war, so citizens are informed only by state media, the result is significant, being the poll conducted by a prestigious statistical center not controlled by the state.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:44\par \par \uc2 Russia announces ceasefire in Mariupol to evacuate civiliansMariupol is the city hardest hit by the war. \uc2 Xinhua\uc2  photo.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  announced that it will institute a "regime of silence," or ceasefire, starting at 10 a.m. Thursday (4 a.m. in Argentina) in the besieged Ukrainian port of Mariupol to evacuate civilians.?This measure should facilitate the opening of a humanitarian corridor to the Ukrainian city of Zaporiyia. "For this humanitarian \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be successful, we propose to carry it out with the direct participation of representatives of the \uc2 UN High Commissioner for Refugees\uc2  (\uc2 UNHCR\uc2 ) and the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2 ,