ricultural commodities, the price of wheat fell 4.04 percent (US$ 15.71 per ton) and ended at US$ 372.67 per ton. As for soybeans, the May contract fell 1.27 percent (US$ 7.81) to US$ 603.70 per ton, and corn fell 2.97 percent (US$ 8.76) to US$ 285.91 per ton.Read more\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 15:59\par \par \uc2 Russian Orthodox Church hopes for a face-to-face meeting with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  this yearThe Russian Orthodox Church wants \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  in person. Photo AFP\par \par \uc2 This was reported today by the Russian embassy to the Holy See by relaunching a Ria Novosti article that reports statements to this effect by Metropolitan Hilarion, head of international relations of the Moscow Patriarchate.\par \par \uc2 "Work is being done" on this meeting, he said, adding that due to the development of events in Ukraine, the Pope and the Patriarch needed to communicate, prior to the meeting being organized, even if at a distance.\par \par \uc2 In the interview he explained that "it was very important the online meeting on March 16 between the Pope and Kirill, linked to the crisis in Ukraine and that both agreed that "everything possible must be done so that the differences can be resolved peacefully".\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 15:48\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Irpin estimates that at least 200 people were killed in the city by the Russian invasionIrpin was able to drive out the Russians, but half of the city was destroyed. Photo Reuter\par \par \uc2 Irpin Mayor Oleksander Markushin estimated Wednesday that between 200 and 300 people were killed in this Ukrainian town in the Kiev region by the Russian invasion, although he could not give an exact death toll.\par \par \uc2 "There is no death toll," he said, before explaining that, with the daily shelling, citizens were "simply hiding people in yards, in parks," Ukrinform Ukrainian news agency reported him as saying.\par \par \uc2 Markushin, who put the number of people remaining in