3\par \par \uc2 US says Putin is misinformed by his entourage about the war in Ukraine For the US, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is misinformed. Photo AFP\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is misinformed about the development of the war in Ukraine because his advisersare afraid to reveal to him the military and economic losses suffered by Russia, a senior US official said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Putin didn't even know that his military was recruiting and losing conscripts in Ukraine, which demonstrates a clear disruption in the flow of reliable information reaching the Russian president," the official said on condition of anonymity, based on declassified U.S. intelligence data.\par \par \uc2 "From our point of view, Putin is misled by his advisers about the poor performance of the Russian military and the severity of the impact of sanctions on the Russian economy, because his top aides are afraid to tell him the truth," he added.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 14:40\par \par \uc2 UK bans repair of Russian oligarchs' planes and shipsGrant Shapps, UK Transport Minister, poses in front of the yacht "Phi", seized on Tuesday. Photo \uc2 Twitter\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British government\uc2  on Wednesday approved a legal instrument prohibiting the provision of technical maintenance services to vessels and aircraft owned by Russian oligarchs sanctioned as a result of the invasion of Ukraine or their companies.\par \par \uc2 London wants to prevent those subject to sanctions"frombenefiting from British industries and engineers, world leaders in the aviation and maritime sectors," the Foreign Office said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The ministry detailed that the new legal instrument has been used "immediately" to punish businessmen Eugene (Yevgueni) Shvidler and \uc2 Oleg Tinkov\uc2 , who had already appeared on British sanctioned lists.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 14:25\par \par \uc2 Spain suffers the highest inflation in 37 years due to the war in Ukraine