tanbul, whose negotiations were chaired by Turkish President Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Nothing too promising in the peace talks," Russian spokesman Dmitry Peskov said. But he promised an update later. Read more.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 13:39\par \par \uc2 Bachelet warns of Russian attacks that "could constitute war crimes" in UkraineMichelle Bachelet spoke in front of the \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  in Geneva. Photo EFE.\par \par \uc2 The United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, \uc2 Michelle Bachelet\uc2 , assessed today that the indiscriminate bombings and attacks by Russia against populated areas of Ukraine generate "immense concern" and could constitute "war crimes".\par \par \uc2 The former Chilean president spoke before the \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  in Geneva and resorted to the conditional by convention, given that the accusations must be decided by a court of law as a matter of principle.\par \par \uc2 She also urged Russia to abide by international calls and to "act immediately to withdraw its troops from Ukrainian territory". He also expressed concern about the use of weapons with wide radius of action in populated areas, causing "massive damage" among civilians.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 13:25\par \par \uc2 Germany offers to act as a guarantor of Ukraine's security if it declares neutrality and resigns from NATOSteffen Hebestreit, \uc2 German government\uc2  spokesman, looks at his cell phone. Photo EFE\par \par \uc2 Germany is willing in principle to act as Ukraine's security guarantor if Ukraine adopts a neutral status and renounces joining \uc2 NATO\uc2 , a government spokesman in Berlin said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The representative, \uc2 Steffen Hebestreit\uc2 , reported during a press conference that Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymir Zelensky\uc2  asked Chancellor \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  on several occasions whether Germany would be willing to adopt such a role.\par \par \uc2 