ainian ambassador, Eugenia Filipenko, who reiterated that Russia is committing war crimes in her country.\par \par \uc2 In the city, which "has become a symbol of Ukraine's resistance", Russian forces have killed around 5,000 people, while 160,000 people are still living without electricity, heating or ways to communicate with the outside world, said the Ukrainian ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  in Geneva.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 12:05\par \par \uc2 U.S. astronaut returns to Earth in shadow of Ukraine conflictInternational Space Station (ISS) crew member \uc2 NASA\uc2  astronaut Mark Vande Hei is taken to a medical tent shortly after landing. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 U.S. astronaut Mark Vande Hei and Russian cosmonauts Anton Shkaplerov and Pyotr Dubrov arrived on Earth Wednesday aboard Soyuz MS-19 from the International Space Station (ISS), whose future is increasingly uncertain due to sanctions imposed on Russia over its campaign in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "They landed - welcome back, Anton and Pyotr!" could be read on the screen of the Russian Flight Control Center, which added in English, "Welcome back, Mark!"\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 11:37\par \par \uc2 In Ukraine they claim that Abramovich "is an effective mediator".Abramovich was a mediator at the first face-to-face meeting between Russia and Ukraine. Photo Turkish Presidency via AP.\par \par \uc2 Roman Abramovich\uc2  is "an extremely effective mediator between the delegations" of Ukraine and Russia, Kiev negotiator and advisor to President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2 , Mikhailo Podolyak, told Ukrinform agency today.Abramovich "partly moderates the process, so that there are no misunderstandings", as can happen "when one side says something and the other side is not so clear about it, in terms of organization of the negotiating process," Pdolyak explained\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 11:20\par \par \uc2 Moscow shelled the Red Cross building in Mariupol and they claim the city is about to fallA building of the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  (\uc2 ICRC\uc2 ) was targeted by Russian shelling in Mariupol, a besieged strategic port city in southeastern Ukraine, a Ukrainian official said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The occupiers deliberately shelled an \uc2 ICRC\uc2  building in Mariupol," Liudmila Denisova, head of human rights in the Ukrainian parliament, wrote in Telegram. Read more.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 10:37\par \par \uc2 "There is nothing promising in the negotiations," Moscow says The Kremlin said bluntly Wednesday that there is no sign of a breakthrough in the ongoing peace talks between Russia and Ukraine, dousing with a bucket of ice water all expectations of a possible ceasefire, generated Tuesday at negotiations in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 Spokesman Dmitry Peskov spent Wednesday morning telling reporters that Russia had noticed "nothing really promising," adding that there was a long period of work ahead. Read more.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 10:02\par \par \uc2 Death toll rises to 13 in Russian attack on official building in MikolaivThe death toll in Tuesday's Russian attack on an official building in the southern Ukrainian city of Mikolaiv rose to 13, Ukrinform agency reported Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A man seen through the front glass of a damaged car after a Russian attack in the residential area of Mikolaiv. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 Chairwoman of the Mikolaiv Regional Council Hanna Zamaziyeva said on her Telegram account that rescue work is continuing and that so far emergency services "have pulled the bodies of 13 victims out of the rubble."\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 09:44\par \par \uc2 IAEA\uc2  chief \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2  visits a Ukrainian nuclear power plant to warn about safetyRafael Grossi, after crossing the border between Romania and Ukraine. Photo: \uc2 IAEA\par \par \uc2 The director general of the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ), Argentine \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2 , met Wednesday with officials at the South Ukraine Nuclear Power Plant to discuss how the \uc2 UN\uc2  can help prevent an atomic accident in the country attacked by Russia.\par \par \uc2 "I am at the South Ukraine Nuclear Power Plant to meet with Ukrainian government officials and staff, and begin \uc2 IAEA\uc2  technical assistance for the safety of the country's nuclear facilities," Grossi wrote on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account. Read more.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 09:37\par \par \uc2 Russia strikes near Kiev and another city despite its promisesRussian forces attacked areas around Kiev and another Ukrainian city overnight, officials said Wednesday, justhours after Moscow promised to ease military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  there . The violence dampened optimism about possible progress in talks to end the war.\par \par \uc2 The wreckage of a Russian armored personnel carrier (APC) and military vehicles are seen on the front line near Kiev as the Russian invasion of Ukraine continues. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 Russia did not specify what the reduction in activity would look like, and while the pledge initially raised hopes for a way out of the bloody war of attrition, Ukraine's president and others warned that the pledges could be mere lip service.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 09:14\par \par \uc2 The largest exodus in Europe since the Second War: Ukrainian refugees already exceed 4 million. Ukrainians who have fled their country due to the war, mostly women, children and elderly people, passed the four million mark on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN Refugee Agency\uc2  (\uc2 UNHCR\uc2 ) offered this data, when the thirty-fifth day of war has been reached, which registers relevant activity in places like Kiev and Chernikov, where Russia said it would lower the intensity of its actions. Read more.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 08:52\par \par \uc2 Russia and Ukraine downplay expectations of an early end to the war despite promising negotiationsRussia on Wednesday ruled out a quick end to its invasion of Ukraine, after the Ukrainian government and Western countries greeted with skepticism a Russian announcement of reduced military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  thanks to progress in peace negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  said he saw no reason to believe Russia's announcement that it was reducing its military activity around Kiev, Ukraine's capital, and also northern Chernigov, given what continues to happen on the ground.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 08:30\par \par \uc2 Russia shelled a Red Cross building in MariupolA building of the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  (\uc2 ICRC\uc2 ) was targeted by Russian shelling in Mariupol, a besieged strategic port city in southeastern Ukraine, a Ukrainian official said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 This satellite image distributed by \uc2 Maxar Technologies\uc2  shows destroyed apartment buildings and houses east of Mariupol, Ukraine. AFP photo.\par \par \uc2 "The occupants deliberately shelled an \uc2 ICRC\uc2  building in Mariupol," Liudmila Denisova, head of human rights in the Ukrainian parliament, wrote in Telegram. "At the moment, we have no information about casualties," she added, without specifying how many people might have been in the building at the time of the shelling.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 08:12\par \par \uc2 Russia to buy back $2 billion in bonds, but will pay in rubles Russia will buy back $2 billion worth of bonds tomorrow, Thursday, which were due to mature next April 4, although it intends to make the payment in rubles and not in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which they were issued, the dollar, the \uc2 Russian Finance Ministry\uc2  confirmed.\par \par \uc2 In its official Telegram account, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  adds that "payment of the value of the bonds, including coupon income accrued to the date of payment, will be made on March 31, 2022 in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Russian Federation at the official exchange rate of the Bank of Russia."\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:53\par \par \uc2 Russia says nothing "promising" after negotiations with UkraineNegotiations between the Russian and Ukrainian delegations in Istanbul on Tuesday yielded nothing "very promising" or any "breakthroughs," the Kremlin said Wednesday, throwing cold water on hopes for progress in ending the war.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment, we cannot report anything very promising or a breakthrough. There is a lot of work to be done," Russian presidential spokesman Dmitry Peskov told reporters.\par \par \uc2 30.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:30\par \par \uc2 The number of refugees from the war in Ukraine exceeds 4 million. The \uc2 UN refugee agency\uc2  reported Wednesday that more than 4 million people left Ukraine to escape the Russian invasion, a new milestone in the largest refugee crisis since World War II.\par \par \uc2 Warsaw, Poland, Ukraine refugee centers. Photo Sergio Araujo Photo Sergio Araujo / Envoy Clar\u237\'00\'EDn\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN High Commissioner for Refugees\uc2  (\uc2 UNHCR\uc2 ) reported on its website that 4.01 million Ukrainians left Ukraine since the beginning of the Russian offensive on February 24.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220401ei410051a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
