\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ\uc2  ramps up battle to defend yield cap even as weakening yen raises economic risk\b0\par\par\uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 09:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Reuters) -The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  kept up its relentless quest to defend a key yield cap by offering to buy unlimited amounts of 10-year government bonds on Tuesday, underscoring its resolve to keep policy ultra-loose and putting downward pressure on the yen.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the stakes for policymakers in the world's third-largest economy as Japan tries to navigate the rising cost of imports from a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global fallout of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 The bond market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in line with an announcement the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  made on Monday to offer unlimited bond buying from Tuesday to Thursday to keep the 10-year Japanese government bond (JGB) yield from rising above an implicit 0.25% cap it sets around its 0% target.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  made two offers on Tuesday, after the first in the morning failed to push down yields much. Combined, the offers drew bids worth 528.6 billion yen ($4.28 billion).\par \par \uc2 The 10-year JGB yield stood at 0.245% on Tuesday, hovering near the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's implicit 0.25% cap despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some analysts doubted if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can sustain its bond-buying action for a prolonged period.\par \par \uc2 "Theoretically the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  can protect 25 basis-point upper bound through unlimited fixed-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But at the same time, I think this situation is not sustainable," said Kentaro Koyama, chief economist at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "In the short term, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  can continue unlimited purchasing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But if the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  continues to be challenged by the market, I think it may be the trigger to adjust their yield curve control."\par \par \uc2 Struggling to swim against the tide of rising interest rates globally, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  staunchly defended its 0.25% yield cap on Monday with a rare step of offering to buy unlimited sum of 10-year JGBs at 0.25% twice in a single day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then announced its plan for consecutive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will last until Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Aside from the offer to buy unlimited amount of 10-year JGBs at 0.25%, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  may also conduct unscheduled buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  for super-long bonds if yields for the maturity spike, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "With regard to the outright purchases of JGBs...the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  may change the schedule and amounts of the purchases as needed, taking account of market conditions," the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  said in Monday's statement announcing its plan for fixed-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Underlining the selling pressure JGBs faced, the yield curve steepened at the longer end. The yields for 20-, 30- and 40-year notes all rose to their highest levels since 2016.\par \par \uc2 Under yield curve control, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  guides short-term rates at -0.1% and the 10-year JGB yield around 0%.\par \par \uc2 YEN CHALLENGE\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's aggressive efforts to cap yields pushed the yen to six-year lows against the dollar, which could add to the strains facing households and retailers by inflating already soaring raw material import costs.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of the government's growing alarm over the yen's fall, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat said Tokyo has discussed dollar-yen moves with Washington, and the two sides agreed to communicate closely on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen's decline likely won't discourage the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  from defending its yield cap, said Toru Suehiro, senior economist at \uc2 Daiwa Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's message to prevent interest rate rises is a very strong one with no consideration to the weak-yen effect its action could cause," said Suehiro.\par \par \uc2 Deputy Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Seiji Kihara\uc2 , among the closest aides to Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , said on Sunday the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  must maintain its massive stimulus as dealing with cost-push inflation with policy tightening is difficult.\par \par \uc2 In a sign fiscal policy will play a bigger role in cushioning the blow from rising raw material costs, Kishida ordered his cabinet on Tuesday to compile a fresh relief package.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 123.4400 yen)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Additional reporting by Junko Fujita and Tom Westbrook; Editing by Jacqueline Wong, Shri Navaratnam and Kenneth Maxwell) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-3-29T07:10:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220329ei3t00cnl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
