d as the British Lion, the illustrious leader replied, "The British lion was the people, I only gave the roar."\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 05:22\par \par \uc2 At least 4 killed, 6 wounded in shelling near Lugansk At least four people were killed, including two children, and six others were wounded in a Russian attack on the locality of Rubikhne near Lugansk, eastern Ukraine, This was reported Thursday by the governor of the region, Sergei Gaidai\par \par \uc2 .The governor added that the death toll risked "rising sharply" and accused the Russians of using phosphorus bombs. Other regional officials had already made similar accusations in the preceding days, information that has so far been impossible to verify.\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 05:07\par \par \uc2 Russia claims it took control of the Kharkov town ofIziumRussian Defense Ministry spokesman Igor Konashenkov said in the first morning military briefing that "by the morning of March 24 Russian Armed Forces detachments took full control of the town of Izium in the Kharkov region."\par \par \uc2 Konashenkov said that during the night Russian aviation destroyed 60 military targets in Ukraine, including four weapons depots and two drones.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, since the start of the military offensive a month ago, Russian forces eliminated 257 unmanned aerial vehicles, 202 anti-aircraft missile systems, 1,572 tanks and other armored fighting vehicles, 160 multiple rocket launchers, 633 field artillery and mortars, as well as 1,379 units of Ukrainian special military vehicles.\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:53\par \par \uc2 In one month of invasion, Russia attacked 87 residential buildings in KievAccording tothe Kiev government, Russia attacked 87 residential buildings in the Ukrainian capital\par \par \uc2 inthe month since the invasion\par \par \uc2 .In addition, they reported attacks on 10 private houses, 12 schools and 6 kindergartens\par \par \uc2 .24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:43\par \par \uc2 Ukraine confirmed the destruction of a Russian ship in BerdyanskThepicture of the burning ship, released by the \uc2 Ukrainian Defense Ministry\par \par \uc2 .A few hours after the first reports of explosions in the port of Berdyansk, the \uc2 Ukrainian Defense Ministry\uc2  confirmed that it "temporarily" destroyed a large Russian ship.\par \par \uc2 "The large landing ship Orsk of the Russian occupiers' Black Sea Fleet was temporarily destroyed in the Russian-occupied port of Berdyansk," that Ukrainian agency celebrated.\par \par \uc2 Berdyansk, a coastal city located on the shores of the Sea of Azov in the southeast of the country, is used by Russia to deliver supplies to troops occupying Mariupol, some 80 kilometers away.\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:30\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 NATO\uc2 , Putin made "a grave mistake" by invading UkraineStoltenbergspoke to the press, ahead of the \uc2 NATO\uc2  summit in Brussels. Photo Kenzo Tribouillard / AFPThe\par \par \uc2 secretary general of the \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO)\uc2 , \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2 , opined that Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  made a "grave mistake" with the invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .Russia "is facing greater resistance than it expected" in Ukraine, Stoltenberg said, ahead of a \uc2 NATO\uc2  summit in Brussels at which the military alliance will seek to reorganize the defense of its eastern flank. Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  will participate in the meeting via videoconference.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Stoltenberg warned that a Russian chemical attack in Ukraine would "greatly change the nature" of the war and could also affect neighboring allied countries. "I'm not going to speculate beyond the fact that \uc2 NATO\uc2  is always ready to defend, protect and react to any kind of attack against an allied country," he said.\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:18\par \par \uc2 Russia ratified that it will use nuclear weapons "if provoked by \uc2 NATO\uc2  "Russia's deputy ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , \uc2 Dmitry Polyanskiy\uc2 , ratified the statements issued last day by the Kremlin spokesman regarding the possibility of using nuclear weapons, assuring that his country could resort to this type of weaponry "if provoked by \uc2 NATO\uc2 "\par \par \uc2 ."If Russia is provoked by \uc2 NATO\uc2 , if Russia is attacked by \uc2 NATO\uc2 , why not, we are a nuclear power," he admitted in an interview he gave to Sky News, at the premises of the Russian mission to the \uc2 UN\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 In that address, he warned, "It's not the right thing to threaten Russia and try to interfere. Then, when it comes to a nuclear power, of course, you have to calculate all the possible results of its behavior."\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 03:51\par \par \uc2 Lithuanian President deplored Russia's "shameful actions" inUkraineLithuanian President \uc2 Gitanas Nauseda\uc2  said that Russia is carrying out "shameful actions" in Ukraine and noted that the "crimes" committed there as part of the invasion are "universally abhorred and despised."\par \par \uc2 "The countless victims of this aggressive war must not forget that they will come for the victory of the Ukrainian people," encouraged the leader of the nation that was part of the Soviet bloc.\par \par \uc2 In a video he posted on his social networks, Nauseda added: "A month ago your country was brutally attacked by Russia. Today you are standing firm and ready to repel the invaders. The Lithuanian people salute the Ukrainian heroes. They set an immortal example for all. Fighting for every inch of their land. They are an example for all of us."\par \par \uc2 24.03.2022\par \par \uc2 03:20\par \par \uc2 According to the UK, Russia seeks to replace its "considerable losses "In its usual Intelligence report on the situation in Ukraine, the \uc2 UK Ministry of Defense\uc2  slipped that Russia is