ry's official stated.\par \par \uc2 Putin has already been invited to the November G20 summit in Jakarta and intends to participate, Russia's ambassador to Indonesia assured this week\par \par \uc2 .23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 23:38\par \par \uc2 Russian military seized MelitopolairbaseRussian armed forces seized the airbase in Melitopol, a city located in southeastern Ukraine, and from there launch missiles against other cities, local mayor \uc2 Ivan Fedorov\uc2  reported on his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account\par \par \uc2 .In the same publication, Fedorov denounced that Melitopol citizens are used as living shields by the occupation troops.\par \par \uc2 23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 22:17\par \par \uc2 Russia's dead according to NATONATOestimates that between 7,000 and 15,000 Russian troops died during the four weeks of fighting in Ukraine, where the country's defenders are offering much stronger resistance than expected.A senior \uc2 NATO\uc2  military official said the estimate is based on information from Ukrainian officials and intelligence data compiled from open sources.Four weeks into the fighting, Russia is bogged down in a slow-moving military campaign, with untold numbers dead, no end in sight and its economy battered by severe Western sanctions. Read more23\par \par \uc2 .03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:56\par \par \uc2 Due to sanctions, Russia acknowledges difficulties in financing its embassies abroad This was assured by a senior official, who said it is due to problems arising from the sanctions imposed on Russia by the West. "There is a dialogue on these issues with the authorities of the countries where these arose," they explained to the Interfax news agency.\par \par \uc2 23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:45\par \par \uc2 Patricia P\u233\'00\'E9rezTribuna\par \par \uc2 : neutrality is a friend of theoppressorStates and the international community are guided by their interests or those shared with the alliances they are part of; this truism does not alter the ethical margins to be respected\par \par \uc2 .These interests, in the Western world, are usually associated with values and principles to which we adhere and which we are willing to defend, which may or may not be shared by other members of the collective that constitutes the United Nations.\par \par \uc2 Read more\par \par \uc2 .23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:37\par \par \uc2 Forest nearChernobyl power plant reported burningTheInternational Atomic Energy Agency reported that Ukraine claims a forest near the Chernobyl nuclear power plant was on fire on Wednesday evening, The Kyiv Independent reported\par \par \uc2 .23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:19\par \par \uc2 EU Council increased military aid to Ukraine to 1 billion eurosThiswas reported by the European Council website and consigns Ukrinform. The Council adopted two measures of assistance under the European Peace Fund that will enable the \uc2 EU\uc2  to continue to support the\par \par \uc2 capabilities and resilience of the Armed Forces of Ukraine.The assistance measures will increase the original budget announced on February 28, 2020 with an additional \u8364\'20\'AC500 million. This will double its initial amount to \u8364\'20\'AC1 billion.\par \par \uc2 23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 21:06\par \par \uc2 Daphn\u233\'00\'E9 Benoit\par \par \uc2 Tactical nuclear weapons, an option for Moscow?A ballistic missile at a demonstration in Moscow. Photo AFP\par \par \uc2 A frequent question since the start of the Russian invasion of Ukraine is whether Moscow could use its tactical nuclear weapons over a very limited area, which would break a taboo that has existed since 1945.\par \par \uc2 Read more.\par \par \uc2 23.03.2022\par \par \uc2 20:53\par \par \uc2 UK to deliver 6,000 more defensive missiles to UkraineBritish Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  announced that the UK will deliver 6,000 additional missiles to Ukraine, doubling its supplies of defensive weapons to the country since the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 He said this