\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Lavrov admitted that the magnitude of Western sanctions following the invasion of Ukraine surprised Russia\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov said Moscow was surprised by the scale of sanctions imposed by the Ukrainian war. This is the first time that Kremlin officials have admitted that they were not prepared for the Western response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen they froze the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves, no one who predicted the sanctions that the West was going to approve could have imagined that. It's just a robbery,\u8221\'20\'1D Lavrov told the students of the \uc2 Moscow State Institute of International Relations\uc2  , Russia's leading foreign affairs university.\par \par \uc2 The ruble fell to record lows after Western countries froze $300 billion of Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, preventing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from deploying its arsenal of support.\par \par \uc2 Russia has attempted to combat its decline by introducing strict \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls and has promised an \u8220\'20\'1Casymmetric\u8221\'20\'1D response that could include key import restrictions to \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-friendly\u8221\'20\'1D countries that have passed sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Foreign Ministers of Turkey, Russia and Ukraine attend their meeting in Antalya, Turkey, on March 10, 2022. Ministry of Foreign Affairs/Handout via REUTERS\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Lavrov warned that the deployment of \uc2 NATO\uc2  pacification forces in Ukraine would provoke military clashes between troops from Russia and the Atlantic Alliance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat will entail direct clashes between Russian and \uc2 NATO\uc2  forces, something that is not that we all want to avoid, but that we declare that they should not take place on principle,\u8221\'20\'1D he said during the university conference.\par \par \uc2 Lavrov considered the peacemaking proposal of Poland, one of Kiev's main allies and the destination of millions of refugees from the neighboring country, a provocation, and which he also accused of harboring territorial ambitions in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In addition to mentioning \uc2 NATO\uc2  's alleged plans to send to Ukraine a battalion composed of the three Baltic republics, he recalled that he had also opposed the deployment of an international force in the Donbas in due course.\par \par \uc2 He also denounced statements about the need to deploy Stinger anti-aircraft missiles in Ukraine, which, he warned, would pose \u8220\'20\'1Ca colossal threat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 U.S. troops fire a Stinger missile from their Stryker armored combat vehicle during the Saber Strike military drill in Rutja, Estonia, on March 10, 2022. Reuters/Ints Kalnins\par \par \uc2 Lavrov, in turn, accused the United States of being interested in extending \u8220\'20\'1Cas long as possible\u8221\'20\'1D the current Russian \u8220\'20\'1Callied military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey hope to continue supplying arms to Ukraine. You see that they want to keep us as much as possible in a state of combat,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He lashed out at Kiev for continually changing its position during the negotiations, during which, he suggested, the Ukrainian delegation goes hand in hand with the United States.\par \par \uc2 It framed within this strategy the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the President of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Volodymir Zelensky\uc2  , before the parliaments of several Western countries.\par \par \uc2 The President of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymir Zelensky\uc2  , addresses the \uc2 lower house of the Japanese parliament\uc2  via a video conference, amid the ongoing Russian invasion of Ukraine, in Kiev, Ukraine, on March 23, 2022. Press Service of the Presidency of Ukraine/Handout via REUTERS\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe delay (of the negotiations) is aimed at dramatizing the situation, allowing Zelensky in his khaki shirt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the parliaments of the world and after the speech with tears in his eyes to demand \uc2 NATO\uc2  interference again,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Lavrov assured that Moscow is not opposed to mediation by Western countries, but stressed that there are \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely red lines\u8221\'20\'1D that cannot be crossed.\par \par \uc2 As for the attempts to isolate his country and the pressures from the U.S. The \uc2 US government\uc2  for all world powers to join Western sanctions, replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have many friends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 (With information from EFE)\par \par \uc2 KEEP READING:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is worse than Chechnya\u8221\'20\'1D: Russian soldiers attacking Mykolaiv have frozen feet and feel abandoned\par \par \uc2 Putin and a teaching for China: the danger of a lifetime head of state\par \par \uc2 How Ukrainian refugees escaping Putin's invasion welcome in Rome\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220323ei3n004po\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
