ter the attackDespite the fact that the war was felt closely on Sunday, life in Lviv continues almost as normal. Photo: Marcelo Ferreiro\par \par \uc2 The war was felt as never before on Sunday in this city when explosions on Sunday left 35 dead in Yavoriv, just 25 kilometers away.\par \par \uc2 However, the next day the city resumed its usual rhythm even with more relaxed controls than at the beginning of the conflict.\par \par \uc2 Read more.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 18:04\par \par \uc2 Three men arrested in France for breaking into the house of Putin's former son-in-lawThey broke into a house in Biarritz belonging to the former son-in-law of Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  without permission and where they unfurled the Ukrainian flag.\par \par \uc2 The three were arrested in the framework of an investigation for "violation of domicile", and were later released. The violation took place in the villa Alta Mira, whose owner is \uc2 Kirill Shamalov\uc2 , according to a source close to the case.\par \par \uc2 Local media presented this businessman as the former son-in-law of the Russian president, following his marriage to Yekaterina Tikhonova, the youngest daughter of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:46\par \par \uc2 Fox News reporter was wounded near KievBenjamin Hall, Fox News reporter injured in Ukraine. Photo capture.\par \par \uc2 Fox News reporter Benjamin Hall was injured while reporting on the outskirts of Kiev on Monday and was hospitalized, the network itself said.\par \par \uc2 Hall is a Washington correspondent covering the \uc2 U.S. State Department\uc2  for Fox News, where he has worked since 2015.\par \par \uc2 "We have minimal details at this time, but Ben is hospitalized and our teams on the ground are working to gather more information," Fox News Media CEO Suzanne Scott said in a message to Fox employees. Fox's John Roberts read Scott's statement about Hall on air.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:32\par \par \uc2 Some 150,00 civilians evacuated by humanitarian corridors in Ukraine.Civilians are leaving Ukraine. Photo \uc2 Xinhua\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is since Russia launched the invasion of the country 19 days ago, Ukrainian authorities reported.? "We have launched 26 humanitarian corridors. Thanks to them, the collectives were able to evacuate a large number of people. We can say that we are talking about 150,000 people," said Kyrylo Tymoshenko, deputy head of the Ukrainian presidential office.\par \par \uc2 The Interfax-Ukraine news agency and AFP reported that Timoshenko specified that these corridors operate in the regions of Kiev, the capital; Sumy, 350 kilometers northeast of the capital; Kharkov, in the northeast of the country; and Zaporiyia, in the southeast.\par \par \uc2 He also assured that civilians were able to flee the fighting in the Donetsk and Lugansk regions, two Russian-speaking separatist territories in eastern Ukraine, through humanitarian corridors.\par \par \uc2 Today, moreover, in Mariupol, a port city besieged by Russian troops for days, about 160 cars left the city through a humanitarian corridor, heading for Zaporiyia, the municipality of this southeastern city specified.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:18\par \par \uc2 A young woman burst into a live Russian TV signal with an anti-war bannerAs can be seen in the video of the event, rescued in its tweet by Nexa, which unites several larger media outlets in Eastern Europe, the young woman comes up in surprise behind the hostess and reveals a banner reading, "No to war. Don't believe the propaganda. They are lying to you."Automatically, the sign stops focusing on her and gives way to an image inside a hospital.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 17:08\par \par \uc2 Russians reportedly blew up part of ammunition at the Zaporiyia nuclear power plant This was reported in Telegram by the Ukrainian National Nuclear Power Generation Company Energoatom and rescued by the local media Ukrinform.\par \par \uc2 "The Russians blew up part of the ammunition at the site of the Zaporiyia nuclear power plant near the ruins of the training center and power unit No. 1. And they plan to continue carrying out detonations at Europe's largest nuclear facility," Energoatom said.\par \par \uc2 Staff reportedly left their jobs during the explosions. "What further terrorist attacks are needed for resolute action by partners, including the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2 ?" the energy operator added.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 16:59\par \par \uc2 ICJ to announce verdict on Russian invasion Wednesday The ICJ announced Monday that it will communicate its verdict on Wednesday on the proceedings launched by Kiev, which asked the top \uc2 UN\uc2  court to order Moscow to cease its invasion of Ukraine. Russia declined to appear last week during hearings scheduled in the framework of the case before the ICJ, which will release its ruling on Wednesday in The Hague.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 16:41\par \par \uc2 The video of the attack on one of the largest shopping malls in Kiev has been publishedRussian occupation troops shelled Lavina Mall, the largest shopping mall in Kiev. This was reported from the scene by the Ukrainian brand Fox Lingerie on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The Russian military is launching artillery strikes on non-military targets. In the video you can see the remains of a missile in the middle of a children's playground. How long will this last?" they reported."...We thank the Armed Forces of Ukraine, rescuers and workers of the shopping center who eliminated the threat," they concluded the message.\par \par \uc2 In another attack on civilians, Interior Minister's aide \uc2 Anton Gerashchenko\uc2  reported on Telegram that an artillery shell hit a nine-story building in the Obolon district, causing partial destruction of the first to third floors, and fire in the apartments above.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 16:27\par \par \uc2 Ukraine again denounces that Chernobyl is without powerChernobyl plant in the background and the abandoned city of Pripyat. Reuters photo.\par \par \uc2 The Russian Army again damaged the high-voltage line carrying electricity to the Chernobyl nuclear power plant, which is again without power, Ukraine warned on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The plant had already suffered a power outage that authorities said they would clean up. "But before power was fully restored, occupation forces damaged the line that feeds the nuclear plant," the Ukrainian company that operates the facility, Ukrenergo, denounced today on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ukrenergo claimed that its technicians had repaired a high-voltage line supplying Chernobyl and the town of Slavutitch, but the line was damaged again.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, personnel working at the plant decided to carry out maintenance and safety work because of the Russian invasion. The team is made up of 210 employees who have not been able to leave the reactor area since the beginning of the invasion nor rotate to take time off "accumulating hours of work and fatigue".\par \par \uc2 In this regard, \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2 , the director general of the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ) expressed his concern: "I remain deeply concerned about safety at Chernobyl and other nuclear facilities in Ukraine," he said.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 16:12\par \par \uc2 Zelenski's condolences to the family of the American journalist killed in the warPresident of Ukraine \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  said farewell in social networks to the American journalist and documentary filmmaker, Brent Renaud, killed in the town of Irpin. "My deepest condolences to the family of Brent Renaud, who died documenting the cruelty and evil that Russia has instilled in the people of Ukharnia," the president said on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 "May Brent's life and sacrifice guide the world to fight for the forces of light against the forces of darkness," he concluded.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 15:56\par \par \uc2 Julio Alga\u241\'00\'F1araz\par \par \uc2 China and the United States meet in a climate of mistrustThis Monday began the meeting between President \uc2 Joseph Biden\uc2 's security advisor, Jake Sullivan, and the head of Foreign Affairs of the Chinese Communist Party, Yan Jiechi. It was in a rarefied and distrustful atmosphere, after the versions spread by the American media that Russia would have asked China for help in armaments to use in its war against Ukraine Continue reading\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 15:42\par \par \uc2 Attack near Polish border was made from Russian airspace, U.S. official says Cruise missiles that devastated a military base in western Ukraine and near Poland were launched from aircraft flying in Russian airspace, a U.S. defense official said Monday, specifying that a no-fly zone would not have prevented the attack.\par \par \uc2 A "couple of dozen" cruise missiles were launched at the Yavoriv base from bombers flying over Russia overnight Saturday, killing 35 people and wounding 134. The official, who spoke on condition of anonymity, said the attack was an example of how a no-fly zone over Ukraine "would have had no effect." It is a move that officials in \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 's government have been calling for.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 15:15\par \par \uc2 Slovakia expels three Russian diplomats for espionageSlovakia today announced the expulsion of three employees of the Russian embassy whom it accuses of having committed acts of espionage, Foreign Ministry sources told Efe news agency.\par \par \uc2 The Slovak government, whose secret services verified that the Russians' activities contravened "the Vienna convention on diplomatic relations", has given the three diplomats 72 hours to leave the country.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 15:06\par \par \uc2 Russia says US journalist was killed by "Ukrainian gunfire".Russian Ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  Vasily Nebenzia maintained the death of reporter Brent Renaud, shot dead in Irpin, was the responsibility of Ukraine. He also denied that he was a "journalist".\par \par \uc2 It was at a session of the Security Council, where Nebenzia devoted part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to refute different news, according to him, misrepresented. "The testimonies of the attack say that those who fired were Ukrainians," he maintained. He also said that "he was not a journalist, but a filmmaker."\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 14:59\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Can sanctions against Russia work without China?Vladimir Putin and \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 . (Photo Alexei Druzhinin / Sputnik / AFP)\par \par \uc2 Now that Western powers have imposed overwhelming economic and financial sanctions on Russia following its invasion of Ukraine, many are wondering whether China's non-participation will undermine their effectiveness. We should also ask whether rich countries can do more for the poor people in many developing countries who are the collateral damage of war and sanctions. Read more\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 14:15\par \par \uc2 Nine killed in bombing of TV tower located in the West Zone The bombed television station in Rivne. (Photo \uc2 Twitter\uc2  @InaSovsun)\par \par \uc2 Nine people were killed and nine others injured on Monday in a Russian shelling of a television tower near the western Ukrainian town of Rivne, local authorities said.\par \par \uc2 "At 16H00 GMT, we can declare 9 dead and 9 wounded," Vitaly Koval, the head of the local administration, told reporters, specifying that "two missiles" had hit the TV tower in the town of Antopil, 15 km east of Rivne, and an adjoining administrative building.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 12:58\par \par \uc2 URGENT Delegations of Russia and Ukraine agree to continue negotiations tomorrow.The Ukrainian delegation in negotiations with Russia reported Monday that talks on the war and a possible armistice were suspended with a commitment to resume them tomorrow, Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "In the negotiations we have taken a technical pause until tomorrow for additional work in the subgroups and to finalize certain definitions. Negotiations are continuing," Mikhail Podoliak, an advisor to the office of Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymir Zelensky\uc2 , assured on his Telegram account, Russian local agencies report.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 12:45\par \par \uc2 83 men trapped in a mine in DonetskA fireman looks at a fragment of a Ukrainian Tochka-U missile on a street in Donetsk, eastern Ukraine. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 An attack by Ukrainian forces in Donetsk caused a power failure in a ventilation duct at the Zasyadko coal mine, the largest in Donbass, and 83 workers were trapped inside.\par \par \uc2 "There are 83 people inside, they need to be brought to the surface," said the press service of the Ministry of Coal and Energy of the self-proclaimed pro-Russian Donetsk Republic (Dpr).\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 12:37\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is angry, frustrated and willing to escalate the war in UkraineIntelligence officials, during two days of congressional testimony, openly expressed concern about what Putin might do. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 More than two weeks into a war he hoped to dominate in two days, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is projecting anger, frustration over his military's failures and a willingness to cause even more violence and destruction in Ukraine, U.S. intelligence officials say. Read more.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 12:28\par \par \uc2 URGENT Ukraine calls for "immediate expulsion" of Russia from the \uc2 Council of Europe.Ukrainian\uc2  Prime Minister Denis Shmyhal on Monday called on the \uc2 Council of Europe\uc2  to immediately expel Russia from this human rights advocacy organization based in Strasbourg, France.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 12:01\par \par \uc2 European Union\uc2  adds \uc2 Roman Abramovich\uc2  to list of sanctioned Russian tycoonsThe list corresponds to a fourth round of EU sanctions against Russia and is expected to be published still in the day. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) will add billionaire \uc2 Roman Abramovich\uc2  and other Russian tycoons to its latest list of sanctions against those who support the invasion of Ukraine, two diplomats told AFP on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The owner of English soccer club Chelsea and the other oligarchs will be added to a list of people whose assets in the EU may be seized. The list corresponds to a fourth round of EU sanctions against Russia and is expected to be published later in the day.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 11:42\par \par \uc2 Russian oligarchs, the ace up their sleeve to "destroy" Putin? The "Stella Maris", a Russian oligarch's yacht, in Nice, France. Photo credit: AP\par \par \uc2 "The only option for Russian economic and political elites to preserve their assets and funds is to defeat Putin." The speaker is Oleksandr Novikov, the head of Ukraine's National Agency for the Prevention of Corruption (NACP). He is referring, of course, to the oligarchs, at the crossroads of preserving or losing their assets in the face of Western economic sanctions. Read more.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 11:21\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Zelensky to address \uc2 US Congress\uc2  on WednesdayUkrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  will give a virtual address to the \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  on Wednesday at 13H00 GMT amid intense shelling of his country by Russian troops, Democratic leaders of both chambers said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We look forward to the privilege of welcoming President Zelenski's address to the House and Senate and conveying our support for the people of Ukraine as they courageously defend democracy," said Lower House leader \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and her counterpart in the Upper House, ChuckSchumer, in a joint letter to lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 11:01\par \par \uc2 Pro-Ukrainian activists seized a mansion linked to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  in southern France. Two men were arrested on March 14, 2022 after breaking into and occupying the property belonging to \uc2 Kirill Shamalov\uc2 . AFP photo.\par \par \uc2 Two activists who are against Russia's invasion of Ukraine stormed over the weekend a luxury villa that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's former son-in-law owns in Biarritz, southwestern France. The intention? To take over the mansion and make it available to Ukrainian exiles. Read more.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 10:35\par \par \uc2 More than 160 vehicles leave the Ukrainian city of Mariupol through a humanitarian corridor.A woman puts her hand on the window inside a bus at the evacuation of Ukrainian. Photo EFE/Mikhail Palinchak\par \par \uc2 Some 160 vehicles were able to leave the Ukrainian city of Mariupol, besieged for days by Russian forces and pro-Russian separatists, through a humanitarian corridor on Monday, municipal authorities reported.\par \par \uc2 At around 13h00 (11h00 GMT), the column of vehicles was able to take a road linking this strategic port city on the Sea of Azov with the Ukrainian city of Zaporiyia, the Mariupol city council said on Telegram, without specifying how many people had been able to flee the city.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 10:19\par \par \uc2 Julio Alga\u241\'00\'F1araz\par \par \uc2 How \uc2 NATO\uc2  is sending weapons to the UkrainiansLed by the United States, Canada and the European NATO countries, the Western military alliance is sending highly effective light weapons to the Ukrainians to combat the Russian advance, especially their tanks and other armored vehicles.\par \par \uc2 This is a high-risk war because it can produce a Russian attack on the territory of Poland or Romania and escalate the conflict to the nuclear level. In these hours, it is being fought with increasing intensity in Ukraine. Read more.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 09:54\par \par \uc2 Pregnant woman and her baby who had become a symbol of the brutal attack on the maternity hospital in Mariupol diedThe picture of the wounded pregnant woman after the shelling of the Mariupol maternity hospital that went around the world. Photo: AP.\par \par \uc2 A pregnant woman and her baby were killed after Russia shelled the maternity hospital where she was to give birth, The Associated Press has learned. Images of the woman being transferred to an ambulance on a stretcher went around the world and symbolized the horror of an attack on the most innocent. Read more.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 09:35\par \par \uc2 Ukraine maintains ceasefire demand at the fourth round of negotiationsThe Russian and Ukrainian negotiating delegations started a new round of talks on Monday, for the first time by videoconference, in an atmosphere of some positive expectation despite the fact that Kiev's main advisor insisted in the previous hours on the need for a ceasefire and withdrawal of troops on the part of Moscow.\par \par \uc2 The start of the talks was confirmed after noon (Ukrainian time) on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account by Mikhail Podoliak, negotiator and advisor to Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelensky\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 09:14\par \par \uc2 Russia does not rule out taking "full control" of major Ukrainian citiesThe Russian military does not rule out taking full control of Ukraine's major cities, the Kremlin warned Monday, whose forces surround several of the country's urban centers.\par \par \uc2 A man rescues his dead cat from an apartment building after it was shelled in Kiev. AFP photo.\par \par \uc2 "The Defense Ministry, in order to ensure maximum safety of the civilian population, does not rule out the possibility of taking full control of major cities that are already surrounded," Russian presidential spokesman Dmitry Peskov said, assuring that so far President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has not ordered such an assault.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 08:42\par \par \uc2 Over 2.8 million people fled Ukraine because of the warDozens of refugees from Ukraine wait at the train station in Krakow, Poland, as groups of volunteers hand out food and drink. EFE/Rodrigo Jimenez\par \par \uc2 Some 2.8 million people fled Ukraine following the Russian invasion, \uc2 the United Nations Refugee Agency\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 08:33\par \par \uc2 Day 19 of the Russia-Ukraine war in photos.A member of the Emergencies Ministry of the separatist Donetsk People's Republic inspects the wreckage of a missile. Photo REUTERS/Stringer.\par \par \uc2 Pro-Russian troops in uniforms without insignia and police officers inspect the area after recent shelling in the city of Donetsk. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 A member of the Emergencies Ministry of the separatist Donetsk People's Republic inspects the wreckage of a missile that fell on the street in Donetsk city. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 People and medics help a wounded resident of a house destroyed by shelling as Russia's attack on Ukraine continues, in Kiev. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 See the full photo gallery.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 08:19\par \par \uc2 Vatican offered to mediate in the war but Russia does not respond. The top representative of Vatican diplomacy explained "that the offer of the Holy See to mediate was discussed personally in recent days with Lavrov." Photo EFE.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican Secretary of State, Italian Cardinal \uc2 Pietro Parolin\uc2 , explained on Sunday night that everything possible is being done to mediate to put an end to the conflict in Ukraine after Russia's invasion and that this is what he told the Russian Foreign Minister, \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2 , from whom he did not receive a response.\par \par \uc2 In an interview broadcast by the \uc2 Mediaset\uc2  information channel, "Tgcom", and taken up this Monday by the Vatican media, the top representative of Vatican diplomacy explained "that the offer of the Holy See to mediate was discussed personally in the last few days with Lavrov", with whom he had telephone conversations.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:52\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian attack leaves at least 16 dead in Donetsk, pro-Russian separatists say The body of a woman killed during shelling lies on a street in the city of Donetsk. Reuter photo.\par \par \uc2 Pro-Russian separatists in Donetsk, eastern Ukraine, said Monday that a Ukrainian attack left at least 16 people dead and about 20 wounded in the center of this large industrial city.\par \par \uc2 On its Telegram account, the Donetsk territorial defense posted photos showing several bloodied bodies lying in a street amid rubble.\par \par \uc2 14.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:45\par \par \uc2 New round of Russia-Ukraine talks begins The fourth round of negotiations between Russia and Ukrainebegan on Monday morning by videoconference, said \uc2 Mykhailo Podoliak\uc2 , negotiator and adviser to Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Communication (with Moscow) is still established although complicated," Podoliak wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , indicating that "both sides would express their concrete positions."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220316ei3g004gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
