\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , the head of the new Russian autocracy\b0\par\par\uc2 1,012 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 When the admirable Carlos Fayt said that "facts are not disputed", he seemed to be talking to the ideal world. A world where there is no \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who ignores the origin of Climate Change and Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez who forgets his condition of President of the Republic.\par \par \uc2 But reality no longer admits ironic or philosophical reflection. The facts have shown that a large part of the West was unable to predict the invasion of Ukraine or to understand COVID-19.\par \par \uc2 Qualified observers such as \uc2 John Sawers\uc2 , a former member of the specialized intelligence service in that country (MI6) and former British ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , who confirmed at \uc2 Oxford University\uc2  a different prognosis about \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's delusions and ambitions, dared to take a closer look at what we are seeing.\par \par \uc2 The planet has always defined the Russian President as a man educated in espionage, subjected to the shake-up of the confessional structure of Soviet communism and someone who could embrace the scripts of the nationalist ultra-right. None of his traits defined him as a leader of democratic sobriety, so why so many doubts and hesitations?\par \par \uc2 With such a profile, valid discussion required accepting that the West, and moderate Asia, were dealing with the reflexes of a dangerous autocrat.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir acquired a profile similar to that often attributed to Yuri Andropov, the former head of the KGB, who in the last stage of his life served as General Secretary of the Communist Party. Andropov gained influence for his contributions to the violent extraterritorial repression exercised by the former USSR in the 1954 Hungarian uprising, a recipe that the Kremlin used again in Czechoslovakia and Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 This also explains why, when Putin began to make his first steps after the fall of the USSR, he had in mind the appropriate recipe for "disciplining" the populations of Chechnya and Crimea.\par \par \uc2 In view of this curriculum, Vladimir is irritated by the fact that Western rulers never gave serious answers to his continuous demands for geopolitical balance.\par \par \uc2 If they had gone deeper into these questions, experts in political science and military strategy would have detected that Putin is obsessed by the desire to build a quasi-imperial vision of a backyard.\par \par \uc2 They would also have seen that the delirium is more serious than it seems, since the Russian government raised the nuclear alert level without saying a word and its Chancellor raised the language of war bluster without saying a word.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Robert Litwak\uc2 , a highly respected analyst at the Wilson Center, Moscow has what it takes. It has the largest nuclear arsenal in the world, which exceeds 6,000 usable pieces, to which it adds the inventory of tactical weapons based on the same technology.\par \par \uc2 The crux of the situation is that, like the Tsarist regime and the former Soviet leaders, the current occupants of the Kremlin believe it is normal to "discipline" governments or opposition movements in the so-called satellite countries of the former USSR.\par \par \uc2 In the particular case of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Moscow's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was explained by the alleged fragility implied by the disappearance of the buffer zones, which is a unilateral entelechy conceived in equivalent terms by the respective strategists of the United States, Russia and, with a different view, the Chinese government.\par \par \uc2 Moscow considered it insulting that the current President, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2 , announced his desire to make his country a member of \uc2 NATO\uc2  and the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , processes that the West had been treating with tongs.\par \par \uc2 The prognosis for the ongoing responses is guarded. Although the economic sanctions of the main \uc2 OECD\uc2  governments will seriously hurt the Russian people and many of its trading partners, the relevant question is whether such a move will serve to twist the arm of a leader intoxicated with messianism.\par \par \uc2 Not for nothing did the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  go to the trouble of amassing some $640 billion in international reserves to mitigate the effects of the anticipated international retaliation to its absurd invasion. This indicates that Putin's government assumed that an extensive bank run could be fixed with patches or corralitos, which was a major mistake.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin did not calculate that half of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings could be frozen by the foreign banks that decided to participate in the retaliatory measures for the invasion.\par \par \uc2 Moscow's economic partners are not going to have an easy time either. The nations of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  are, at least for now, dangerously addicted to Russian gas and oil (see my last column).\par \par \uc2 In view of this new scenario, Brussels will have to reformulate the origin of the most sensitive supplies with alternative sources of energy, something that is already underway through the use of strategic reserves, a very ephemeral resource that can also undermine the fight against Climate Change outlined in the Green Pact.\par \par \uc2 Eight years ago \uc2 Henry Kissinger\uc2  caught the Ukrainian case on the fly, which is why he elaborated a project that was meant to negotiate, peacefully and preemptively, a rational status for that country's nascent democracy ("\uc2 Henry Kissinger\uc2 : To resolve Ukraine crisis, you need to start at the end," Washington Post of 5/3/2014).\par \par \uc2 His ideas encompassed the notion of preserving that nation's millennia-old ties with Russia; gradual economic-social integration into the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) (an issue on which Ukraine has just taken an unexpected first step in the midst of the invasion); and a modern link with the rest of the Western world. The package should be conceived as a bridge, not a tug of war, between the former "Cold War" blocs.\par \par \uc2 The approach also called for getting the Kremlin, Brussels and Washington to agree to Ukraine being governed harmoniously, and without external pressure, by its different ethnic, political and religious groups (Catholic and Orthodox), to ensure a peaceful link between East and West.\par \par \uc2 But the proposal went unheeded. Western governments are only now realizing the size of the challenge and the vulnerability of their policies.\par \par \uc2 Jorge Riaboi is a diplomat and journalist.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220313ei3d005tc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
