\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia acknowledges that it has \u8364\'20\'AC270 billion frozen due to sanctions, almost half of its reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The financial blockade to which the West is subjecting Russia for invading Ukraine is having a more than remarkable scope. Russian Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  acknowledged Sunday that the United States, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and the other countries that have taken a stand against Russia have managed to block about $300 billion of the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves with the sanctions, almost half of Russia's reserves. "This is about half of these reserves we had.\par \par \uc2  We have a total amount of reserves of about $640 billion and of them about $300 billion are now in a situation where we cannot use them," Siluanov assured, in an interview with Russian public television, as reported by Russian agencies.After the beginning of the invasion, Western countries rejected a direct military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  and opted to supply armaments to \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend against Russian aggression and impose harsh economic sanctions on Russia to strangle its finances and thus stifle its war effort. In what is the toughest package of punishments to date, the EU and the US have frozen the assets of the oligarchs on European soil; disconnected seven Russian and three Ukrainian entities from the Swift payment system and dealt a severe blow to Russia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which are essential to prop up the ruble. This latest setback has led to the free fall of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , higher interest rates and capital controls. In addition, the \uc2 EU\uc2  has also placed cryptocurrency transactions involving Russian citizens under surveillance to prevent them from using this resource to circumvent sations.In his statements, the minister has accused the West of putting pressure on China to limit Russia's access to its yuan reserves. Siluanov recalled that part of the Russian Federation's gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are denominated in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has prompted this pressure on Beijing. "We also see pressure exerted by Western countries on China to limit mutual trade with China. Of course, there is pressure to limit access to those reserves that we have in yuan," according to Siluanov. However, the Russian finance chief said he believes that his country's partnership with China "will still allow us to maintain the cooperation we have achieved and not only maintain it, but also increase it in the conditions when Western markets are closed," he stressed.The finance chief also assured that Russia will not refuse its debt obligations and will pay in rubles as long as Western countries continue to keep gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves frozen, and stressed that the country has enough resources to ensure the production of necessary goods.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220313ei3d005dr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
