\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 [Live]: Russia bombs Mykolaiv, Zelenskiy to "punish" attacks on civilians\b0\par\par\uc2 1,416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The mayor of Przemysl, a Polish city near the Ukrainian border, said the main challenge for local authorities is coordinating the transport of refugees to other urban centers, as thousands of Ukrainians fleeing the Russian invasion have flocked to his city.Photo: Darek DelmanowiczUkrainehas been fighting Russian forces on its territory for 11 days. On Sunday, Russian troops prepared to shell Odessa, a strategic city and Ukraine's main port, Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  warned. "It will be a military crime. It will be a historic crime," he declared, as the Russian army from annexed Crimea continued to advance into southern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the authorities in one of the cities most affected by the Russian attacks, Mariupol, reported that they would again try to evacuate people from the battle zone. However, the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  warned that the second attempt to evacuate the inhabitants was interrupted.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, Ukrainian authorities accused Russia of violating the agreed ceasefire to allow civilians to leave Mariupol. Some 450,000 inhabitants have been holding out for five days without heat, water and electricity in that port city, besieged by Russian forces\par \par \uc2 .????????\par \par \uc2 Follow here the minute by minute of what is happening today in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .???????????? Before we begin, a bit of context:\par \par \uc2 Saturday marked the tenth day since Russia invaded Ukrainian territory in the early hours of February 24 (night in America), under the argument of "demilitarizing" Ukraine.More than 1.5 million people have fled Ukraine since the start of the Russian invasion, according to the latest \uc2 UN\uc2  figures released Saturday.At least 364 civilians have been killed in Ukraine since Russian troops invaded on February 24, and another 759 were injured, according to \uc2 UN\uc2  data.Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski spoke by phone with U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to discuss financial support for Ukraine and sanctions against Russia. Hours earlier, the Ukrainian leader addressed by video call U.S. lawmakers who he asked for more assistance for his country and to cut off Russian oil imports. The U.S. lawmakers pledged another $10 billion in aid.The third round of Russian-Ukrainian negotiations to seek a cessation of hostilities in the Ukrainian war will take place next Monday the 7th, a member of the Ukrainian delegation said.Credit card companies \uc2 Visa\uc2  and \uc2 Mastercard\uc2  announced Saturday the suspension of their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Russia, the latest major U.S. firms to freeze their business activity with Moscow.8:15 a.m.: Russia adopts list of "hostile" countries to be repaid inrublesRussian authorities established a list of countries "hostile" to the country, which individuals and companies will be able to repay their debts in rubles, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that lost 45% of its value since January, the government said. This list of countries includes \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) countries, Australia, the United States, Canada, the United States, Switzerland and Japan.\par \par \uc2 According to AFP, the debtor will be able to ask a Russian bank to create a special ruble account in the name of the foreign creditor and send him a payment in Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the amount due, at the exchange rate of the day in question, as indicated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This measure will apply to payments exceeding 10 million rubles per month. This is one of the first Russian responses to sanctions imposed on Russia by numerous foreign countries, following its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 7:26 a.m.: Foreign ministers of Russia, Ukraine and Turkey tomeetTurkish Foreign Minister Mevlut Cavusoglu will meet Thursday with his Russian and Ukrainian counterparts, \uc2 Sergey Lavrov\uc2  and \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , respectively, at a trilateral meeting in Antalya\par \par \uc2 ."Following the initiative of our president and our intensive diplomatic efforts, the foreign ministers of Russia and Ukraine have decided to meet with my participation" in the framework of the Antalya Diplomatic Forum, Cavusoglu explained in a tweet. For her part, Russian diplomacy spokeswoman \uc2 Maria Zakharova\uc2  confirmed the meeting via Telegram.\par \par \uc2 6: 56 a.m.: Red Cross warns of dangers on Mariupol evacuation routeDominikStillhart, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  (\uc2 ICRC\uc2 ), told BBC Radio, about the humanitarian corridors, that "the problem or the challenge is to get both sides to come to an agreement that is concrete, workable and precise. We have been talking to them for days and days to get them to come to an agreement that is precise enough so that it can then be implemented," he said, noting that problems remain, for example, over routes.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the official said that the Red Cross team in Mariupol "was ready yesterday (Sunday), even though it was not entirely clear what the agreement was, and as soon as they arrived at the first checkpoint, they realized that the route they had been told to take for evacuation was mined."\par \par \uc2 6:00 a.m.: The mayor of a Ukrainian city died amid Russian attacksThemayor of Gostomel, a city northwest of the Ukrainian capital where a strategic airport is located, died, according to reports from the municipality. The entity assured through a statement issued on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  that "Yuri Illich Prylypko died while distributing bread and medicine to the sick".\par \par \uc2 In the town of Gostomel, northwest of Kiev, is located the Antonov military airport, which had been attacked by Russian forces on February 25, the day after the beginning of the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 5:52 a.m.: U.S. Secretary of State begins visit to Baltic countriesLatvia, Lithuania and Estonia are \uc2 NATO\uc2  members and, as such, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  will meet with officials to discuss security. "We are strengthening our shared defense so that we and our allies are prepared. We will defend every inch of \uc2 NATO\uc2  territory if it comes under attack."\par \par \uc2 Beginning his visit to the Baltic States with Lithuania, Blinken told the Lithuanian president that, "Unfortunately, the worsening security situation in the Baltic region is of great concern to all of us and around the world. Russia's reckless aggression against Ukraine proves once again that it is a long-term threat to European security, the security of our alliance."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lithuanian President \uc2 Gitanas Nauseda\uc2  asserted that a policy of deterrence was no longer sufficient and that "advanced defense" was needed. He further emphasized that, "if he is not stopped, Putin will not stop in Ukraine," AP reported.\par \par \uc2 5:32 a.m.: In Kiev there is discontent because humanitarian corridors only let go to Russia or BelarusAccording tomaps published by the RIA news agency, the corridors will only allow civilians to go to non-Ukrainian territories, with the Kiev corridor leading to Belarus, while civilians in Kharkiv will only be able to go to Russia. Russia will also set up an air bridge to take Ukrainians from Kiev to Russia, the country's Defense Ministry said.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  , told Reuters that the move was "completely immoral," adding that Russia was trying to "use people's suffering to create a TV image."\par \par \uc2 5:00 a .m: Russia agrees to trilateral meeting to protect nuclear facilitiesRussiabacks \uc2 UN\uc2  atomic watchdog chief \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2 's idea of a trilateral meeting with Ukraine to ensure the safety of facilities, excepting Chernobyl as Grossi wants, Moscow's envoy to the watchdog said\par \par \uc2 ."Russia supported Grossi's idea regarding a trilateral meeting and we hope that the Ukrainians will also cooperate," Russia's ambassador to the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2 , \uc2 Mikhail Ulyanov\uc2 , told reporters Monday. "I think Chernobyl is not the best place for such a meeting. There are numerous capitals in the world," Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 4:40 a.m.: Russia did not attend \uc2 International Court of Justice (ICJ) \uc2 hearing in The HagueAccording toAP, "Russia turned down a hearing at the top \uc2 U.N\uc2 . court on a legal attempt by Kiev to halt Moscow's devastating invasion of Ukraine. A row of seats reserved for Russian lawyers at the \uc2 International Court of Justice\uc2  was empty Monday morning when the hearing opened. The presiding judge of the court, U.S. Judge Joan E. Donoghue, said Russia's ambassador to the Netherlands informed the judges that his government did not intend to participate in the oral proceedings."\par \par \uc2 Thus, the hearing was held without the Russian delegation\par \par \uc2 .???????????? Have you already heard the latest news in the world? We invite you to check them out at El Espectador.\par \par \uc2 Receive alerts from GoogleNewsRelated topicsNewstheworldNewsthe world todayLatest news in the worldNews todayLatest newsUkraineRussia#Live UkraineVolodymyr ZelenskiyCoronavirus vaccineJoe BidenEuropean Union\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220307ei370060a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich4