\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 AFP general forecasts at 02H00 GMT\b0\par\par\uc2 2,293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 MAIN NEWS\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE RUSSIA CONFLICT: First talks between Ukraine and Russia as shelling continues\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  CLIMATE: New \uc2 UN\uc2  report presents 'atlas of human suffering' from climate change\par \par \uc2 -- UKRAINE RUSSIA CONFLICT\par \par \uc2 KHARKOV, Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 First talks between Ukraine and Russia as shelling continues.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Monday presented his conditions for ending the invasion of Ukraine, where his troops launched deadly shelling of several cities, including Kharkov (northeast), despite reinforced international pressure and sanctions.\par \par \uc2 By Sergey BOBOK, with Dave CLARK in Kiev\par \par \uc2 (Ukraine conflict Russia diplomacy \uc2 UN\uc2  diplomacy economy war peace, Central Note Update, 1,200 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO, INFOGRAPHICS\par \par \uc2 UNITED NATIONS:\par \par \uc2 Russia under heavy pressure at \uc2 UN\uc2  to cease invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In the international dock, Russia on Monday defended its invasion of Ukraine at an exceptional emergency meeting of the 193 members of the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2 , which has multiplied calls for an end to the war, described as "madness".\par \par \uc2 By Philippe RATER and Ana FERN\u193\'00\'C1NDEZ\par \par \uc2 (UN Russia Ukraine conflict diplomacy China, Focus Update, 750 words - 22H00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 GENEVA:\par \par \uc2 Russia under the spotlight at the \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ukraine won broad support Monday for holding an urgent debate at the \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  on Russia's invasion of its territory.\par \par \uc2 By Agn\u232\'00\'E8s PEDRERO and Christophe VOGT\par \par \uc2 (Russia conflict Ukraine \uc2 UN\uc2  rights, Focus Update, 550 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 VIDEO, PHOTOS\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON:\par \par \uc2 US downplays Russian nuclear 'threat'.\par \par \uc2 The United States on Monday downplayed the risk of a nuclear confrontation with Russia, saying it has not noted any "concrete" moves a day after Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered Moscow's deterrent forces to be put on alert.\par \par \uc2 (USA Russia Ukraine nuclear conflict, Focus, 700 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS:\par \par \uc2 EU ajar door to Ukraine, but not immediately\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) has opened a door of access to Ukraine, but warned that the process will not happen immediately, as demanded by the Ukrainian president, Volodimir Zelenski, who wants the country to be accepted "without delay".\par \par \uc2 (EU Ukraine conflict Russia diplomacy, Focus, Update, 600 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 Fashion Week kicks off in Paris with "seriousness" in wartime.\par \par \uc2 Fashion Week kicked off Monday in Paris with a massive return to the catwalks after two years of pandemic, but with an atmosphere of "seriousness" because of the war launched by Russia over Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 By Olga NEDBAEVA\par \par \uc2 (Ukraine Russia Russia France Paris conflict fashion luxury, Central Note, 500 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS\par \par \uc2 DOMODEDOVO, Russia:\par \par \uc2 The complicated journey of several passengers blocked at a Moscow airport.\par \par \uc2 Many passengers encountered a multitude of difficulties at Moscow airport, among stranded European tourists, foreign students and Russians who wanted to leave the country for work or pleasure, in the midst of the crisis around Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 By Ekaterina ANISIMOVA\par \par \uc2 (Ukraine Russia conflict diplomacy aviation, Report, 550 words - Already broadcast)\par \par \uc2 VIDEO\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 Excluded from the World Cup, sponsors ruled out: Russia suffers from sports sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The Russian invasion in Ukraine continues to cause harsh consequences on professional sport, starting with Russia's exclusion from the World Cup-2022 soccer tournament, adding to the IOC's recommendation to exclude Russian athletes from competitions, less than a week before the start of the Beijing Paralympics.\par \par \uc2 (Ukraine Russia conflict sport fbl RUS, Sidebar, 800 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 MEDYKA, Poland:\par \par \uc2 From one war to another, Afghan refugee in Ukraine flees to Poland in the face of Russian advance.\par \par \uc2 Ajmal Rahmani left Afghanistan a year ago thinking he would find peace in Ukraine, but now he is fleeing back to Poland, along with thousands of refugees, because of the Russian advance.\par \par \uc2 By Bernard OSSER\par \par \uc2 (Poland Afghanistan Ukraine conflict Russia migration refugees, Report, 550 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS\par \par \uc2 GENEVA:\par \par \uc2 More than 500,000 Ukrainian refugees in border countries.\par \par \uc2 More than 500,000 people fled Ukraine to bordering countries since the military offensive by Russia began on Thursday, according to the latest \uc2 UN\uc2  assessment, reported on Monday.\par \par \uc2 (Ukraine refugee conflict armed-forces Russia, Sidebar, 350 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 ROSTOV DEL DON, Russia:\par \par \uc2 Young Russians "without a future" in Rostov-on-Don fearfully protest against war.\par \par \uc2 In a central square in Rostov-on-Don a clandestine demonstration of young people protest against the invasion of Ukraine, without getting too close to each other, looking at each other sideways and frightened by police controls.\par \par \uc2 By Andrea PALASCIANO\par \par \uc2 (Russia Ukraine war youth political demonstrations, Report, 650 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 LEOPOLIS, Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 From beer to Molotov cocktails, a Ukrainian brewery's fight against Putin.\par \par \uc2 In an industrial zone of Lviv, the main city in western Ukraine, workers at a brewery stopped brewing beverages and now produce Molotov cocktails for use against the Russian army.\par \par \uc2 By Ionut IORDACHESCU\par \par \uc2 (conflict Ukraine war Russia, Videostory, 250 words - Already broadcast)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO.\par \par \uc2 DAMASCUS:\par \par \uc2 Syria, another flank of Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Russia, which invaded \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  on February 24, has maintained since 2015 a significant military presence in Syria supporting the forces of Bashar al-Assad's regime, and has been able to test armaments and tactics there.\par \par \uc2 (Syria Russia diplomacy economy economy forces-armed forces education society, Sidebar, 500 words - Already transmitted)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS\par \par \uc2 BERLIN:\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , the conversion of the "automaton" into war chancellor.\par \par \uc2 German Chancellor \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , criticized for his lack of charisma and nicknamed "the automaton" for his monotone, has become a staunch war chancellor since the beginning of the Russian invasion of Ukraine, a conflict that broke many German taboos.\par \par \uc2 By Mathieu FOULKES\par \par \uc2 (Germany Ukraine conflict Russia conflict government economy defense, Focus, 550 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 ARCHIVE PHOTOS, ARCHIVE VIDEO\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 Western countries punish Russian oligarchs for war.\par \par \uc2 The decision by Western countries to extend their sanctions against Russia to oligarchs and their assets around the world represents a significant breakthrough in making Moscow pay for its invasion of Ukraine, international anti-corruption advocates said.\par \par \uc2 By Tom BARFIELD\par \par \uc2 (EU U.S. diplomacy conflict Ukraine Russia sanction, Focus, 550 words - Already Transmitted)\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES:\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of Latin Americans evacuated from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Several hundred citizens of Latin American countries were evacuated from Ukraine since the armed conflict with Russia began, others are waiting for assistance and some moved out of the war scene on their own, their governments reported.\par \par \uc2 (Latam Ukraine Refugees Russia Latin America Argentina Peru Chile Uruguay, Summary Update, 650 words - 02H30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON:\par \par \uc2 US banned all transactions with \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The United States on Monday banned all transactions with \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Treasury Department announced, a sanction of immediate effect and unprecedented severity taken in coordination with several Washington allies, in response to the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (conflict USA Russia Ukraine sanctions markets finance banks, Note, 500 words - Already Transmitted)\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK:\par \par \uc2 Tech giants target media close to power in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  blocks them, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  makes them less visible, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  removes them from its app store; tech giants on Monday took a new step to limit the influence of media close to Russian power, accused of misinforming since the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (USA Russia Ukraine internet techology telecommunications, Focus, 700 words - 03H00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 By Thomas URBAIN\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW:\par \par \uc2 Putin announces drastic measures to support the ruble in the face of sanctions\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Monday lashed out at the brutal sanctions imposed by the Western "empire of lies" in response to the invasion of Ukraine and announced drastic measures to stem the ruble's slide.\par \par \uc2 By Antoine LAMBROSCHINI\par \par \uc2 (\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  economy conflict sanction Ukraine Russia, Focus, 500 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW:\par \par \uc2 Russians worried about their savings as ruble falls sharply\par \par \uc2 Noting the fall of the ruble, Natalia Proshina rushed to the bank: like her, many other Russians fear the evaporation of their savings following Western sanctions imposed for invading Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 By Marina LAPENKOVA\par \par \uc2 (Russia Ukraine political conflict banking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Report, 600 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 VIDEO\par \par \uc2 KIEV:\par \par \uc2 With Molotov and Kalashnikov, from the trenches Kiev prepares to "receive" the Russians.\par \par \uc2 On the tracksides in Kiev, billboards calmly parade under a blazing sun the same phrases in Russian: "Russian soldiers, go fuck yourselves!". "Don't become murderers." "Go back!".\par \par \uc2 By Daphne ROUSSEAU\par \par \uc2 (conflict unrest Ukraine Russia, Report, 600 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO.\par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS:\par \par \uc2 Russia's invasion of Ukraine consolidates European defense.\par \par \uc2 The decision by \uc2 European Union\uc2  states to jointly spend \u8364\'20\'AC500 million on arms purchases for Ukraine, at war with Russia, is a "turning point" for European defense, according to politicians and analysts.\par \par \uc2 By Christian SPILLMANN\par \par \uc2 (EU arms diplomacy conflict defense Ukraine Russia, Analysis, 500 words - Already Transmitted)\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 Leave Russia or stay? Foreign companies have no choice\par \par \uc2 The departure of the British oil giant BP from Russia is an exception among the foreign groups present in the country, which can hardly repatriate factories or supermarkets overnight.\par \par \uc2 By Katia DOLMADJIAN\par \par \uc2 (diplomacy economy conflict companies investment energy sanction Ukraine Russia, Focus, Update, 500 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 New sanctions against Russia sink world stock markets.\par \par \uc2 Major world stock markets fell again on Monday, following new sanctions imposed on Russia for its attack on Ukraine, amid fears that they will spike energy prices and reinforce ongoing inflation.\par \par \uc2 (Ukraine conflict Russia stock exchanges debt \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stock market, Summary, Update, 650 words - Already Transmitted)\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 What are the consequences of economic sanctions against Russia?\par \par \uc2 A ruble at historic lows, the closure of the Moscow stock exchange, a drastic rise in interest rates.... These are some of the consequences this Monday of the sanctions imposed on the Russian economy and finances.\par \par \uc2 By Ali BEKHTAOUI\par \par \uc2 (growth economy conflict defense sanction EU banks Ukraine Russia USA, Questions-Answers, 650 words - Already transmitted)\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 What is the impact on aircraft traffic of airspace closures?\par \par \uc2 The reciprocal closure of their airspaces by the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) and Russia has only a limited impact on Russian transport in the sector, as European airlines will be forced to make long and costly detours to reach Asia.\par \par \uc2 By Mathieu RABECHAULT\par \par \uc2 (EU Russia Ukraine aviation tourism conflict sanctions, Sidebar, 700 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 -- UN CLIMATE\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 New \uc2 UN\uc2  report presents an "atlas of human suffering" due to climate change.\par \par \uc2 Half of the world's population is already "highly vulnerable" to the cruel and growing impacts of climate change, and "criminal" inaction by leaders threatens to reduce the planet's slim chances of a "livable future," the United Nations warned Monday.\par \par \uc2 By Am\u233\'00\'E9lie BOTTOLLIER-DEPOIS\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 UN\uc2  climate environment economy, Central Note Update, 850 words - Already transmitted)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO, INFOGRAPHICS\par \par \uc2 PARIS:\par \par \uc2 Getting worse and worse: the harsh conclusions of the \uc2 UN\uc2  climate report.\par \par \uc2 The report released Monday by \uc2 UN\uc2  climate experts paints a picture of the harsh consequences of global warming, for which humanity is not sufficiently prepared.\par \par \uc2 By Marlowe HOOD and Am\u233\'00\'E9lie BOTTOLLIER-DEPOIS\par \par \uc2 (UN IPCC climate environment economy impact, Sidebar, 800 words - Already transmitted)\par \par \uc2 OTHER NEWS BY REGION\par \par \uc2 -- AMERICAS\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON:\par \par \uc2 Biden to try to boost U.S. morale with first State of the Union address\par \par \uc2 An unpopular \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , weighed down by several policy failures, will try to boost American morale Tuesday with his first State of the Union address, with the world watching Russia's invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 By Aurelia END\par \par \uc2 (government diplomacy Ukraine Russia economy Congress, Presentation Update, 650 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON:\par \par \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  considers climate case amid \uc2 UN\uc2  warnings.\par \par \uc2 The highly conservative \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  on Monday examined an environmental dossier that could complicate the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  administration's fight against global warming, essential for a "livable future," according to a \uc2 U.N\uc2 . report.\par \par \uc2 By Charlotte PLANTIVE\par \par \uc2 (USA, climate, environment, justice, energy, Central-Note, 700 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 FILE PHOTO\par \par \uc2 -- EUROPE\par \par \uc2 A\u209\'00\'D1OVER DE TORMES, Spain:\par \par \uc2 An elderly Spaniard's revolt against bank digitalization.\par \par \uc2 Spanish retiree Carlos San Juan got fed up with his bank begrudging him personal attention and making him feel foolish for his problems with tellers, apps and a digital revolution that sows panic among many seniors.\par \par \uc2 By Alfons LUNA\par \par \uc2 (Spain internet banks elderly people, Report, 900 words - Already broadcasted)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 -- ASIA\par \par \uc2 HERAT, Afghanistan:\par \par \uc2 Afghans sell kidneys to feed their families.\par \par \uc2 Unemployed and burdened by debt, Nooruddin was left with no choice: to feed his famine-threatened family, he sold one of his kidneys like many other Afghans.\par \par \uc2 By Rouba EL HUSSEINI\par \par \uc2 (Afghanistan poverty economy health, Feature, 750 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO.\par \par \uc2 -- AFRICA:\par \par \uc2 GBARPOLU, Liberia:\par \par \uc2 Pangolin nears extinction in Liberia for its meat and coveted scales.\par \par \uc2 Emmanuel takes advantage of the dark night during the dry season in Liberia to go hunting armed with a rifle and machete. That's the time when the shy pangolin goes out looking for ants or termites in the forest.\par \par \uc2 By Emmet LIVINGSTONE\par \par \uc2 (Liberia animals environment medicine tradition hunting crime food, Special Report, 1,200 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 -- ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 BARCELONA, Spain:\par \par \uc2 Mobile World Congress kicks off in Barcelona with explicit support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 From 'tech' to geopolitics: the Mobile World Congress (MWC), a key event for the new technologies sector, kicked off Monday in Barcelona with the organizers condemning the war in Ukraine, symbolically removing the Russian pavilion from the event.\par \par \uc2 By Valentin BONTEMPS and Yassine KHIRI\par \par \uc2 (Spain Ukraine conflict Russia mobile pandemic mobile pandemic computer epidemic virus telecommunications armed-forces, Central Note, 700 words - Already transmitted)\par \par \uc2 PHOTOS, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 -- SOCIETY\par \par \uc2 LOS ANGELES:\par \par \uc2 "CODA," drama about a deaf family, takes top \uc2 SAG\uc2  award.\par \par \uc2 The independent film "CODA," which tells the story of a struggling deaf family, won the \uc2 SAG\uc2  Award for Best Picture on Sunday from the U.S. Screen Actors Guild, a preview of what could happen at the Oscars.\par \par \uc2 By Andrew MARSZAL\par \par \uc2 (USA film award people television, Central Note, 500 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 LOS ANGELES:\par \par \uc2 SAG\uc2  Awards Winners.\par \par \uc2 These are the winners in the major categories at the 28th annual Screen Actors Guild (\uc2 SAG\uc2 ) Awards, held Sunday in Santa Monica, west of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 (USA film award people television, Sidebar, 200 words - Already aired)\par \par \uc2 zm/mar/yow/jvb/rsr\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220301ei31002ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
