\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: Moscow shells Kharkov and advances towards Kiev with a 64-kilometer line of armored vehicles\b0\par\par\uc2 17,298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 EN VIVONoticia enDesarrolloRussian army shells on Tuesday the center of Kharkov, Ukraine's second city near the border with Russia, as it advances towards Kiev with a 64-kilometer line of armored vehicles.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:55\par \par \uc2 Russia says \uc2 NATO\uc2  takes dangerous steps by bolstering military capabilitiesRussiatoday insisted that the existence of U.S. nuclear weapons in Europe is inadmissible and again demanded security guarantees from \uc2 NATO\uc2 , in a video message from Foreign Minister \uc2 Sergey Lavrov\uc2  on the Russian offensive in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 ."For us it is unacceptable that, contrary to the fundamental provisions of the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty, U.S. nuclear weapons are still located on the territory of several European countries," he said.\par \par \uc2 "It is high time for US nuclear weapons to be brought home and the associated infrastructure in Europe to be completely dismantled," Lavrov said at the UN Conference on Disarmament, which is meeting in Geneva and which he was unable to attend in person because his plane cannot fly over several European countries due to sanctions.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:48\par \par \uc2 European Union\uc2  says Kharkov shelling ?violates laws of war?The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) High Representative for Foreign Affairs \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2  said on Tuesday that Russia's shelling of civilian infrastructure in the Ukrainian city of Kharkov on Monday "violates the laws of war".\par \par \uc2 The Spanish politician expressed himself in this sense after speaking with the Ukrainian Foreign Minister, Dmitro Kuleba. "I spoke with Dmitro Kuleba. The shelling of civilian infrastructure yesterday in Kharkov violates the laws of war. The \uc2 EU\uc2  stands firmly by Ukraine in these dramatic moments," Borrell wrote on his profile on the social network \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:34\par \par \uc2 Mass boycott of Russian Foreign Minister's speech at Conference on Disarmament in GenevaManydelegations, including Ukraine and Western countries, boycotted Russian Foreign Minister \uc2 Sergey Lavrov\uc2 's speech on Tuesday as his address to the Conference on Disarmament was being broadcast, leaving the hall almost empty.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:41\par \par \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2 , Russian Foreign Minister. Photo Russian Foreign Ministry Press Service via AP.\par \par \uc2 Diplomats left the hall at the beginning of Lavrov's speech, a recording relayed, an AFP journalist noted.\par \par \uc2 The Russian minister was due to travel to Geneva but cancelled his visit on Monday citing "anti-Russian sanctions" that prohibit him from flying over the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . A few delegations remained in the room, including those of Venezuela, Yemen, Algeria, Syria and Tunisia. Outside the hall, the boycott was met with loud applause.\par \par \uc2 "It is important to show a gesture of solidarity with our Ukrainian friends," declared Yann Hwang, French ambassador to the Conference on Disarmament, the international community's single multilateral body for negotiations in that sector.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:17\par \par \uc2 Russia will continue its offensive in Ukraine until its "objectives" aremetRussian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  (c) with his Defense Minister \uc2 Sergey Shoigu\uc2  (d) and Foreign Minister \uc2 Sergey Lavrov\uc2  during a meeting in the Kremlin. Photo EFE.\par \par \uc2 Russia will continue its offensive in Ukraine until it achieves its objectives, announced Defense Minister \uc2 Sergey Shoigu\uc2 , almost a week into the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 "The Russian armed forces will continue the special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the set objectives are met," Shoigu said in a press conference broadcast on state television. ?Russia seeks the "demilitarization" and "denazification" of Ukraine, as well as to protect Russia from the "military threat created by Western countries," the minister said.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 07:05\par \par \uc2 UNHCR\uc2  raises refugees from Russian invasion of Ukraine to 660,000 People walk near the Polish-Ukrainian border crossing in Dorohusk, Poland. EFE photo.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations Refugee Agency (UNHCR) \uc2 United Nations Refugee Agency\uc2  (UNHCR) raised to 660,000 the number of people who have left Ukraine\par \par \uc2 for neighboring countries in the first five days of war.Refugees are suffering long waiting times to enter some countries, up to 60 hours according to \uc2 UNHCR\uc2  spokeswoman Shabia Mantoo at a press conference, and their exodus is also complicated by low temperatures and transportation problems that force them to walk long distances.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 05:54\par \par \uc2 YouTube\uc2  blocked two Russian channelsYouTubeblocked Russian media channels RT and Sputnik across Europe "in the wake of the ongoing war in Ukraine," the platform announced Tuesday in a mail sent to the AFP news agency\par \par \uc2 ."We blocked RT and Sputnik's \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channels across Europe, effective immediately. Our systems need some time to become fully \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Our teams are monitoring the situation around the clock to act as quickly as possible," they indicated from \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 05:35\par \par \uc2 France assured that sanctions will provoke the "collapse" of Russia'seconomyFrench Finance Minister \uc2 Bruno Le Maire\uc2  said Tuesday that sanctions against Russia for the invasion of Ukraine will provoke the collapse of its economy\par \par \uc2 ."We are going to provoke the collapse of the Russian economy. The balance of economic and financial forces is entirely in favor of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  which is discovering its economic power," \uc2 Le Maire\uc2  said in statements to France Info radio.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 05:15\par \par \uc2 Ukraine to sell war bonds to finance armyTheUkrainian government confirmed it will put on sale from Tuesday war bonds to be able to finance the armed forces fighting against the Russian army. The value of each bond is 1,000 grivnas ($33) and the interest rate was not yet determined. This was reported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Ukraine\uc2  through its official \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account: "The proceeds from the bonds will be used to meet the needs of the Armed Forces of Ukraine."\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:42\par \par \uc2 Russian missile hit Kharkov Regional State AdministrationAshocking video showing the exact moment when a Russian missile hit the front of the Regional State Administration building in Kharkov began to circulate on social networks. The aftermath of the explosion shows burnt cars and debris on the city square\par \par \uc2 . So farno fatalities or injuries were reported from the attack.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:41\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 04:13\par \par \uc2 Russian attack on Kherson city startedTheRussian military has already started its attack on the city of Kherson in southern Ukraine, the State Service for Communications and Information Protection reported on its official Telegram account\par \par \uc2 ."The assault on Kherson has begun. According to witnesses, the enemy is advancing from the airport to the Nikolaev highway and the ring near the refrigeration plant," they specified."\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 03:44\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \uc2 UN\uc2  Ambassador welcomed the end of his Russian peer's chairmanship of the Security CouncilTheUkrainian ambassador to the United Nations Sergiy Kyslytsya welcomed the end of the monthly term of his Russian peer \uc2 Vassily Nebenzia\uc2  as president of the \uc2 UN Security Council\par \par \uc2 ."I look forward to midnight, when this abomination, the occupation of the council president's seat, will end," Kyslytsya wrote on his official \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account on Monday\par \par \uc2 .01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 03:10\par \par \uc2 Russian army threatens Kherson cityRussia's army is at the gates of the southern Ukrainian city of Kherson near the Crimean peninsula, its mayor Igor Kolikhayev said in the early hours of Tuesday\par \par \uc2 ."The Russian military is setting up checkpoints at the entrances to Kherson. It is difficult to say how the situation will develop. Kherson is and will remain Ukrainian.Kherson resists!" the mayor closed\par \par \uc2 .01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 02:55\par \par \uc2 Mastercard\uc2  blocked transactions from RussiaMastercardreported that it has blocked multiple transactions from its payment system as a result of sanctions imposed on Russia over the invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .The news comes as the United States, along with the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the United Kingdom and Canada, said they would take action against Russia by shutting Russian banks out of the Swift international payments system and preventing \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from deploying its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to cushion the impact of the sanctions.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 02:25\par \par \uc2 70 Ukrainian soldiers killed in Russian attack?01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 03:23\par \par \uc2 "Many people have died. Currently, places are being prepared at the cemetery for about 70 dead Ukrainian soldiers," reported Dmytro Zhyvytskyi, head of the state administration of the Sumy region.\par \par \uc2 According to Zhyvytskyi, it was a Russian artillery attack that destroyed a Ukrainian militia unit in the northeastern town of Okhtyrka.\par \par \uc2 "But the enemy also gets what he deserves," he added, saying there were "many Russian bodies" in the town, which are now being handed over to the Red Cross.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 01:55\par \par \uc2 Chinese embassy in Ukraine began evacuationsThe Chinese embassy in Ukraine reported that the first organized group of citizens left the country on Wednesday. According to local media, they were Chinese students from Kiev who were on their way to Moldova.\par \par \uc2 The fact that China is only evacuating its citizens now could mean several things.One possibility is that Beijing initially felt it was important not to upset Russia prematurely. Another, that China thought Russia would take Ukraine so quickly that it wouldn't need people to leave.\par \par \uc2 And another, more worrisome possibility is that China has calculated that Russia's invasion is about to get worse.\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 01:25\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President told that he has not yet reached an agreement with Russia to stop theinvasionUkrainian President Volodymir Zelensky said Ukraine has received "some signals"\par \par \uc2 from Russia during negotiations between representatives of the two countries on Monday, but it is still not the outcome he would like to have."So far, we do not have the result we would like to have\par \par \uc2 . Russia has expressed its points, we have expressed ours to end the war. We received some signals. When the delegation returns to Kiev, we will analyze what we have heard and then we will decide how to move to the second round," the head of state said. He continued, "I think Russia wants to put pressure with such an uncunning method, but let it not waste time, such a tactic does not work with us."\par \par \uc2 01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 00:55\par \par \uc2 Japan announced sanctions against Vladimir PutinThegovernment of Japan reported Tuesday that it resolved to impose a set of sanctions on Russian individuals and organizations, including President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , in response to Russia's invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .The penalties involve freezing assets that Putin\par \par \uc2 and a group of Russian officials may have in the country, the \uc2 Japanese Foreign Ministry\uc2  said in a statement.The measures cover Russian Foreign Minister Serguei Lavrov, Defense Minister Serguei Shoigu, Deputy Chairman of the Security Council Dmitri Medvedev and Chief of the General Staff of the Armed Forces General Valeri Gerasimov, among others.\par \par \uc2 They also cover 49 companies and organizations\par \par \uc2 , including the \uc2 Federal Security Service\uc2 , the General Staff of the Armed Forces, the industrial group of aerospace engineering companies Sukhoi and the state corporation Ristec, according to Sputnik news agency.01.03.2022\par \par \uc2 00:04\par \par \uc2 China, with distance from Russia: 'Cold War mentality must be abandoned'China's message at Monday's emergency \uc2 UN\uc2  meeting marked some distance from \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's regime. The Asian giant appealed for reflection by arguing that "there is nothing to be gained" in this war.\par \par \uc2 "The Cold War mentality based on bloc confrontation must be abandoned. There is nothing to be gained by fomenting a new cold war, but everyone will have to lose," said Chinese Ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  Zhang Jun. The Chinese representative added that "the security of one country should not be at the expense of the security of other countries. Least of all can regional security be guaranteed by strengthening or even expanding military blocs. ?He added: "China supports the EU, \uc2 NATO\uc2  and Russia resuming dialogue, properly addressing the legitimate security concerns of all parties, including Russia, and working to forge a balanced, effective and sustainable European security mechanism to achieve lasting peace and stability for the European continent."\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:27\par \par \uc2 Russia alleged to have used thermobaricbombsUkrainian Ambassador to Washington \uc2 Oksana Markarova\uc2  revealed that Russia has dropped thermobaric bombs in Ukraine, demonstrating the "devastation" sought by Moscow\par \par \uc2 .After holding meetings in the \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  with senators of both parties to explain the situation in her country in the midst of the Russian invasion, Markarova denounced the use of this weaponry, also known as vacuum bombs, which cause high temperature explosions.\par \par \uc2 The diplomat remarked that this type of weapons "are forbidden by the Geneva Convention" and therefore their use underlines that the "devastation" sought by Russia in Ukraine is "great". In statements picked up by the US Fox network, Markorava called, therefore, for more weapons and military assistance.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:15\par \par \uc2 A huge Russian armored convoy advances towards KievARussian convoy, 64 kilometers long, advances towards Ukraine's capital. Photo EFE/\uc2 EPA\uc2 /\uc2 Maxar\par \par \uc2 TechnologiesSatellite\par \par \uc2 photos\par \par \uc2 show a giant convoy of Russian forces north of Ukraine's capital stretching 64 kilometers. The huge convoy of armored vehicles, tanks, artillery and support vehicles was 25 kilometers from the center of Kiev, according to satellite images from \uc2 Maxar Technologies\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This Monday night Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski claimed that the invading troops intensified artillery fire on his country, calling it an attempt to force his government to make concessions in talks begun hours earlier to try to agree on a cease-fire.\par \par \uc2 Zelenski reiterated that Kiev remains a "key target'' for Russia and that Kremlin soldiers also attacked with artillery and missiles on Kharkov, the country's second largest city, where local authorities reported nine dead and 37 wounded during the day.\par \par \uc2 "It is a peaceful city, with no military installations, against which they fired brutally with shells. It is an obvious war crime," the president charged. He added: "Four people who left the shelter to get water were killed, and a family of two adults and three children was burned alive inside a car."\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:06\par \par \uc2 Stephen King\uc2  expressed his support for UkraineTherenowned American writer \uc2 Stephen King\uc2  broke his own precepts related to virtuality and posted on his social networks a photo of himself, wearing a T-shirt expressing his support for Ukraine, in the face of the Russian military invasion\par \par \uc2 ."I don't usually post pictures of myself, but today is an exception," said the author, who wore a T-shirt with the caption "I stand with Ukraine".\par \par \uc2 Stephen King\uc2 's tweet was answered by the official Ukrainian account in that network and it was in the form of a promise: "We will prevail for you, sir".\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:50\par \par \uc2 Shocking images: 64 kilometers of Russian armored vehicles towards KievTheendless caravan of Russian troops, south of Ivankiv, Ukraine. Photo EFE/\uc2 EPA\uc2 /\uc2 Maxar\par \par \uc2 TechnologiesSatellite\par \par \uc2 photos\par \par \uc2 show a convoy of Russian forces north of Ukraine's capital stretching for 64 kilometers\par \par \uc2 .The long convoy of armored vehicles, tanks, artillery and support vehicles was 25 kilometers from the center of Kiev, according to satellite images from \uc2 Maxar Technologies\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Maxar\uc2 's photos also showed the deployment of ground forces and attack helicopter units in southern Belarus.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:39\par \par \uc2 Russia and Belarus suspended by \uc2 World Rugby\uc2  "until further notice"As indicated by the sport's world federation, it also announced "full and immediate" sanctions following the invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .Russia's membership in the \uc2 World Rugby\uc2  federation was also suspended indefinitely, ending the few chances its national team had of qualifying for next year's World Cup in France.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:25\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  suspends \uc2 Pixar\uc2  releases in RussiaRed, new \uc2 Pixar\uc2  film DisneyThe\par \par \uc2 entertainment company announced that it suspended the release of its films in Russian theaters following "the unprovoked invasion of Ukraine and the tragic humanitarian crisis."\par \par \uc2 Among the suspended films is \uc2 Pixar\uc2 's "Turning Red".\par \par \uc2 The U.S. giant thus follows the example of other companies that chose to disassociate themselves, temporarily, from the invading country.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:33\par \par \uc2 Dilemmas over Russia's role in the spaceraceNASA on Monday highlighted the collaboration between Russia and the United States for the proper functioning of the International Space Station and\par \par \uc2 stated that it is not affected by the tension between the two countries due to the invasion in Ukraine.On the other hand, the \uc2 European Space Agency\uc2  considered that it is unlikely that the launch of the ExoMars \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , scheduled for this year, which aims to study Mars in depth and install a Russian platform on the planet, will take place.28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:22\par \par \uc2 Pablo Vaca\par \par \uc2 Clar\u237\'00\'EDn on the Polish-Ukrainian borderClar\u237\'00\'EDn's special correspondent, Pablo Vaca, reports in his chronicle the exodus of Ukrainian women and their children, while the men stay behind to fight.Read the chronicle of the trip to the war here.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:57\par \par \uc2 Local media report 11 dead in Kharkov after attacksThe Ukrainian city of Kharkov was attacked on Monday by Russian troops.\par \par \uc2 At least 11 people were killed Monday in Kharkov, Ukraine's second largest city, after Russian forces attacked residential buildings with rocket launchers, according to the country's media.\par \par \uc2 They also noted that earlier a woman was killed, while 15 soldiers and 16 civilians were hospitalized due to gunfire in the area.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:40\par \par \uc2 Ukraine releases prisoners with military experience to fight RussiaUkrainian President Volodymir Zelensky announced that he will release prisoners with military experience to give battle to Russian forces, although he admitted that it was not an easy decision "from a moral point of view." "Anyone who can join the fight against the occupiers should do so. The decision was not easy, from a moral point of view, but useful from the point of view of our protection," the president said.?and explained: "Under martial law, the participants in hostilities, Ukrainians with real combat experience, will be released from prison and will be able to atone for their guilt in the most dangerous places of the war. The key now is defense.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:14\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Criminal Court\uc2  announced that it will investigate war crimes in UkraineThe prosecutor of the \uc2 International Criminal Court (ICC) \uc2 Karim Khan reported that he will launch "as soon as possible" an investigation into war crimes and crimes against humanity in Ukraine in the context of war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 "I am convinced that there is a reasonable basis to believe that alleged war crimes and crimes against humanity were committed in Ukraine since 2014," Khan said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:08\par \par \uc2 More limits on Russian media: \uc2 Facebook\uc2  will restrict those controlled by the Kremlin in the EUThe technology company Meta confirmed Monday that it will restrict on its social networks, which include \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and WhatsApp, access to the RT network and the Sputnik agency, media affiliated with the Russian government, at the request of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:59\par \par \uc2 Ukraine denounces "war crime" for the shelling of "a peaceful city".Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  gave a speech on Monday via his social networks.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelensky said so in a harsh speech he posted tonight on his social networks, following the attack on Kharkov.\par \par \uc2 "It is a peaceful city, with peaceful residential areas, without military structures. Dozens of eyewitnesses confirm that this was not errant shooting, but deliberate destruction of people: the Russians knew where they were shooting," the president said."He continued, "No one in the world will forgive them for murdering peaceful Ukrainian citizens," he said sharply and called on the international community to ban Russian ships and aircraft from accessing "all ports and airports in the world.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:44\par \par \uc2 New satellite images show the advance of Russian troops towards KievA new satellite image shows the advance of Russian troops on Monday (Photo: \uc2 Maxar Technologies\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Russian rocket attacks have already killed "dozens" of civilians in Ukraine's second largest city and, as reported by \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  newspaper, have already begun new assaults on Kiev where during the afternoon anti-aircraft sirens began to sound and several detonations were alerted.\par \par \uc2 The advance of the troops was captured by new images released on Monday in which the long Russian columns can be seen only 27 kilometers from the Ukrainian capital.\par \par \uc2 They said the widespread use of weapons such as multiple rocket launche