el Seifert\par \par \uc2 Belarus' return to a nuclear state alarmingWith the report that Belarus approved a "constitutional" change by referendum to renounce the country's "non-nuclear" status , the atomic escalation of the war in Ukraine adds another step following Putin's challenge this Sunday. Belarus, former Soviet republic and mirror for the Russian president of what he intends Ukraine to be , is ruled with a lead foot, acts as a Russian satellite and is one of the platform from where it invades towards Kiev.\par \par \uc2 In theory, the Belarusian measure could allow Russia to place nuclear weapons on its soil for the first time since the country abandoned them after the fall of the USSR or to outsource the claim, with a local demand for the return of the atomic bombs of that time.\par \par \uc2 The result of the referendum would take effect ten days after its official publication, the Russian news agency RIA Novosti reported. The border between Ukraine and Belarus will host the diplomatic contact between Moscow and Kiev on Monday.?its role in the war takes another dimension.\par \par \uc2 28.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:27\par \par \uc2 Australia confirmed sanctions against Russia and PutinAs the Minister for Foreign Affairs Marise Payne announced, the Australian government officially announced the approval of a new package of sanctions against Russia, including a ban on President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , as well as members of the \uc2 Russian Security Council\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Australia's financial sanctions and entry restrictions came into force for the Russian president and other members of the Security Council," Prime Minister Scott Morrison said early Monday.\par \par \uc2 The sanctioned officials, in addition to Putin, are Russian Prime Minister \uc2 Mikhail Mishustin\uc2 , Foreign Minister \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2 , Interior Minister Vladimir Kolokolstev and Defense Minister \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:55\par \par \uc2 Kiev reports successful drone strike in MalynThe Ukrainian military claimed that a drone attack was successful against Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 It was reported by CNN, citing Russian armed forces, according to which the Turkish-produced Bayraktar TB2 drone strike took place near the town of Malyn, 100 kilometers northwest of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:17\par \par \uc2 Ukraine: alert for shortage of medical oxygenThe supply of medical oxygen in Ukrainian hospitals is "dangerously low" due to the crisis and the reserves are barely sufficient for the next 24 hours. This is a critical situation, at a time when the number of wounded is growing due to the war emergency.\par \par \uc2 This was warned by the Director General of the \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO)\uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  (WHO), \uc2 Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus\uc2 , and the Regional Director for Europe, Hans Henri P. Kluge "It is crucial to ensure that life-saving medical supplies, including oxygen, reach those who need them," explains the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WHO\uc2  assumes an increase of 20% to 25% over the needs prior to the escalation of the crisis. Supplies would need safe transit, including through a logistics corridor through Poland.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:59\par \par \uc2 Pablo Vaca\par \par \uc2 200,000 Ukrainians crossed the border: between the pain of a refugee wave and the strength of solidarityA Ukrainian woman cries as she crosses the border into Poland. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 In Warsaw, war is just around the corner. The conflict between Russia and Ukraine has completely altered local political life, like that of half the planet, but also the daily life of Poles.\par \par \uc2 They have no way of escaping it when in just four days of war some 200,000 refugees have already crossed the border here, with their pain and uncertainty in tow: the line on the map that formally separates Poland from the war is just four and a half hours away from driving. Like going from Buenos Aires to Mar del Plata.\par \par \uc2 To continue reading the full article click here.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:53\par \par \uc2 New satellite images show the advance of troops against Kiev.This image shows an overview of a part of a large deployment (Photo: \uc2 Maxar Technologies\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 This image shows an overview of a part of a large deployment (Photo: \uc2 Maxar Technologies\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 As the fourth consecutive day of attacks on Ukraine unfolds, and after the Russian military redoubled its efforts to overrun the Ukrainian capital Kiev on Saturday, new satellite images captured on Sunday showed how the Russian offensive progressed.\par \par \uc2 They were taken by the \uc2 Maxar\uc2  satellite that captured the deployment of Russian ground forces in several areas of Ivankiv, a town located north of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 To read the full article click here.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:42\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president portends "anti-war coalition in action".Volodimir Zelenski tweeted this, revealing his contacts with British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  and Polish President \uc2 Andrzej Duda\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:29\par \par \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2  talks with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and follows the conflict "with caution"\uc2 .Jair Bolsonaro\uc2  and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . Photo Reuters.,\par \par \uc2 Brazil's president spoke this Sunday with his Russian counterpart, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and affirmed that the South American giant's position in the face of the war that Moscow launched over Ukraine will continue to be one of "caution," the president told a press conference.\par \par \uc2 "Our position has to be quite cautious, we cannot act when we are trying to solve a case that is serious," Bolsonaro said at a press conference on the premises of a military base in Guaruj\u225\'00\'E1, on the