 of armored vehicles," Ukrainian official sources reported.\par \par \uc2 "Berdiansk is occupied by the adversary, there were no troops of ours there, the city was conquered," Alexei Arestovich, an adviser to the Ukrainian presidency, told journalists, according to the Russian news agency Sputnik.\par \par \uc2 Russia had earlier reported that its troops were blockading the towns of Berdiansk and Kherson, and had taken control of the town of Guenichesk and the Chernobaevka airfield in Kherson province, according to Defense Ministry spokesman Igor Konashenkov.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:26\par \par \uc2 Paul Cow\par \par \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war also hit vodka.Russian vodka. File photo.\par \par \uc2 The boycott of Russian products by almost everyone took off on social networks on the very first day of the war, last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In Poland it took shape immediately with a hashtag calling not to buy Russian vodka. It was not just any rejection: in this country vodka is a subject that is taken seriously.\par \par \uc2 And they take it seriously: Poland ranks third among the largest consumers of this drink per head, with 7.7 liters per year (the ranking is headed, comfortably, by Russia, with 13.9).\par \par \uc2 To read the full article click here.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:09\par \par \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2  to hold emergency meeting on MondayThe United Nations Security Council voted for the 193-member General Assembly to hold an emergency session on Monday on Russia's invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The vote had 11 votes in favor, Russia voting against and China, India and the United Arab Emirates abstaining.\par \par \uc2 It was a vote exactly like a resolution last Friday, which demanded that Moscow stop its attack immediately and withdraw all its troops. But in that case, Russia used its veto power and the resolution failed.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  Sergiy Kyslytsya called for a General Assembly meeting to be held under the so-called "Uniting for Peace" resolution, initiated by the United States and adopted in November 1950 to circumvent Soviet vetoes during the Korean War.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:50\par \par \uc2 US approved delivery of Stinger anti-aircraft missiles to Ukraine. For the first time since the outbreak of the conflict, the United States approved direct shipment of Stinger missiles to Ukraine as part of a package approved by the White House last Friday.\par \par \uc2 The exact timing of when they will be delivered is unknown, but officials say Washington is working on the logistics of the shipment. Officials agreed to discuss the decision on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 The move comes on the heels of Germany's announcement that it will send 500 Stinger missiles and other weapons and supplies to Ukraine. The high-velocity Stingers are highly accurate, and are used to shoot down helicopters and other aircraft.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:28\par \par \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  denounced Russia's use of cluster bombsThe human rights advocacy organization said there was a cluster bomb attack on a hospital in the Ukrainian town of Vuhledar, in the pro-independence Donetsk area, which left four civilians dead and 10 others wounded.\par \par \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  said it confirmed the information through telephone interviews with a doctor at the hospital and a representative of the facility, Central City Hospital, as well as photographs of two of the deceased.\par \par \uc2 The organization also said that other snapshots posted on social networks or sent to the hospital show the remains of one of the weapons apparently used in the attack, a Tochka 9M79 ballistic missile with a 9N123 cluster warhead.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:05\par \par \uc2 International Judo Federation\uc2  suspended \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  as honorary president. In the wake of the war between Russia and Ukraine, the \uc2 International Judo Federation\uc2  (\uc2 IJF\uc2 ) decided to suspend \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  as honorary president and ambassador of the body.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president is a recognized passionate of the sport and a black belt. In Russia, judo has a great weight for being one of the sports in which sambo, its national sport, was reflected to forge its system of body-to-body defense.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:45\par \par \uc2 Russian airline \uc2 Aeroflot\uc2  suspends all flights to EuropeThe airline announced the suspension as of Monday of all its flights to Europe, following the \uc2 EU\uc2 's decision to close its airspace to Russian aircraft.\par \par \uc2 "As a result of airspace restrictions implemented by the European authorities, \uc2 Aeroflot\uc2  is suspending its flights to all European destinations as of February 28, 2022, until further notice," the airline said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  said Sunday that it would close its airspace to Russian carriers in retaliation for the invasion of Ukraine, a measure also adopted by several non-EU European countries and Canada.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:28\par \par \uc2 Sweden and Denmark to supply Ukraine with military weaponsThe governments of Sweden and Denmark announced on Sunday the shipment of military hardware and further economic aid to the Ukrainian authorities to cope with the war against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Sweden authorized the shipment of 5,000 rocket launchers and equipment valued at 400 million Swedish kronor (37.7 million euros), in addition to another 500 million kronor (47.2 million euros).\par \par \uc2 The Danish government, meanwhile, announced the donation of 2,700 rocket launchers to Ukraine, a day after pledging military and medical equipment, plus DKK 50 million (\u8364\'20\'AC6.7 million) in humanitarian aid.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:58\par \par \uc2 War report: 14 children among 352 Ukrainian civilians killedAt least 352 Ukrainian civilians, including 14 children, lost their lives since the Russian invasion began on February 24.\par \par \uc2 This was reported Sunday by the \uc2 Ukrainian Ministry of Health\uc2 , which added that so far 1,684 people have been injured, 116 of them children.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:45\par \par \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2  to hold emergency meeting on MondayThe United Nations Security Council voted in favor of the 193-member General Assembly holding an emergency session on Monday to discuss Russia's invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The vote to authorize the emergency session had 11 votes in favor, Russia voting against, and China, India and the United Arab Emirates abstaining.\par \par \uc2 The result of the vote was exactly the same as a resolution on Friday demanding that Moscow stop its attack immediately and withdraw all its troops. In that case, Russia used its veto power and the resolution failed.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:31\par \par \uc2 Cristina Kirchner tweeted about the Russia-Ukraine war and compared the conflict with the Falklands conflictCristina Kirchner referred to the war unleashed in Ukraine due to Russia's invasion in a thread of tweets, with a comparison with Malvinas and without mentioning the words "war" and "invasion" or \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . See more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:16\par \par \uc2 US urges its citizens to leave Russia as long as there are flightsThe US embassy in Moscow on Sunday urged its citizens in Russia to leave the country "immediately" while flights are available, as numerous countries have closed their airspace to Russian aircraft in response to the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The embassy posted this message on its website "in the face of the growing number of airlines canceling flights to and from Russia, and given that numerous countries have closed their airspace to Russian airlines."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:09\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 : Putin's nuclear alert is a "distraction"Johnson met with members of the Ukrainian community in London. Photo: AFP.\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  said Sunday that Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's announcement to put his nuclear force on alert seeks to divert attention from the fierce resistance encountered by his troops in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "I think it is a distraction from what is actually happening in Ukraine," Johnson said after meeting with members of the Ukrainian community in London.\par \par \uc2 "This is an innocent people facing unprovoked aggression. What is really happening is that they are defending themselves more effectively, more resiliently, than the Kremlin imagined," he added.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:43\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claims to have recaptured Kharkov, the country's second largest cityThe corpse of a Russian soldier lies next to a destroyed Russian military vehicle in a suburb of Kharkov. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 Kharkov, Ukraine's second most populous city, was under control of local forces on Sunday, a few hours after fighting intensified in the city.\par \par \uc2 The city's mayor, Igor Trekhov, was emphatic: "We have survived perhaps the hardest day in the history of Kharkov since the world war," a reference to the 1941 Nazi invasion. Read more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:36\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  countries to provide Ukraine with fighter jetsEuropean Union foreign affairs chief \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2  . Photo: EFE.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) will financially support countries of the bloc to send fighter jets to Ukraine to resist Russia's offensive, \uc2 EU\uc2  diplomacy chief \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2  said Sunday.\par \par \uc2 "We are going to send even fighter jets. We are hardly talking about ammunition. We are providing more important weaponry for a war," Borrel said at the end of a video conference of European foreign ministers, in response to a request from Ukrainian Foreign Minister Dmitro Kuleba.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Borrel confirmed that the bloc will allocate 500 million euros (more than $500 million) to finance the supply of lethal and non-lethal military equipment to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:04\par \par \uc2 More than 5,000 detained over protests in Russia against invasion of UkrainePolice detain a man during a demonstration against Russia's invasion of Ukraine in St. Petersburg. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 Since the invasion of Ukraine began, Russian authorities have detained 5,250 people for demonstrating against the war, according to OVD-info, an organization specializing in tracking arrests and defending detainees.\par \par \uc2 OVD-info reported police abuses in the cities of Moscow, St. Petersburg, Kazan, Novosibirsk and Nizhny Novgorod. Read more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:55\par \par \uc2 Ukraine recruits "foreign volunteers" for defenseUkrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  called on citizens from all over the world to form an "international legion" of volunteers to be ready to fight alongside Ukrainian forces against Russian invasion\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:21\par \par \uc2 Ukraine asks \uc2 EU\uc2  to speed up aid Ukrainian Ambassador to the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) and \uc2 NATO\uc2  Vsevolod Chentsov on Sunday urged to "accelerate and increase" cooperation with his country in economic, military and humanitarian fields, and assured that Ukraine is "ready to continue diplomacy, but without any preconditions".\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a press conference in Brussels after the meeting of European interior ministers he attended, Chentsov stressed that his country "is fighting, is bleeding, but has already won" because "the strength, resilience and spirit of the people is impossible to kill" and that is something that "the Russian leadership did not take into account."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:14\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  to finance arms purchases and deliveries to UkraineUrsula von der Leyen and \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2  during their joint press conference in Brussels. Photo: EFE.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) will finance the purchase and delivery of weapons to Ukraine, which is suffering a military invasion by Russia, announced this Sunday the President of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  foreign affairs chief \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , for his part, confirmed that the bloc will allocate 450 million euros (more than $500 million) to finance the supply of lethal military equipment to Ukraine and another 50 million euros for non-lethal equipment, such as fuel and protective gear.\par \par \uc2 "For the first time in history, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  will finance the purchase and delivery of weapons and other equipment for a country that is under attack," \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "We are closing airspace for the Russians (...) Russian aircraft will no longer be able to land, take off, or fly over EU airspace (...) This includes also the private jets of oligarchs," the official added.\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  also stated that in another unprecedented sanction, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  will ban on its territory "the Kremlin's press machine", which includes Russia Today and Sputnik and their subsidiaries.\par \par \uc2 The official also advanced that the \uc2 EU\uc2  will sanction Belarus for its role in the Russian military aggression on Ukrainian territory.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:02\par \par \uc2 Attacks on radioactive waste plant in Ukraine recorded, although they did not cause any damageUkraine informed the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  that in the early hours of Sunday morning it recorded missile attacks on a radioactive waste facility in Kiev that did not cause damage.\par \par \uc2 As reported hours later by the \uc2 IAEA\uc2 , the facility continues to operate normally, as do the rest of the country's nuclear power plants.\par \par \uc2 The agency's director general, \uc2 Rafael Mariano Grossi\uc2 , made an urgent appeal to the parties to the conflict to "refrain from military or other actions that could threaten the safety of nuclear facilities."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:57\par \par \uc2 "At the moment we are surrounded," says the mayor of KievVitali Klitschko acknowledged the difficult situation in the Ukrainian capital. Photo: AP.\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Kiev acknowledged Sunday that the Ukrainian capital is surrounded, so it would be impossible to evacuate its inhabitants.\par \par \uc2 Vitali Klitschko\uc2  expressed his pride in the mood of the population but also his anxiety about how long they will be able to resist, at a time when Russian troops are closing the siege around the city.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the AP on Sunday, the mayor was silent for several seconds when asked if Kiev residents would have to be evacuated should the Russians reach the city.\par \par \uc2 "That we cannot do, because all the streets are blocked, at the moment we are surrounded,'' he finally said.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:38\par \par \uc2 Massive marches in Europe against Russian invasion of UkraineThousands of people mobilized in the cities of Prague, Berlin and Lisbon, respective capitals of the Czech Republic, Germany and Portugal, to express their solidarity with Ukraine, amid the escalating advance of Russia's troops. See more\par \par \uc2 Thousands of demonstrators marched through the streets of Berlin. Photo: Reuters.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:19\par \par \uc2 Russian official's unexpected apology for invasion of Ukraine: 'There is no justification'The head of the Russian delegation to a major United Nations climate summit apologized Sunday for his country's invasion of Ukraine, which he said lacked justification.\par \par \uc2 "Let me present an apology on behalf of all Russians who could not prevent this conflict," Oleg Anisimov said during the closed-door meeting of the \uc2 Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change\uc2 . Read more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:15\par \par \uc2 The idea of a nuclear war is "inconceivable", says \uc2 UN\uc2  spokesmanThe idea of a nuclear war in Europe is "inconceivable," United Nations spokesman \uc2 Stephane Dujarric\uc2  said Sunday, after Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  announced he had put the nuclear deterrent on alert.\par \par \uc2 "The very idea of a nuclear conflict is simply inconceivable," the spokesman said, when asked for a reaction from \uc2 UN\uc2  Secretary-General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2  to the Russian leader's statements.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:02\par \par \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  to meet on Monday.File image of a recent \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  meeting in New York. Photo: \uc2 Xinhua\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following the decision to activate the Kremlin's defensive nuclear deterrent systems, a new \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  meeting will be held on Monday. The focus of the meeting will be the humanitarian situation in Ukraine, diplomatic sources said. An extraordinary \uc2 Council of European Union\uc2  defense ministers will also be held. The meeting will be held by videoconference. See more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:49\par \par \uc2 Russia's invasion of Ukraine causes displacement of "more than seven million people".The military offensive launched by Russia in Ukraine causes displacement of "more than seven million" people, the European Commissioner for Crisis Management, Slovenian \uc2 Janez Lenarcic\uc2 , said on Sunday. "Currently the estimate of the number of displaced Ukrainians is more than seven million people," Lenarcic added at a press conference. "We are witnessing what could become the biggest humanitarian crisis on the European continent in many years," he added.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a "vast majority" of \uc2 European Union\uc2  countries are in favor of activating the regulation allowing to grant temporary protection throughout the bloc to all Ukrainian displaced persons as a result of the war initiated by Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 People trying to leave Kiev in the face of a siege by Russian troops. AFP Photo/Emilio Morenatti.\par \par \uc2 "I have noted a large majority (of countries) to be able to quickly use this possibility," said French Interior Minister G\u233\'00\'E9rald Darmanin at a press conference following the extraordinary meeting held in Brussels.\par \par \uc2 The Commissioner for Home Affairs, \uc2 Ylva Johansson\uc2 , said for her part that "the time has come" to activate the temporary protection directive and detailed that the legislative proposal in this line will be ready to be discussed at the meeting of the ministers of the Interior that was planned for some time for this Thursday.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:24\par \par \uc2 Ukraine will try to negotiate with Russia, but with skepticism"We have to try," the Ukrainian president said. Photo: Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine wants to "try" to negotiate with Russia although without much conviction that talks scheduled for Sunday can end the invasion, Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski said. "I say things clearly, as always: I don't think it will work" but "we have to try," Zelensky said in a video, ahead of the scheduled talks on the border with Belarus. He added that he did not want Ukrainians to think in the future that he had "not tried to stop the war when there was even a small chance of doing so."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:17\par \par \uc2 Call for EU-wide airspace closure for Russia and new sanctions against BelarusAfter 20 countries announced the closure of their airspace to Russia, \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  proposed to extend the measure to the entire territory of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . In practice, this means banning the landing, take-off or passage of any Russian aircraft. She also called for sanctions against Belarus for its collaboration in the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 These measures are in addition to the freezing of \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions and the exclusion of several Russian banks from SWIFT announced yesterday, as well as European funding for the purchase and delivery of arms and military equipment to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Commission's proposal has to receive the approval of the Council (the countries) before it can enter into force after publication in the EU Official Journal.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:05\par \par \uc2 Russia acknowledges the existence of dead, wounded and prisoners among its troopsThe \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  for the first time acknowledged for the first time the existence of dead, wounded and prisoners during the "special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " ordered by Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately we have comrades killed and wounded," \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  spokesman Igor Konashenkov told a press conference, without specifying the number of casualties.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 13:51\par \par \uc2 Argentine families with surrogate babies have already arrived in PolandFive Argentine families who had traveled to Ukraine for surrogacy and claimed help are already in Poland, Argentine Foreign Minister Santiago Cafiero said. See more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 13:15\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people marched for peace in PragueIn Prague, thousands of demonstrators marched for peace in Ukraine. Photo: AFP.\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of people showed their support for Ukraine in the center of Prague on Sunday, in a new act of solidarity reminiscent of Thursday's and now joined by artists, businessmen students, politicians and local church figures.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the Czech Republic donated ammunition and light weapons to Kiev, made available train convoys with a capacity of 6,000 people for evacuation work and approved today, in an extraordinary council of ministers, a shipment of weapons worth 16 million euros.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 13:09\par \par \uc2 WHO\uc2  warns of difficulties in transporting medical suppliesThe \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO) \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  (WHO) on Sunday called for safe corridors to deliver emergency medical supplies on the fourth day of the Russian invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "It is imperative that life-saving medical supplies, including oxygen, reach those who need them," the \uc2 UN\uc2  agency said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 WHO\uc2 , oxygen supplies in Ukraine have reached "a very dangerous situation," with "trucks unable to transport oxygen between factories and hospitals."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 12:47\par \par \uc2 Russian nuclear force alert is "irresponsible," says \uc2 NATO\uc2  chiefStoltenberg called Putin's decision "irresponsible." Photo: AP.\par \par \uc2 NATO\uc2  Secretary General \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2  on Sunday called Russia "irresponsible" after President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  put the Russian military's nuclear "deterrent force" on alert.\par \par \uc2 "It's dangerous rhetoric. It's irresponsible behavior," Stoltenberg told CNN television network.\par \par \uc2 "And if you combine this rhetoric with what they're doing on the ground in Ukraine, waging war against an independent sovereign nation, carrying out a full-blown invasion, it adds gravity to the situation." he added.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 12:37\par \par \uc2 More countries close their airspace to Russian aircraftCanada and Austria, a non-NATO European country, joined the list of nations closing their airspace to Russian aircraft in response to the invasion of Ukraine by \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's troops.\par \par \uc2 "We will hold Russia accountable for its unprovoked attacks on Ukraine," Canadian Transport Minister \uc2 Omar Alghabra\uc2  announced on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Aircraft registered in Russia or belonging to or chartered by Russian citizens must no longer enter Austrian airspace or land at Austrian airports," Austrian Minister for Mobility, Energy and Climate Protection \uc2 Leonore Gewessler\uc2  wrote for her part, also on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two countries thus joined Germany, France, Spain, Italy, the Netherlands, Belgium and Ireland, which announced the same measure today, after it was announced inthe Baltic States, Poland, the Czech Republic, Romania, Bulgaria and Slovenia.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 12:12\par \par \uc2 We will not surrender", Ukraine's response to Putin's nuclear threatUkrainian Foreign Minister \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 . Photo: AP.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Foreign Minister Dmitro Kuleba warned that putting Russian nuclear forces on alert is aimed at "putting pressure" on Ukraine, but affirmed that his country will not capitulate to Moscow.\par \par \uc2 In a video conference, Kuleba assured, "We will not surrender. We will not capitulate. We will not give up a single inch of our territory."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 12:03\par \par \uc2 Putin fabricates threats to justify aggression, says U.S.Jen Psaki. Photo credit: AP.\par \par \uc2 The United States accused Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  of "fabricating threats" by placing his nuclear deterrent forces on high alert amid the Ukraine crisis.\par \par \uc2 "This is a pattern from President Putin that we've seen throughout this conflict: fabricating threats that don't exist in order to justify further aggression," White House press secretary Jen Psaki told ABC when asked about Moscow's announcement.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 11:24\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian and Russian representatives will meet to hold dialogueUkrainian delegates will meet with Russian diplomats, the Ukrainian presidency said Sunday, shortly after Russia announced that its delegation had left for Belarus to take part in bilateral dialogues.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski's office reported via a Telegram message that the two sides will meet at an unspecified location on the Belarusian border. It did not give a specific time of the meeting. Read more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 11:11\par \par \uc2 368 thousand Ukrainians fled the country: more than half took refuge in PolandIn Poland already received more than 200 thousand Ukrainians fleeing their country. Photo: EFE.\par \par \uc2 Some 368,000 refugees fled the fighting in Ukraine since the outbreak of the Russian invasion, of which more than half (more than 200 thousand) entered Poland, and their number "continues to grow," the United Nations and Polish authorities said Sunday.\par \par \uc2 This number "is based on data provided by national authorities," the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) stressed in a tweet.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:50\par \par \uc2 Kiev confirmed that it will send a delegation to negotiate with Russia on the Ukrainian-Belarusian borderThis was reported by the office of Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky. "We agreed that the Ukrainian delegation would meet with the Russian delegation without preconditions on the Ukrainian-Belarusian border near the Pripiat River," according to the official Telegram channel of the Ukrainian leader.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:37\par \par \uc2 Putin puts Russian nuclear deterrent forces on alert, AP reports.At a meeting, he ordered his defense minister and the head of the Russian Armed Forces to put Russia's nuclear deterrent forces "on special combat alert."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:24\par \par \uc2 Moscow claims that Kiev confirmed sending representatives to Belarus for negotiations. This was reported by the head of the Russian delegation, Vladimir Medinsky, to the Russian agency TASS "At around 15:00 (local time, 11:00 Argentina time) we received confirmation that the negotiations will be held in the Gomel region, as we had suggested," Medinsky said. Kiev has not yet confirmed the information.\par \par \uc2 Hours earlier, it was Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky himself who had refused to participate in the agreements.\par \par \uc2 ? According to the Belarusian official agency Belta, the negotiations are scheduled to take place "in the Gomel region, on the Belarusian-Ukrainian border".\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:02\par \par \uc2 More sanctions against Russia: Putin loses honorary judo postFile photo of Russian President Vladimir Putin at a judo training. Photo: AFP.\par \par \uc2 Due to the attacks on Ukraine, Vladimir Putin temporarily lost his highest official position in judo. The International Federation made the decision on Sunday to remove him from the status of honorary president of the body.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president is an avid judo player and attended the discipline's events at the 2012 Olympics.\par \par \uc2 The judo federation is one of the few Olympic bodies that referred to the Russian invasion of Ukraine as "war''. Other bodies have used phrases such as "escalation of the conflict''.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:56\par \par \uc2 Governor of Kharkov, the second largest Ukrainian city, says he maintains control in the face of Russian incursion A Russian armored vehicle set on fire in the streets of Kharkov. Photo: AFP.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's second city of Kharkov is under control of Ukrainian forces, Governor Oleg Sinegubov said Sunday, a few hours after fighting in the city intensified.\par \par \uc2 "Kharkov is fully under our control," Sinegubov wrote on social networks, assuring that "elimination of enemies in the city" was underway.\par \par \uc2 According to him, "the Russian enemy is completely demoralized", leaving their vehicles abandoned, and even, he said, groups of Russian soldiers "surrender to the Ukrainian army".\par \par \uc2 Kharkov, with a population of 1.4 million, is the main city in northeastern Ukraine and is located near the border with Russia and the territories under the control of pro-Russian separatists, Donetsk and Lugansk. Read more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:19\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis' plea for peace: "Silence the weapons".The Pope, at his Angelus this Sunday. (AP)\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis today called for an end to the war in Ukraine and recalled that "ordinary people are the real victims" of armed conflicts, while calling on the international community to open "humanitarian corridors" for people fleeing the European country after the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 "In these days we have been upset by a tragic thing, war. Many times we prayed so that this path would not be invoked, and we did not stop talking, we prayed to God intensely," the pontiff said while praying the traditional Sunday Angelus from the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 "I am disconsolate for what is happening in Ukraine and in other parts of the world", "silence the weapons, God is with the peacemakers, not with those who use violence", he affirmed. See more\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:13\par \par \uc2 Ukraine sues Russia at the International Court in The HagueIt was announced by President Volodimir Zelensky via his Twitter account. He also called for "celerity" to the Dutch court. The full note.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:11\par \par \uc2 The number of refugees fleeing Ukraine reaches 368 thousand people, UNHCR says Ukrainian refugees arrive in Przemysl, Poland, on Sunday. (AP)\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:11\par \par \uc2 Belgium, Finland and Denmark close their airspace to Russian aircraft.It was announced on Sunday morning by authorities of the three countries. The Danish chancellor also announced that they will push for an EU-wide ban.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:10\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president refuses to hold talks with Russia in BelarusThe Russian government sent a delegation to Belarus, ostensibly to hold talks with Ukraine in search of an agreement that would allow a cessation of hostilities.\par \par \uc2 However, Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelensky rejected the offer and said that talks in Minsk might have been possible if Russia had not attacked Ukraine from Belarusian territory.\par \par \uc2 Despite that, the president left the door open for negotiations in another country.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220301ei31005d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
