\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Ruble records record drop after new Western sanctions\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Russian ruble posted record declines against the dollar on Monday (28) after Western nations announced a set of tough sanctions over the weekend to punish Russia for its invasion of Ukraine, including restrictions on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The ruble even fell to 119.50 per dollar in Asian trading, a record low of 30 percent from last Friday's close (25). It subsequently recovered to around 110 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered his military command to put its nuclear-armed forces on high alert on Sunday (27) in response to Western reprisals for its war against Ukraine - the biggest attack on a European state since World War II.\par \par \uc2 Illustration shows Russian ruble \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in front of chart on downward trajectory - Dado Ruvic - 24.Feb.2022/Reuters Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 CBR\uc2 ) announced a series of measures on Sunday to support domestic markets as it struggles to manage the fallout from sanctions that will block some of the country's banks from the Swift international payments system\par \par \uc2 . The bank said it will resume buying gold on the domestic market, launch an unlimited repurchase auction and ease restrictions on banks' open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found some support last week with the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2014, when Moscow annexed Crimea from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also read In act of financial warfare, West to seize Russian reserves and cause panic Russians rush to withdraw cash as West imposes sanctions on banks See the list of sanctions on Russia that the West has imposed for its invasion of Ukraine Sanctions on Russia plunge global economy into new unknown Europe offers fighters to Ukraine after Putin puts nuclear forces on alert West cuts Russian banks from global financial system, says G7 Analysts at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  said the sanctions on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves removed what little support the ruble had.\par \par \uc2 "Even gold is not liquid if no one can use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for it. There will be a complete collapse of the ruble today," they wrote.\par \par \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 , said in a note on Sunday that "a ruble collapse looks inevitable on Monday morning" and that there was an increased risk of Russian debt default as a result of the weekend's events.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220228ei2s0039s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
