\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war, \uc2 IMF\uc2  agreement, gas cuts in industry, cattle raising in Corrientes and loss of reserves: BAE Negocios' topics of the day\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Alert for gas cuts for industry in view of the deficit in the energy trade balance The industrialists turned on all their alarms due to the certain possibility of programmed cuts in production due to the lack of gas during the winter period due to the combination of a new fall in the Bolivian offer and a fiscal cost for the import of liquefied natural gas (LNG) which goes against the reduction scheme proposed by the new agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) due to the lack of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Due to fires, it is estimated that cattle raising in Corrientes will lose $30,000 million According to private estimates, the fires in Corrientes will have a major impact on livestock activity, with economic losses of close to $30 billion. According to what this newspaper was able to reconstruct from consultations with the livestock and meat chain in that province, there will be a sharp drop in productivity, which will be reflected in fewer calves available for domestic consumption.\par \par \uc2 Debt and tourism accounted for the strong loss of reserves in 2022 Debt payments, added to a foreign tourism that continues to recover steadily, marked the worst January in terms of dollars since 2014. The opening of 2022 started with twin reds in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market: negative in the current and financial accounts. February repeated the dynamics of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage although, due to unfavorable seasonality, the BCRA noted that the result was better than expected. Reserves lost USD2,600 million so far this year. Net reserves are at minimum levels and become negative if liabilities are subtracted from assets.\par \par \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war: Zelenski agreed to hold talks tomorrow with Russian delegation at the border with Belarus. Four days after the beginning of the Russian invasion of Ukraine, the government of Volodymir Zelensky agreed to hold talks tomorrow with the administration of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  at the border between \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Belarus. The meeting was achieved through the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Belarusian President, \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2 , and will be without preconditions.\par \par \uc2 Agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 : fiscal adjustment may reach 9 billion dollars in two years "The agreement is a court marking of Guzman's speech. This is an adjustment, which will be seen much more in the fine print", Javier Timerman, in his role as Wall Street investor, had told BAE Negocios. The Instituto de Pensamiento y Pol\u237\'00\'EDticas P\u250\'00\'FAblicas (IPyPP), directed by Claudio Lozano and coordinated by Ana Ramieri, put a number to this adjustment: 9 billion dollars that will cease to circulate in the real economy between 2022 and 2023.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220228ei2s002we\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
