\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble tumbles to record low\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2022\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble tumbled to a record low against the dollar on Monday, after Western nations announced a harsh set of sanctions over the weekend to punish Russia for its invasion of Ukraine, including sanctions on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The dollar/rouble rate was up 41.50% at a record 119.00 per dollar, in Asian trading. So far this month, the dollar is up 53.77% versus rouble.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered his military command to put nuclear-armed forces on high alert on Sunday, in response to Western reprisals for his war on Ukraine - the biggest assault on a European state since World War Two.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a slew of measures on Sunday to support domestic markets, as it scrambled to manage the fallout of the sanctions that will block some banks from the SWIFT international payments system.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would resume buying gold on the domestic market, launch a repurchase auction with no limits and ease restrictions on banks' open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had found some support last week from the first \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2014, when Russia annexed Crimea from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  said the sanctions on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves removed what little support the rouble had.\par \par \uc2 "Even the gold is not liquid if nobody can use \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for it. There will be a complete collapse in the rouble today..." they wrote.\par \par \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 , said in a note on Sunday, "a collapse in the rouble appears inevitable on Monday morning", and there was an increased risk of a Russian debt default as a result of the weekend developments.\par \par \uc2 "For the rouble whilst you might see it should sell off somewhat, I really doubt you are going to see people put on fresh bets to sell the rouble at these levels \u8211\'20\'13 so you might well see it weakening, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t think you will see people transacting all that heavily," said Peter Kinsella, London-based global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at UBP.\par \par \uc2 "There is a general lack of liquidity, and where you do see liquidity it is one sided, skewed to rouble sellers. It will be tricky, I can see rouble weakening quite severely \u8211\'20\'13 but just because it is weakening doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it will be transacting heavily." (Reporting by Vidya Ranganathan Additional reporting by Karin Strohecker in London Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-2-28T02:41:49.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220228ei2s007k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
