\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: another early morning terror in Kiev besieged by Russian troops\b0\par\par\uc2 34,142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 EN VIVONoticia en DesarrolloWhileRussian troops are advancing on Ukrainian territory, Kiev is facing a new dawn of terror. Zelenski's government announced that there will be "heavy air strikes" and a loud explosion lit up the skies of the country's capital. They ask citizens to seek shelter in bunkers and subway parking lots.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:00\par \par \uc2 Kharkov building hit and killedAnine-story building in Kharkov, Ukraine's second largest city, was hit by a Russian missile and one woman was killed and 20 other people evacuated, Ukraine's state emergency service confirmed.\par \par \uc2 Another 60 residents of the building had taken shelter in the basement and none were injured, but were evacuated after the impact.\par \par \uc2 Separately, according to CNN, a six-year-old boy was killed and several people were injured amid heavy fighting in a western district of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Serhii Chernysuk, a doctor at Kyiv's Okhmatdyt hospital, said that among the wounded were two teenagers and three adults.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:16\par \par \uc2 UN reported 240 civilian casualties in Russian attacks on UkraineTheUnited Nationsconfirmed at least 240 civilian casualties, including the deaths of at least 64 people\par \par \uc2 , in fighting in Ukraine that erupted since Russia's invasion on Thursday. The "actual numbers are believed to be considerably higher'' because many of the casualty reports have not yet been confirmed. The \uc2 UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs\uc2  (OCHA) released the count Saturday night from the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights (UNHCHR), which has strict methodologies and verification procedures on losses from the conflict.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:00\par \par \uc2 Germany closes airspace to RussiaTheGerman government closed airspace to Russia as part of sanctions imposed from the invasion of Ukraine, German Transport Minister Volker Wissing said\par \par \uc2 .German airline \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  will also immediately avoid Russian airspace due to the war, a \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  spokeswoman announced Saturday. The airline said it will no longer operate services to Russian destinations.\par \par \uc2 All flights to and from Russia were suspended as of Saturday for the next seven days.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:45\par \par \uc2 Tense calm in early morning in Kiev as Russian siege continuesInUkraine it is past 3 a.m. Sunday and a tense atmosphere is in the air in Kiev after residents were warned of possible shelling\par \par \uc2 .Following the attack on an oil terminal some 40 km south of Kiev, so far no explosions have been reported in the Ukrainian capital, which has suffered some shelling in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Russia's ground advance on Kiev appears to be stalled at the city limits amid concerted Ukrainian resistance.\par \par \uc2 However many expect an air strike and people take refuge in subway bunkers.\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian soldier walks past the debris of a burning military truck on a street in Kiev, Ukraine. Photo: AP26\par \par \uc2 .02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:27\par \par \uc2 From Ukraine Believe Snake Island Border Guards Alive andPrisonersBorder guards on the Black Sea's Snake Island, which was seized by Russian forces, may still be alive\par \par \uc2 , according to a statement issued Saturday by Ukraine's State Border Guard Service (SBGSU)."We firmly believe that all Ukrainian defenders of Snake Island may still be alive," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Both President Zelensky and official agencies had said on Friday that all the soldiers had died after Russian forces captured the small island .\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:11\par \par \uc2 Russia denounces "unprecedented cyber attack" on institutional websitesRussiatoday confirmed that institutional websites, with the Kremlin's in the lead, suffered an "unprecedented cyber attack" that was "successfully" repelled in most cases\par \par \uc2 ."The Ministry of Digital Transformation is facing an unprecedented scale of cyber-attacks. More than 50 DDoS attacks with a capacity of more than 1 TB were recorded on February 26, as well as a series of professional attacks targeting the utility portal," a statement said.\par \par \uc2 "All attacks were successfully repelled by specialists of the security center," the authorities added, according to Europa Press agency.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:41\par \par \uc2 Gas pipeline in flames after Russian shellingTheimages, showing the flames after the shelling of a gas pipeline in Kharkov, were made by the Ukrainian State Special Communications Service\par \par \uc2 .26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:18\par \par \uc2 Kremlin retaliation: Russia closes airspace to four countries Russia decided on Saturday to close its airspace to companies linked to or registered in Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Slovenia, in retaliation for similar measures taken by these countries\par \par \uc2 .The ban also concerns transit flights carried out in Russia by the same companies, the Russian civil aviation agency \uc2 Rosaviatsia\uc2  announced in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "Due to hostile decisions of the aviation authorities of Latvia, Lithuania, Slovenia and Estonia, the airlines of these states and/or those registered in them are subject to restrictions on flights to points on the territory of the Russian Federation, including transit flights through the airspace of the Russian Federation," the text specifies.\par \par \uc2 It concludes, "This decision was taken in accordance with the norms of international law in response to the ban on all civilian flights of aircraft operated by Russian and/or Russian-registered airlines to/from the territory of these states."\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:01\par \par \uc2 The shocking flames on a gas pipeline bombed by the Russian army 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:42\par \par \uc2 From the US they say that with the new sanctions Russia will be "a global economic and financial pariah" The new sanctions that the \uc2 European Union\uc2  , the United States and Canada announced on Saturday for Russia for invading Ukraine turned the country ruled by Vladimir Putin into a financial "pariah", a senior US official assured\par \par \uc2 ."Russia has become a global economic and financial pariah\par \par \uc2 ," he said, and now its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "cannot support the ruble (its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )."He insisted that only Putin can decide how much additional cost he is willing to take on," adding that a task force "will go after" the "yachts, jets, luxury cars and luxury homes" of Russian oligarchs.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:26\par \par \uc2 A powerful explosion lit up the sky over KievApowerful explosion lit up the sky over Kiev in the early hours of Sunday morning. Initial reports say it was a Russian bombing about 20 kilometers from the capital.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:05\par \par \uc2 Cuba holds US and NATO responsible for Russia's invasion of UkraineCubaon Saturday held the United States and NATO responsible for Russia's invasion and attack on Ukraine by pointing out that "the progressive expansion" of those countries toward Russian borders led to this scenario\par \par \uc2 ."The U.S. determination to continue NATO's progressive expansion towards the borders of the Russian Federation has led to a scenario, with implications of unpredictable scope, which could have been avoided," the \uc2 Cuban Foreign Ministry\uc2  's statement said.\par \par \uc2 And it adds: "The military movements carried out by the United States and NATO in recent months towards regions adjacent to the Russian Federation, preceded by the delivery of modern weapons to Ukraine, which as a whole amounts to a progressive military encirclement, are well known".\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:44\par \par \uc2 " We will make sure that Putin no longer uses his war funds," warn from the \uc2 European Union\uc2  after sanctions againstRussiaEuropean Commission President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  announces sanctions against\par \par \uc2 RussiaEuropean Commission President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  on Saturday took aim at Vladimir Putin as she announced new economic measures against Russia for its invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 ."We will make sure that Putin no longer uses his war funds. We will stop \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions\par \par \uc2 ," the EU official said, adding that together with the United States and Canada they are ready to "ban Russian oligarchs from using our financial markets."26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:29\par \par \uc2 US , EU and Canada implemented the sanction Russia feared the mostRussia'sremoval from the Swift system was one of the most claimed. Photo Credit: ReuterThe\par \par \uc2 United States, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and Canada on Saturday resolved to slap Russia with more sanctions for its invasion of Ukraine, including the one most feared by the Kremlin\par \par \uc2 .In a statement, the leaders of those countries announced that Russian banks will be removed from the \uc2 Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial Telecommunication\uc2  known as SWIFT? the international banking network.\par \par \uc2 In addition, they announced restrictive measures that will prevent \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from deploying its international reserves\par \par \uc2 ; limit the sale of citizenship, so-called golden passports, which allow wealthy Russians connected to the Russian government to become citizens of other countries; and launch a task force to identify and freeze the assets of sanctioned individuals and companies. Read more here.26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:08\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claims to have killed 1,000 Russian soldiers and captured300Ukrainian\par \par \uc2 soldierstake positions around a military installation as two cars burn on a street in Kiev. Photo credit: Emilio Morenatti.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claimed Saturday that its army killed more than 1,000 Russian soldiers since the start of the war launched by Vladimir Putin and to have captured more than 300 uniformed men who surrendered.\par \par \uc2 "The Russian army surrenders massively. Even senior officers surrender. Today the commander of a Russian military unit surrendered. The commander of the tank battalion also surrendered. We have already taken more than 300 regular fighters," said Oleksiy Arestovych, advisor to the Office of Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky, at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 As for the casualties suffered in the Russian ranks, the numbers are not definite he assured that there are "more than 1,000 men killed and about 2,500 wounded".\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:53\par \par \uc2 Tension in Kiev continues: sirens sound and citizens flee tosheltersSirens sounded again on Saturday night in Kiev, where a curfew is already in force\par \par \uc2 .Local authorities have urged all citizens to seek shelter in bunkers and dungeons, anticipating "heavy air strikes," according to local media.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:36\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson spoke with Zelenski and took aim at Russia: "It should be isolated diplomatically and financially "British Prime Minister Boris Johnson spoke Saturday with Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski and joined the call for more diplomatic and financial sanctions on Russia\par \par \uc2 ."Tonight I spoke with President @ZelenskyyUa . The heroism of the President and his people in defense of their country is impressive. We are clear: Russia must be isolated diplomatically and financially. I welcome greater willingness to exclude Russia from SWIFT," Johnson maintained.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:10\par \par \uc2 More than 3,000 detained in Russia over protests against Ukraine invasion Russian police detained those demonstrating against Russia's invasion of Ukraine. Photo: EFMore than\par \par \uc2 400 people were detained Saturday in various Russian cities in the third consecutive day of protests against the invasion of Ukraine, reported human rights NGO OVD-Info, which raised the total number of arrests since the start of the offensive to more than 3,000\par \par \uc2 ."At least 3,052 people were detained" since Thursday, including 467 this Saturday, in demonstrations that have multiplied across Russia despite being banned, the association detailed.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:54\par \par \uc2 The video published by the Russian embassy in Argentina and justifies the invasion of UkraineTheRussian embassy in Argentina published this Saturday a video in which a Serbian woman who survived the NATO bombings in 1999 assures that "the Russian state leadership" is not "celebrating for having opted for military action", and warns that the government of Vladimir Putin "seeks to put a brake on NATO and its imperial arrogance"\par \par \uc2 .26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:35\par \par \uc2 Putin's troops are allegedly dropping "toy bombs "A toy in the rubble of an attacked building in Kiev, Ukraine. Photo: APIn\par \par \uc2 the context of the violent confrontation between Ukraine and Russia that broke out with the invasion of Vladimir Putin's army, a new strategy to shell Ukrainian cities ignited more alerts among the inhabitants of the region\par \par \uc2 ."Attention! In the Sumy area, Russian planes are scattering children's toys, cell phones and valuables filled with explosives," tweeted the Verchovna Rada, the Ukrainian parliament, warning about the new action detected in the northeastern town near the Russian border.\par \par \uc2 The denunciation is in line with what President Volodymyr Zelensky had stated, who affirmed that Russia was attacking civilian populations, although Moscow affirms that its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are aimed at taking control of military targets. Read the full story here.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:15\par \par \uc2 100,000 Russian troops advance into Kiev and mayor teaches how to arm Molotov cocktails toresistUkrainian\par \par \uc2 soldierswalk past the remains of a burnt-out military truck on a Kiev street\par \par \uc2 .Nearly 100,000 Russian soldiers are advancing towards Kiev to try to take control of the Ukrainian capital and the mayor of the city, former world heavyweight champion Vitali Klitschko, has issued an instruction for citizens to arm Molotov cocktails to defend themselves.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, in the last hours, according to the Ukrainian government, more than 25,000 weapons were distributed among the citizens, in addition to thousands of bullets, grenade launchers and grenades.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian Minister of Defense, Oleksiy Reznikov, assured today that more than 3,000 invaders were eliminated and another 200 have been captured since Thursday. "More than 55 hours of resistance. The number of prisoners of war is growing. They did not expect so much resistance and are surrendering," he noted.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:37\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis spoke with Zelenski and expressed his "deep sorrow" for the war inUkrainePope Francis had a telephone conversation with Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski on Saturday and expressed his "deep sorrow" for the war unleashed after the Russian invasion\par \par \uc2 .It was the Ukrainian embassy in the Vatican that gave an account of the talk. "Today Pope Francis had a telephone conversation with President ???????? Volodymyr Zelenskyi. The Holy Father expressed his deepest sorrow for the tragic events taking place in our country," the Ukrainian embassy to the Holy See said.\par \par \uc2 Moments later Zelenskyi thanked Francis for trying to mediate for Russia to stop its attacks on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "Thank you Pope Francis @Pontifex for praying for peace in Ukraine and ceasefire. Ukrainian people feel the spiritual support of His Holiness," Zelenski wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis visited the Russian ambassador to the Vatican at noon on Friday and expressed his concern over Russia's attack on Ukraine. Francis took the unprecedented decision despite being in seclusion due to severe pain of inflammatory origin in his right knee that had forced him to cancel his engagements this week.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:22\par \par \uc2 UN expressed to Ukraine its "determination" to reinforce humanitarian aid in the face of the RussianinvasionUN Secretary General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2  spoke by telephone on Saturday with the President of Ukraine, Volodimir Zelenski, to express "the determination" of the organization "to reinforce humanitarian aid to the Ukrainian people\par \par \uc2 ," according to a UN statement.Guterres "informed the (Ukrainian) president that the \uc2 United Nations\uc2  will launch an appeal on Tuesday to fund (the organization's) humanitarian \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine," the text said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the UN called for "safe and unimpeded access" for humanitarian aid in Ukraine, overrun by the Russian army. The organization estimates that there will be more than 1.8 million people displaced in the near future due to the war.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:06\par \par \uc2 "It is our duty to help Ukraine defend itself from the invading army," German Chancellor said as he confirmed the armsshipmentGerman Chancellor Olaf Scholz assured Saturday that his country has "a duty" to "help Ukraine defend itself from Putin's invading army\par \par \uc2 ." He said this as he confirmed the shipment of 500 Stinger missiles and 1,000 anti-simile weapons. "The Russian invasion marks a turning point. It is our duty to support Ukraine as best we can to defend against Putin's invading army. That is why we are delivering 1000 anti-tank weapons and 500 Stinger missiles\par \par \uc2 to our friends in Ukraine," Scholz noted.26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:51\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian town residents' desperate attempt to stop advancing Russian tanksIna desperate attempt to stop the advancing army, a group of Ukrainian civilians stood in front of Vladimir Putin's army tanks\par \par \uc2 .Some of them were kneeling in front of the tanks or throwing their bicycles under the tracks. It happened in Bakhmach, about 150 km northeast of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:35\par \par \uc2 Russia publishes images of Chernobyl after its captureRussia on Saturday released footage taken in the Chernobyl exclusion zone, whose capture by Moscow's military on the first day of the invasion of Ukraine caused concern.\par \par \uc2 A video released Saturday by the \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  shows soldiers patrolling near the plant, next to a tank.\par \par \uc2 A soldier then says with his face covered that radiation levels are "under control" and assures that "protection of the area is being carried out (jointly) with the Ukrainian National Guard and civilian personnel working here."\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:16\par \par \uc2 Zelensky asked the UN to strip Russia of its voting rights in the Security Council Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelensky held a conversation with UN Secretary General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2  on Saturday and asked him to take away Russia's voting rights in the Security Council and to qualify its attacks as "genocide of people".\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 15:09\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian woman confronted Russian soldiers: "Take these seeds so that sunflowers will grow when you die here."A Ukrainian woman confronted a group of Russian soldiers in Kherson, southern Ukraine, and the video went viral. In the footage, the woman calls the soldiers fascists, occupiers and enemies and insists with a shocking phrase in which she assures them that they will die there.\par \par \uc2 "Take these seeds to grow sunflowers when you die here," the young woman defiantly told one of the Russian soldiers.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:59\par \par \uc2 Ukrainians flee in desperation amid sirens in KievDesperate and dragging suitcases many Ukrainian families were trying to flee Kiev on Saturday amid siren warning of possible Russian attacks in the country's capital.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:46\par \par \uc2 Red Cross warns of "devastating" consequences if war in Ukraine spreads to densely populated areas The \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  on Saturday expressed fears that the conflict in Ukraine could spread to densely populated areas, which could have "devastating" consequences for civilians, "including children, the sick and the elderly."\par \par \uc2 "We are concerned that the conflict will affect densely populated areas, including the capital, Kiev, and other major cities," Florence Gillette, head of the ICRC delegation in the Ukrainian capital, stressed in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The delegate called on the parties to the conflict not to forget their obligations under international humanitarian law, ensuring the protection of the civilian population and all persons not taking part in the fighting, including detainees, wounded and sick, and asked them to avoid "the use of explosive weapons with a wide area of impact in populated areas" as well as placing military targets in or near these areas.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:30\par \par \uc2 Germany to send 400 rocket launchers to Ukraine for defense against Russian invasion German Chancellor Olaf Scholz and Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski at a bilateral meeting in Munich, weeks ago. Photo: EFE\par \par \uc2 Germany on Saturday authorized the delivery to Ukraine of 400 anti-tank rocket launchers, breaking with its traditional policy of not exporting lethal weapons to conflict zones, a government source told AFP.\par \par \uc2 "Taking into account the Russian attack on Ukraine, the government is ready to urgently send the material required for Ukraine's defense," the source said.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 14:15\par \par \uc2 U.S. warns Russian forces "frustrated" at slow progress of invasion of Ukraine Soldiers of the Russian army, aboard an armored vehicle head towards central Ukraine. Photo: EFE\par \par \uc2 Russian military forces are increasingly "frustrated" at the lack of "progress" in their assault on Ukraine with the heaviest fighting centered around the northeastern Ukrainian city of Kharkov, Pentagon sources said Saturday.\par \par \uc2 "We know they have not made the progress they wanted, particularly in the northern part of Ukraine. What they've seen is determined resistance, and that has slowed them down," said a senior Defense Department official quoted by U.S. media outlets including the Washington Post and CNN. As a result, he said, Russian forces are "increasingly frustrated."\par \par \uc2 According to this official, the most violent fighting is taking place near Kharkov, the second largest city in Ukraine, with almost 1.5 million inhabitants and located in the northeast of the country, and he specified that the Russian military attack against Ukraine is advancing on three axes: from Belarus, in the north; from the Russian region of Belgorod, in the northeast; and from Crimea, in the south.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 13:57\par \par \uc2 As Russia launches new attack, Ukrainian president thanks the West for its supportUkrainian President Volodimir Zelensky during a message to the population. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski again used social networks to thank Western countries for their supports in the face of Russia's invasion.\par \par \uc2 "I spoke with the Prime Minister of the Netherlands. I thanked Mark Rutte for the decisions taken in support of Ukraine in the sphere of defense and security. The coalition against war is working!", Zelenski expressed in the networks.\par \par \uc2 He added: "The largest demonstration in the modern history of Estonia took place in support of Ukraine. I am grateful to the Estonian people and Alar Karis for their solidarity in these difficult times."\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 13:15\par \par \uc2 Russia orders all-out offensive after accusing Kiev of refusing dialogue Russia launches a new attack to take Kiev. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 Russia's Defense Ministry\uc2  on Saturday ordered the army to launch an all-out offensive after accusing Kiev of refusing to sit at the negotiating table with the Kremlin.\par \par \uc2 "After the Ukrainian side rejected the talks process, today all units were given the order to launch an offensive in all directions in correspondence with the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan," \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  spokesman Igor Konashenkov told a press conference.\par \par \uc2 The military officer recalled that the day before, "following the statements of the regime in Kiev about its readiness for dialogue, the combat actions in the main directions of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stopped", but now the offensive has resumed.\par \par \uc2 Konashenkov highlighted the advance in eastern Ukraine of separatist militias from Donetsk and Lugansk, which, he said, seized new villages with the help of the Russian Army in the direction of Rubezhnoye.\par \par \uc2 "Today the forces of the Lugansk People's Republic advanced to a depth of 46 kilometers and seized the villages of Schastie and Muratovo," he reported, noting that in their turn the Donetsk militias advanced about 10 kilometers and seized Starognatovka, Otkiabrskaya and Pavlopol.\par \par \uc2 "The nationalist battalions use so-called 'bander-mobiles', all-terrain vehicles with high-caliber machine guns or mortars," he noted, recalling that this type of transport was widely used by "international terrorists in Syria."\par \par \uc2 He also referred to clashes in the Black Sea, reporting that the day before, during the evacuation of 82 Ukrainian border guards who "voluntarily laid down their arms", Russian ships were attacked by 16 Ukrainian Navy gunboats, which he accused of taking cover with civilian vessels.\par \par \uc2 "The aim of this attack was, first of all, a revenge to the Ukrainian servicemen who surrendered, in order to accuse the Russian Army of murdering prisoners of war," he said, noting that six Ukrainian gunboats were sunk during the clash. Read more here\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 12:27\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis again called for peace in UkrainePope Francis renewed Saturday his call to stop the fighting in Ukraine, in a new message on the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  network in which he lamented "the madness of war" and urged the world to pray for peace.\par \par \uc2 The message has the hashtags "Let us pray together" and "Ukraine," and is accompanied by a plaque with a quote from Francis himself from Wednesday's general audience, a day before the start of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Russian military forces on Ukrainian soil.\par \par \uc2 "Jesus has taught us that the diabolical folly of violence is answered with the weapons of God, with prayer and fasting. May the Queen of Peace preserve the world from the madness of war," the quote said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday he had posted another message, in Russian and Ukrainian, with a quote from his latest encyclical, Fratelli Tutti, which warns that "every war leaves the world worse off than it found it."\par \par \uc2 Also yesterday the Pontiff had visited the Russian embassy to the Vatican to meet with Ambassador Alexander Avdeev in an attempt to try to mediate in the conflict between that country and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The half hour that Francis spent at the diplomatic headquarters of Via della Conciliazione 10, a few meters from St. Peter's Square, was the first Vatican move with the Pope as protagonist after the Secretary of State, Pietro Parolin, opened the possibility of a mediation on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 12:12\par \par \uc2 Russia forbids the press to use the word "invasion".Russia's broadcasting affairs authority demanded independent media to remove reports of civilian casualties and attacks on cities by Moscow's army in Ukraine and also vetoed the word "invasion."\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin's media authority has focused on reports containing "inaccurate information about the shelling of Ukrainian cities and the death of civilians as a result of the actions of Russian forces." In a statement it warned that access to such media will be prevented if the material is not removed.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has banned the dissemination of war information that does not have the government's approval, reports various international media.\par \par \uc2 Also, the \uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  , Russia's state media watchdog agency, has ordered domestic media to remove the terms "invasion," "offensive" or "declaration of war" to refer to the Ukrainian crisis.\par \par \uc2 "We emphasize that only official Russian sources have current and reliable information," \uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  noted in its statement Moscow officially defines its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a "special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " aimed at "peacekeeping."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Australian satellite operator Foxtel announced to \uc2 Russia Today\uc2  that it had suspended the channel's transmission "in consideration of concerns about the situation in Ukraine". This was announced by \uc2 Russia Today\uc2  itself on its official website.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 11:56\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  banned Russian state media from advertising on its platformFacebook banned all Russian state media from advertising on its platform. This was reported by \uc2 Nathaniel Gleicher\uc2 , head of security policy at \uc2 Facebook\uc2  . He said that Russian state media are now banned from running ads or monetizing content on its platform.\par \par \uc2 Via a tweet, Gleicher said \uc2 Facebook\uc2  would continue to apply tags to Russian state media. "We now prohibit Russian state media from running ads or monetizing on our platform anywhere in the world," he announced. "We are also continuing to apply tags to other Russian state media. These changes have already begun to be implemented and will continue through the weekend," he added.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 11:21\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president thanked Turkey for its supportTayyip Erdogan, president of Turkey. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 President of Ukraine, Volodymir Zelenski expressed in social networks thanks to the president of Turkey, a NATO member since 1952.\par \par \uc2 Zelenski stressed that Turkey banned the passage of Russian warships to the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 "I thank my friend Mr. President of Turkey Tayyip Erdo?an and the people of Turkey for their strong support. The ban on the passage of Russian warships to the Black Sea and significant military and humanitarian support for Ukraine are extremely important today. The people of Ukraine will never forget it!", Zelenski posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:56\par \par \uc2 Russia closes skies to aircraft from Bulgaria, Poland, Czech RepublicIn response to decisions by Bulgaria, Poland and the Czech Re