r.\par \par \uc2 He also urged Germany and Hungary to have the "courage" to support a motion to exclude Russia from the SWIFT international financial transactions system, a key instrument of global finance.\par \par \uc2 "We have stood our ground and successfully repelled enemy attacks. Fighting continues in numerous cities and regions of the country (...) but it is our army that controls Kiev and key localities around the capital," Zelensky said in a video posted on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and quoted by the AFP news agency.\par \par \uc2 "The occupiers wanted to blockade the center of our state and place puppets, as in Donetsk. We managed to thwart their plan," added Zelensky, who claimed that the Russian army "has not gained any advantage."\par \par \uc2 He also accused Russian troops of attacking residential areas and attempting to destroy electrical installations.\par \par \uc2 In a call to Western countries to harden their stance towards Russia, he considered that Ukraine "has the right to obtain its accession to the \uc2 European Union\uc2  ".\par \par \uc2 He also addressed Russians and urged them to call on their government to "immediately stop the war."\par \par \uc2 "We know that many people are shocked by the meanness and cruelty of your government," he said.\par \par \uc2 In several Russian cities, including Moscow and St. Petersburg, anti-war demonstrations were violently suppressed at the start of the invasion of Ukraine on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:05\par \par \uc2 Macron warns that the war in Ukraine "will last" after talks with Zelenski - The President of France, Emmanuel Macron, warned today that the war in Ukraine "will last" and said that "we must prepare", after a telephone conversation with his Ukrainian counterpart, Volodomir Zelenski, about the situation in the country in the face of the Russian offensive.\par \par \uc2 In the conversation, Zelenski informed Macron about the latest developments in the conflict and assured