ssian military plane carrying paratroopersAccording to a statement from the Army General Staff, the Il-76 heavy transport aircraft was shot down near Vasylkiv, a town 40 kilometers south of Kiev. The Russian military has not commented on the incident so far and the report could not be immediately verified.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:16\par \par \uc2 Paula Lugones\par \par \uc2 Argentina avoided condemning in the OAS Russia's invasion of UkraineLuis Almagro, secretary general of the OAS. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 Argentina avoided condemning within the \uc2 Organization of American States\uc2  (OAS) Russia's invasion of Ukraine, which was considered by most countries in the region as "illegal, unjustified" and a "flagrant violation of international law".\par \par \uc2 In a session of the OAS Permanent Council convened virtually to analyze the crisis in Ukraine, a declaration was voted that "strongly condemns the illegal, unjustified and unprovoked invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation and calls for the "immediate withdrawal of the military presence and the cessation of any further military action in that country." Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:50\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President calls for resistance: "We cannot lose capital".Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy calls for resistance in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy said that the invading Russian army is preparing a final offensive to take Kiev, the capital, during the early hours of Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 "We cannot lose the capital. I address our defenders, men and women on all fronts: tonight, the enemy is going to use all his forces to break through our defenses in the most vile, harsh and inhuman way. Tonight, they are going to attempt an attack," Zelenski said in a video posted on the presidential website.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the Ukrainian president expressed himself on social networks about a call from France: