arance a third set of sanctions against Russia that include not only Putin but also his foreign minister, Sergey Lavrov.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian prime minister declared that the world is witnessing "the horrors" of the war decided by Putin and that Canada is ready to put "all options on the table" to put an end to the Russian invasion of Ukraine. Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:52\par \par \uc2 Bulgaria closes its airspace to Russian aircraftBulgaria has on Friday night closed its airspace to all Russian aircraft, a measure taken "in solidarity with Ukraine" and for an indefinite period, the \uc2 Bulgarian Transport Ministry\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "All aircrafts licensed by the Russian Federation are prohibited from entering the sovereign space of the Republic of Bulgaria, including the skies over the territorial waters," reads the text of the official note.\par \par \uc2 A few moments earlier, the three mobile operators in the Balkan country (A1, Telenor and Vivacom) announced that all calls between Bulgaria and Ukraine up to 1,000 minutes will be free of charge.\par \par \uc2 The operators said they took this measure in solidarity with the population of Ukraine and the Bulgarian community in that country, which is estimated to be between 200,000 and 300,000 people.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:39\par \par \uc2 With Kiev under siege, Ukraine agreed to Russia's proposal to negotiate a ceasefireTension in Ukraine on the second day of Russian attacks. Photo:EFE\par \par \uc2 Sergey Nikiforov, presidential spokesman of Ukrainian government communicated this Friday that Ukraine accepted Russia's proposal to start negotiations, and stressed that his country is ready to talk about ceasefire and peace.\par \par \uc2 "I have to refute the claims that we refused to negotiate. Ukraine was and remains ready to talk about ceasefire and peace; this is our consistent position. We responded in accordance with the proposal of the President of Russia (Vladimir Putin)," Nikiforov stated on his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the spokesman remarked that "at this hour," the two countries are coordinating where and when they will move forward with the negotiation process. "The sooner the negotiations begin, the more chances there will be to restore normal life," he augured.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:32\par \par \uc2 Former Ukrainian Olympic boxing champion and brother of the mayor of Kiev fights on the front line Former Ukrainian Olympic and world boxing champion Vladimir Klitschko fights on the battlefront. AP Photo\par \par \uc2 Former Ukrainian Olympic and world boxing champion Vladimir Klitschko fights on the front lines to repel the invasion of Russian troops, as he had promised his older brother Vitali, also a world boxing champion and current mayor of Kiev Vladimir, 45, posted a photo showing him in combat fatigues as a Ukrainian army officer on the front lines at Hostomel airport, some 70 kilometers away from the capital Kiev.\par \par \uc2 The youngest of the Klitschko brothers (he is five years younger than Vitali, baptized as "Fists of Steel" for the power of his punches) was Olympic champion in the super heavyweight category at the Atlanta 96 Games and as a professional he reigned in the heavyweight category in the IBF, WBO and IBO, winning 23 world titles in that category?\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:25\par \par \uc2 Maria Laura Avignolo\par \par \uc2 British fighter jets carry out aerial surveillance in Poland and Romania Britain is no longer part of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  but remains an active member of NATO. With a Churchillian air, Prime Minister Boris Johnson did not rule out military action in the Ukraine-Russia crisis as an inevitable option.\par \par \uc2 British participation in NATO at this time is more active than that of the other partners. British fighter jets flew last night from Britain and Cyprus to carry out air surveillance missions, non-stop, in Poland and the Romanian border with Ukraine. Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:18\par \par \uc2 Like Britain, the United States says it will sanction Putin and his foreign ministerJen Psaki, the White House spokeswoman. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 The United States will sanction, like the United Kingdom and the \uc2 European Union\uc2  , Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov, White House spokeswoman Jen Psaki announced Friday.\par \par \uc2 She also indicated at a press conference that an attack against Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelensky would be "an atrocious act" on the part of the Russians.\par \par \uc2 "The United States will join (the \uc2 European Union\uc2  ) in sanctioning Putin, Foreign Minister Lavrov, and the rest of Russia's security team," Psaki said,.\par \par \uc2 Washington's sanctions come after the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) announced on Friday the freezing of Putin's and Lavrov's financial assets on European territory.\par \par \uc2 According to the White House spokeswoman, the option of sanctioning Putin has been "on the table" for some time and, in the last 24 hours, U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made the final decision after talks with his European allies.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions against Putin include a ban on travel to the United States, said Psaki, who insisted several times that details would be released later.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:00\par \par \uc2 Former world heavyweight champion boxer and mayor of Kiev assures that "the night will be tough"Wladimir Klitschko, former world boxing champion and now mayor of Kiev, worried about the invasion. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Kiev, Vitali Klitschko, warned Friday that the situation that has been created before the advance of Russian troops towards the Ukrainian capital is "very dangerous" and the night promises to be "hard".\par \par \uc2 "The night and early morning hours are going to be very hard. Russian troops are concentrated near Kiev, law enforcement agencies and our army neutralize subversive groups," the mayor of Kiev said.\par \par \uc2 Klitschko assured that the strategic infrastructure of the city is "well protected" and thanked Kiev residents for enlisting in the territorial defense brigades.\par \par \uc2 This Friday Vitali Klitschko was worried about how the second night in Kiev will be in the face of the invasion. Photo: Reuters\par \par \uc2 "We are forming additional forces to defend the city," he noted. And he addressed a message to the inhabitants of Kiev, where some 3 million people live. He asked to remain alert to the "marks" that the "enemy" can leave on roads and buildings to "adjust fire."\par \par \uc2 "We have confidence in our Armed Forces, in our country and in ourselves!", he concluded.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:52\par \par \uc2 Russia hits back at Britain over seizure of Putin's and Russian foreign minister's accounts."Neither Putin nor Lavrov have accounts in Britain or elsewhere abroad," Moscow Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Maria Zakharova assured on Friday.\par \par \uc2 She did so while commenting on the sanctions announced against Russia's president and foreign minister by the UK, the EU and the U.S. in the wake of the invasion of Ukraine Russian state news agency TASS reported.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:42\par \par \uc2 Russia says Ukraine proposed to address possible start of dialogue on Saturday Maria Zakharova, spokeswoman for the \uc2 Russian Foreign Ministry\uc2  . Photo: EFE/ Sergei Ilnitsky\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian authorities proposed to Russia to talk on Saturday, about possible negotiations between the parties and declined to move forward on that issue on Friday, \uc2 Russian Foreign Ministry\uc2  spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said. "The Ukrainian side refused to negotiate (this Friday). The representatives of the Kiev regime proposed to address that issue