rom the West.\par \par \uc2 Hostomel airport has a long runway capable of accommodating heavy transport aircraft. Its fall would allow Russia to airlift troops directly to the outskirts of Kiev. Hostomel is just 7 kilometers (4 miles) northwest of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  spokesman Maj. Gen. Igor Konashenkov said Friday that Russian airborne forces used 200 helicopters to land at Hostomel.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:35\par \par \uc2 Formula 1 canceled the Sochi Grand Prix over Russia's invasion of Ukraine.An image of the Sochi Grand Prix in 2021. Photo: AP.\par \par \uc2 Formula 1 resolved Friday after a meeting with the \uc2 International Automobile Federation\uc2  (FIA) to cancel the Sochi Grand Prix, which was scheduled for Sept. 25, in the wake of Russia's invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 F1 and the FIA held a meeting with the teams that are carrying out a series of tests at the Montmel\u243\'00\'F3 circuit in Barcelona, with a view to the start of the competition, and it was decided to align with the \uc2 European Union\uc2  in its policy of sanctions and isolation of Russia.\par \par \uc2 "Formula One visits all countries around the world with the positive vision of bringing people together and bringing nations together. We are watching the situation in Ukraine unfold with sadness and shock. We hope for change and a peaceful resolution," the FIA said in an official statement.\par \par \uc2 It added: "We spoke with the FIA, together with the teams, about the position our sport is in and the conclusion is that it is impossible to bring the Russian Grand Prix to change under the current circumstances."\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:21\par \par \uc2 From the \uc2 European Union\uc2  accuse Putin of behaving "like the Nazis".Russian President Vladimir Putin is behaving in Ukraine "like the Nazis" and is on the verge of committing genocide, a spokesman for the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  , Slovak Peter Stano, accused on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Russian leader talks about "preventing a genocide, which makes no sense, because he is committing one or is about to commit one. He talks about 'de-nazifying' Ukraine, but he behaves like the Nazis," the spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 Putin had justified the military offensive against targets in Ukraine with the need to eliminate Nazi-like elements in that country, who were carrying out a genocide against the Russian-speaking population.\par \par \uc2 In the last hours, Ukraine published through its official \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account a caricature of Hitler caressing Putin's face and together with that message it specified that it was not a meme but the reality they were living.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:10\par \par \uc2 Putin assured Xi Jinping that he is ready to negotiate with UkraineVladimir Putin with Chinese President Xi Jinping in Beijing. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 Russian President Vladimir Putin assured Chinese President Xi Jinping during a telephone conversation on Friday that he is ready to hold "high-level negotiations" with Ukraine following the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  he launched in that country.\par \par \uc2 For his part, Xi, quoted by state television CCTV, said he supports Kiev and Moscow"resolving their problems through negotiation", and that his country "respects the sovereignty and territorial integrity of states", although he emphasized that "it is important to respect the legitimate security concerns of all countries involved".\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:00\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis went to the Russian embassy to the Vatican Francis next to Putin at an audience they held in 2015. Photo: AP.\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis visited the Russian embassy to the Vatican on Friday to express to Alexander Avdeev his concern over the attack on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Francis' gesture as he left the Vatican to visit the nearby Russian embassy, which is located on Via della Conciliazone, is part of the Holy See's attempt to call for dialogue and a return to the negotiating table.\par \par \uc2 Adveed works to prepare for the second meeting between Francis and Russian Orthodox Church Patriarch Kirill and keeps Francis constantly informed about the conflict in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:53\par \par \uc2 "Let's sit down to negotiate", the Ukrainian president's request to Putin.Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Photo: Reuter.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday asked his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin to sit down at the negotiating table to stop the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched the day before against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "I want to address once again the president of Russia. All over the territory of Ukraine there is fighting. Let's sit down at the negotiating table to stop the death of human beings," he said in a televised message.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:41\par \par \uc2 Maria Laura Avignolo\par \par \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war: an awkward situation for China, Vladimir Putin's key allyIsabel Hilton, CEO of China Dialogue and specialist on North Korea and China.\par \par \uc2 In Russia's invasion of Ukraine, the world is also looking to China. Xi Jinping's government declined to identify it as an "invasion" but called for "containment" to prevent the crisis from spiraling "out of control."\par \par \uc2 China-Russia relations are the best in 70 years. President Xi Jinping called Vladimir Putin "my best friend" when he opened, in his presence, the Winter Olympic Games in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 But it is obligatory to ask: did Russian President Vladimir Putin inform his best friend Xi Jinping of his intentions to invade Ukraine or threaten the West with a nuclear attack if he is removed from the system from which he benefited until before the sanctions?\par \par \uc2 Appearances indicate that China was surprised by this military offensive to invade Ukraine. It probably did not know that its action would sweep away Ukrainian sovereignty, which Beijing defended at the Munich Security Summit days earlier.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Isabel Hilton is a China specialist. There she studied and speaks fluent Mandarin and its dialects. Founder and CEO of China Dialogue, she is a journalist and visiting professor at the Lau Institute of King's College London. This was her dialogue with Clar\u237\'00\'EDn from London on China's role in this crisis. Read the full article here.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:27\par \par \uc2 Italy prepares for a possible energy crisis due to the warItalian Prime Minister Mario Draghi in parliament. Photo: EFE\par \par \uc2 Italian Prime Minister Mario Draghi announced Friday that his government is working to cope with a possible energy crisis after Russia's attack on Ukraine that even the reopening of coal-fired power plants is being studied.\par \par \uc2 "We hope that these plans will not be necessary, but we cannot be caught off guard," he warned while appearing in Parliament.\par \par \uc2 He further advanced that the emergency measures under consideration "include greater flexibility in gas consumption, suspensions in the industrial sector and rules on gas consumption in the thermoelectric sector, where there are also reduction measures."\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:07\par \par \uc2 More than 1,800 detained in anti-war protests in RussiaMore than 1,800 people have been arbitrarily detained in Russia during protests against the war launched by the Russian government in Ukraine and it is unknown whether some have been released, the \uc2 UN Human Rights Office\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 This is three times the number reported by the Main Directorate of the \uc2 Russian Interior Ministry\uc2  in recent hours.\par \par \uc2 "Being arrested for exercising the right to freedom of expression or assembly is an arbitrary deprivation of liberty and we call for the individuals concerned to be released," Human Rights Office spokeswoman Ravina Shamdasan said in Geneva\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:48\par \par \uc2 Marcelo Cantelmi\par \par \uc2 Opinion: Vladimir Putin in the time tunnel, threw the world into the pastA man looks at the wreckage of a downed military plane in Kiev. Photo EFE.\par \par \uc2 One criticism of today's China is that it has ignored a key command of the legendary Deng Xiao Ping founder of the modern and economically successful People's Republic.\par \par \uc2 That advice, in an almost poetic format and with tones of Machiavelli to the prince, recommended: "Face problems calmly, hide your abilities, buy time, never claim a position of leadership, lower your profile". That is how it should be, he warned, because there, in front of the wall "foreign troops are camped, stronger than ours". Read more.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:41\par \par \uc2 URGENT - Russia assures that it is ready to negotiate "if Ukraine lays down its arms". "We are ready to negotiate at any time, as soon as the Ukrainian armed forces hear our call and lay down their arms," Lavrov said at a press conference, a day after the start of the Russian offensive in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:28\par \par \uc2 Champions League: because of the war, the final will not be played in Russia and will be played on May 28 in ParisImage of the stadium in Paris where the Champions League final will be played. Photo AFP.\par \par \uc2 The Stade de France in Paris will host the Champions League final on May 28 instead of St. Petersburg, announced Friday \uc2 UEFA\uc2  , which has withdrawn the organization to this city in reaction to the invasion of Ukraine by the Russian army.\par \par \uc2 The stadium on the outskirts of Paris already hosted the Champions League final in 2006, in which Barcelona defeated Arsenal. Read more.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:13\par \par \uc2 R