ncrete action," Zelenski stressed\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:21\par \par \uc2 Paula Lugones\par \par \uc2 Do economic sanctions work to stop Putin?Threats were not enough to stop the Kremlin leader's offensive. Will punishments do it?\par \par \uc2 U.S. President Joe Biden on Thursday charged again with very tough language against Russian leader Vladimir Putin and launched a new package of sanctions, but it fell short of what many experts expected.\par \par \uc2 Biden limited Moscow's ability to do business in dollars, euros and yen; blocked four more Russian banks; froze the assets and \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other officials in the Kremlin's entourage; and cut U.S. technology exports to Russia. "Putin chose this war: he and his country will suffer the consequences," the president warned.\par \par \uc2 However, he did not expel Russia from the Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial Telecommunication known as SWIFT. Removing it from that international banking network would mean blocking it from all trade.In this analysis Clar\u237\'00\'EDn tells you why.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:05\par \par \uc2 Accident in war: Soviet military plane crashes in RussiaA Russian Antonov AN-26 military transport plane crashed in western Russia near the Ukrainian border, the Kremlin's Defense Ministry confirmed, adding that the people on board, whose number is unknown, died.The plane "crashed in the Voronezh region during an equipment transport mission" and "the crew died," local military authorities quoted by the Russian press said, evoking a technical failure.An official spokesman confirmed the incident, without giving details. The Soviet-made Antonov AN-26 can carry up to forty soldiers or several tons of equipment.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:13\par \par \uc2 Ukraine decrees general mobilization and summons every adult to "serve in the army"Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky signed a decree calling for 