ops took control of Antonov International Airport in Hostomel, about 40 kilometers from Kiev, CNN said.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 11:16\par \par \uc2 Russia says it destroyed 74 Ukrainian military facilities, including 11 airfields?The Russian military said Thursday it destroyed 74 military facilities in Ukraine, including 11 airfields, as part of an early morning Moscow-ordered attack.\par \par \uc2 "Following air strikes by the Russian armed forces, 74 ground military facilities were knocked out of service. This includes 11 airfields of the air force," Russian Defense Ministry spokesman Gen. Igor Konashenkov announced on television.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 11:08\par \par \uc2 There is fighting at an airport 30 kilometers from KievRussia is attacking Ukraine on several fronts, from the north, east and south of the country, Ukrainian presidential adviser Mykhailo Podolya said today, specifying that heavy fighting is underway at Hostomel airport, some 30 kilometers northwest of Kiev. "Our army repels the attacks and the enemy suffers significant losses," Podolya added.According to the president's adviser Volodomir Zelensky, "the main thing now is to concentrate as much as possible on the defense of the country and on maintaining normality for the people."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:49\par \par \uc2 Russia: sanctions for those who march against war in Ukraine?Russian authorities on Thursday threatened to crack down on any "unauthorized" anti-war demonstrations in Ukraine, where it launched a wide-ranging military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few hours ago.\par \par \uc2 The Interior Ministry, the Prosecutor's Office and the Russian Investigative Committee warned its population against any protest actions. The Committee noted that people who take part in rallies on "the tense situation in foreign policy" or in clashes, expose themselves to prosecution.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:38\par \par