n\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:07\par \par \uc2 Russia says invasion met with no resistance on the borders The Russian Defense Ministry stated that the Ukrainian Armed Forces' anti-aircraft defense facilities "are suppressed" and the military infrastructure of its air bases "is disabled".\par \par \uc2 Moreover, as reported by the Russian RT channel, Ukrainian border guards do not put up any resistance to the Russian troops, stated from the Ministry.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:46\par \par \uc2 NATO allies invoke Article 4 after feeling threatened."Russian soldiers leave Ukraine," the sign of a protester at the Brandenburg Gate in Berlin. (AFP Photo)\par \par \uc2 The North Atlantic Council, NATO's highest decision-making body, held a meeting Thursday under Article 4 of the alliance, which is triggered when one of the member countries feels threatened.\par \par \uc2 The move followed Russia's invasion of Ukraine early Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 Today we have held consultations under Article 4 of the Washington Treaty. We have decided, in accordance with our defensive planning to protect all Allies, to take additional measures to further strengthen deterrence and defense throughout the Alliance. Our measures are and will continue to be pre-emptive, proportionate, but not escalatory,? the North Atlantic Council said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:43\par \par \uc2 Pro-Russian militias in Donetsk and Luhansk launch counter-offensive, Moscow saysMilitias of the self-proclaimed Donetsk and Lugansk People's Republics have launched a counteroffensive against Ukrainian forces with the support of Russian Army units, the Russian Defense Ministry reported today.\par \par \uc2 "The people's militias (...) are currently conducting a counteroffensive with the support of the Russian armed forces," Defense spokesman Igor Konashenkov said.\par \par \uc2 He assured that the counteroffensive "broke the first