d the town of Shchastia in the Lugansk region, and annihilated fifty Russian soldiers.\par \par \uc2 "Shchastia was recaptured after the attack of the Russian aggressor. During the attempted attack enemy equipment was destroyed and about 50 enemies were killed," the entity announced on its Facebook account.\par \par \uc2 For its part, the Russian Defense Ministry assured that the country's Armed Forces are not attacking Ukrainian cities in the course of the "special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " launched by President Vladimir Putin.\par \par \uc2 "The Russian Armed Forces are not attacking Ukrainian cities. There is no threat to the peaceful population," Defense said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:07\par \par \uc2 The first videos of Russia's attacks on Ukraine.24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:05\par \par \uc2 More international condemnation of the attack on Ukraine: "Russia will pay a heavy price".This was stated by Irish Prime Minister Miche\u225\'00\'E1l Martin, who called the "attack" launched by Russia against "the sovereign people" of Ukraine "unjustifiable" and warned that there will be consequences for Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "Russia will pay a heavy price for this outrageous act of aggression. We stand with Ukraine," the head of the Dublin government said in a brief statement.\par \par \uc2 Martin assured that his country will work with its partners in the European Union (EU) and the UN - where it is a non-permanent member of the security council - to ensure that "President Putin and his regime are held accountable" for their actions.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 07:01\par \par \uc2 Sirens in Kiev after the Russian attack 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 06:46\par \par \uc2 The aftermath of the shelling in Mariupol.A radar and some destroyed vehicles in the Ukrainian military regiments in Mariupol. Photo AP\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin announced early Thursday morning (Argentine time) a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine. (AP Photo)\par \par \uc2 The attack on Mariupol, Donetsk region, left one dead and two wounded. (AP Photo)\par \par \uc2 Ukraine reports at least eight dead and a dozen wounded in the first hours of the Russian invasion of the country. (AP Photo)\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 06:46\par \par \uc2 Ukraine breaks off diplomatic relations with RussiaUkrainian President Volodymir Zelensky announced today that his country is severing diplomatic relations with Russia following the military aggression against Ukrainian territory ordered by the head of the Kremlin, Vladimir Putin\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 06:10\par \par \uc2 Kosovo condemned the Russian attackKosovo President Vjosa Osmani condemned Russia's aggression against Ukraine and expressed her country's support for Ukraine and its people, who "face the consequences of a war they did not provoke."\par \par \uc2 "We will cooperate with our allies to stop any destabilization in our region. Russia's hegemony will not succeed. Freedom and democracy will prevail," Osmani said on Twitter.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 05:58\par \par \uc2 Ukraine denounced the entry of Russian tanksThe Ukrainian Interior Ministry denounced the entry of several rows of Russian tanks into the area of the Kiev-controlled Lugansk region in the east of the country.\par \par \uc2 "Columns of Russian tanks entered the Lugansk region near the villages of Krasna Talivka, Milove, Horodysche," the Ministry reported on its Facebook page.\par \par \uc2 The advance of these units is resisted by the Border Guard Service, the Armed Forces and the National Guard of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 05:48\par \par \uc2 First fatalities reportedUkraine reported that at least eight people were killed and a dozen injured, in the first hours of the Russian invasion of the country.\par \par \uc2 "A woman and a child were injured in the Konopot region, where a car burned. In the city of Podolsk of the Odessa region, seven dead, seven wounded and 19 missing as a result of shelling. In the city of Mariupol, Donetsk region, one dead and two wounded," Ukrainian Interior Ministry advisor Anton Guersaschenko detailed on his Telegram channel.\par \par \uc2 Guersaschenko added that in Mykolaiv district, northeast of Odessa, one person was wounded during an attack on a military airfield, while in Semykhatky, Kherson district, a 17-year-old was killed.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 05:41\par \par \uc2 Germany urged its citizens to leave "through safe channels". The German government urged its citizens to leave Ukraine "through safe channels" as soon as possible in the face of Russian attacks, while informing that the embassy in Kiev has been "temporarily closed".\par \par \uc2 Those who do not have the possibility to leave the country under these conditions, "should get to safety somewhere safe", urged the German Foreign Ministry, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 05:23\par \par \uc2 Empty airspace over Ukraine and western RussiaAirspace is mostly empty over Ukraine and western Russia, with aircraft in the area avoiding border regions, according to images the flight tracking service Flightradar24.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Thursday, Ukrainian aviation authorities issued an advisory restricting the country's airspace, covering regions around Kyiv, Dnipro, Lviv, Odessa and Simferopol.\par \par \uc2 European aviation regulators also warned that any civilian aircraft near the Ukrainian border could face a "high risk" of being attacked.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 04:06\par \par \uc2 The US embassy in Kiev recommended Americans to "shelter in place."Russian tanks entered Ukraine from the east after Putin's announcement. Photo: REUTERS/Carlos Barria\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Embassy in Kiev issued a warning for Americans in Ukraine to "shelter in place" due to Russian attacks on several major Ukrainian cities.\par 