y" to the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced by Vladimir Putin over eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "I am appalled by the horrific events in Ukraine and have spoken to President Zelenskyy to discuss next steps," the premier relayed via his Twitter account.\par \par \uc2 In the message he added: "President Putin has chosen a path of bloodshed and destruction by launching this unprovoked attack on Ukraine. The UK and our allies will respond decisively."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:26\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president held talks with Joe Biden and Boris Johnson.Ukrainian President , Volodymyr Zelensky, held a telephone conversation with his U.S. peer, Joe Biden, after Vladimir Putin announced the start of a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Zelensky also had a telephone contact with British Prime Minister Boris Johnson.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy communicated by telephone with his U.S. counterpart, Joe Biden. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:12\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president imposed martial law over Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 operationUkrainian\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Volodymir Zelensky on Thursday imposed martial law across the country following the start of a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Russia.\par \par \uc2 "We are imposing martial law on the whole territory of our country. A minute ago I had a conversation with President Biden. The US has already begun to rally international support," he said.\par \par \uc2 Zelenski conveyed to Ukrainians: "Today each of you should remain calm. Stay at home if you can. We are working. The army is working. The entire defense and security sector is working."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:05\par \par \uc2 The price of a barrel of oil rose and surpassed US$100 after Russia's attack on UkraineThe price of a barrel of oil surpassed US$100 for the first time in more than seven years, following the start of Russia's military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine. In addition, the Tokyo Stock Exchange falls more than 2%.\par \par \uc2 According to information from AFP Agency, the barrel of Brent crude oil reached U$S100.04 after the announcement, which intensified fears of a large-scale conflict in Eastern Europe; while WTI oil traded at U$S95.54.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's ambassador to the UN: "Russia declared war".Ukrainian Ambassador to the United Nations Sergiy Kyslytsya stated before the Security Council that Russian President Vladimir Putin "has declared war on Ukraine''. He also pressed his Russian counterpart to declare that Russia will not shell or use artillery against Ukrainian cities.\par \par \uc2 Kyslytsya noted Wednesday night that if Russian Ambassador Vassily Nebenzia was not in a position to give an affirmative answer he should resign from the presidency of the Security Council, which Russia is chairing this month.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Ambassador to the UN Sergiy Kyslytsya during a press conference after a meeting of the United Nations Security Council convened to discuss the ongoing crisis in Ukraine. Photo: REUTERS\par \par \uc2 Subsequently, the Ukrainian called for a new emergency meeting of the Security Council and called on the body to "stop the war because it is too late to talk about reducing tensions'' Shortly afterwards, Kyslytsya asked whether he should play the video in which Putin announces the start of military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Nebenzia replied, ''This is not called war. It is called a special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Donbas''.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:43\par \par \uc2 NATO: "Reckless and unprovoked attack".Stoltenberg considered it "a serious violation of international law", Photo: JOHN THYS / AFP\par \par \uc2 NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg condemned Russia's "reckless and unprovoked attack" on Ukraine and warned that it put "countless" lives at risk.\par \par \uc2 "Once again, despite our repeated warnings and tireless efforts to engage in diplomacy, Russia has chosen the path of aggression against an independent and sovereign country," the diplomat added in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Stoltenberg considered this "a serious violation of international law and a grave threat to Euro-Atlantic security" and announced a meeting of NATO allies to address the "consequences of Russia's aggressive actions."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:33\par \par \uc2 For Ukraine, it is a "war of aggression".The Ukrainian Foreign Minister stressed that Russian President Vladimir Putin launched "a full-scale invasion" on his country, stressed that "peaceful cities are being attacked" and considered, finally, that it is "a war of aggression".\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:16\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden will give definitions on Russia's military action in DonbassU.S. President Joe Biden announced that during this Thursday afternoon he will give definitions on Russia's decision to take military action in the Donbass region of eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 White House spokesmen quoted by CNN indicated that Biden will announce "further consequences that the United States and our allies and partners will impose on Russia for its unprovoked and unjustified attack on Ukraine."\par \par \uc2 Shortly after Russian President Vladimir Putin announced the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Thursday morning, Biden issued a statement denouncing Putin's choice as "a premeditated war that will bring catastrophic loss of life and human suffering."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:11\par \par \uc2 From the Ukrainian government they say that "the invasion has begun".Advisor to the Ukrainian Interior Minister Anton Gerashchenko confirmed this Thursday morning that the "invasion of Russia has begun", with "missile attacks on Kiev".\par \par \uc2 Gerashchenko added on his Facebook page that control centers, such as airfields and military headquarters, are being hit by shelling in Kyiv and Kharkiv, and that there is artillery fire along the border.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:02\par \par \uc2 Russian ambassador to the UN defended the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in UkraineRussian Ambassador to the United Nations Vasily Alekseevich Nebenzya defended President Vladimir Putin's decision to take military action in the Donbass region of eastern Ukraine during an emergency meeting of the UN Security Council.\par \par \uc2 "The root of the current crisis around Ukraine is the actions of Ukraine itself, which for many years sabotaged its obligations under the (Minsk agreement)," Nebenzya said. He said the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at protecting residents in the pro-Moscow separatist regions of eastern Ukraine, "who for eight years have been in fear of Ukrainian shelling."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:48\par \par \uc2 The House of Banca condemned the Russian attack on UkraineIn a press release reported that President Joe Biden is monitoring the situation unfolding in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Biden condemned the attack and called it "unjustified and unprovoked". He also promised to hold Russia "accountable". ?\par \par \uc2 He also expressed, "The prayers of the whole world are with the people of Ukraine."\par \par \uc2 "President Putin has chosen a premeditated war that will bring catastrophic loss of life and human suffering," he said.\par \par \uc2 President Joe Biden assured that the world will hold Russia accountable. Photo: REUTERS\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:24\par \par \uc2 Putin tells Ukrainian forces to lay down their weapons and go homeIn a speech given early Thursday morning broadcast on national television, Russian President Vl