\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war, live: Putin puts Russia's nuclear deterrent on alert\b0\par\par\uc2 36,470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 LIVE News inDevelopmentRussian President Vladimir Putin ordered today that Russia's nuclear deterrent forces be put on alert, in the midst of the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Moscow announced that it was sending a delegation to Belarus to begin a round of negotiations with Ukraine, but the Ukrainian President, Volodymir Zelenski, rejected dialogue in that country, considering it an accomplice of the Russian aggression\par \par \uc2 . In another step in the strategy at the \uc2 United Nations\uc2  , the Ukrainian government confirmed this Sunday that it denounced Russia before the \uc2 International Criminal Court\uc2  in The Hague\par \par \uc2 .27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:50\par \par \uc2 Kiev confirmed that it will send a delegation to negotiate with Russia on the Ukrainian-Belarusian borderThiswasreported by the office of Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky. "We agreed that the Ukrainian delegation would meet with the Russian delegation without preconditions on the Ukrainian-Belarusian border near the Pripiat River," according to the official Telegram channel of the Ukrainian leader\par \par \uc2 .27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:37\par \par \uc2 Putin puts Russian nuclear deterrent forces on alert, AP reports At a meeting, he ordered his defense minister and the head of the Russian Armed Forces to put Russian nuclear deterrent forces "on special combat alert."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:24\par \par \uc2 Moscow claims that Kiev confirmed sending representatives to Belarus to negotiateThis was reported by the head of the Russian delegation, Vladimir Medinsky, to the Russian agency TASS "At around 15 (local time, 11 Argentina time) we received confirmation that the negotiations will be held in the Gomel region, as we had suggested," Medinsky said. Kiev has not yet confirmed the information.\par \par \uc2 Hours earlier, it was Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky himself who had refused to participate in the agreements\par \par \uc2 ? According to the Belarusian official agency Belta, the negotiations are scheduled to take place "in the Gomel region, on the Belarusian-Ukrainian border".\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 10:02\par \par \uc2 More sanctions against Russia: Putin loses honorary judo positionDueto the attacks on Ukraine, Vladimir Putin temporarily lost his highest official position in Judo. The International Federation took this Sunday the decision to remove him from the status of honorary president of the body.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president is an avid judo player and attended the discipline's events at the 2012 Olympics.\par \par \uc2 The judo federation is one of the few Olympic bodies that referred to the Russian invasion of Ukraine as "war''. Other bodies have used phrases such as "escalation in the conflict''\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:56\par \par \uc2 Governor of Kharkov, Ukraine's second city, says he maintains control in face of Russian incursionUkraine's second city of Kharkov is under control of Ukrainian forces, Governor Oleg Sinegubov said Sunday, a few hours after fighting intensified in the city\par \par \uc2 . "Kharkov is fully under our control," Sinegubov wrote on social networks, assuring that "elimination of enemies in the city" was\par \par \uc2 underway. Accordingto him, "the Russian enemy is completely demoralized," leaving their vehicles abandoned, and even, he claimed, groups of Russian soldiers "surrender to the Ukrainian army."\par \par \uc2 Kharkov, with a population of 1.4 million, is the main city in northeastern Ukraine and is close to the border with Russia and the territories under the control of pro-Russian separatists, Donetsk and Lugansk.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:19\par \par \uc2 "Silence the guns," Pope Francis' plea for peaceThePope, at his Angelus on Sunday. (AP)\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis today called for an end to the war in Ukraine and recalled that "ordinary people are the real victims" of armed conflicts, while calling on the international community to open "humanitarian corridors" for people fleeing the European country after the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 "In these days we have been upset by a tragic thing, war. Many times we prayed so that this path would not be invoked, and we did not stop talking, we begged God intensely," the pontiff said while praying the traditional Sunday Angelus from the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 "I am heartbroken by what is happening in Ukraine and in other parts of the world", "silence the weapons, God is with the peacemakers, not with those who use violence," he said\par \par \uc2 . 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:13\par \par \uc2 Ukraine sues Russia at the International Court in The HagueIt was announced by President Volodimir Zelensky through his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account. He also called for "celerity" to the Dutch court. The full note.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:11\par \par \uc2 The number of refugees fleeing Ukraine reaches 368 thousand people, according to UNHCR Ukrainian refugees arrive in Przemysl, Poland, on Sunday. (AP)\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:11\par \par \uc2 Belgium, Finland and Denmark close their airspace to Russian aircraftIt was announced on Sunday morning by authorities of the three countries. The Danish foreign minister also announced that they will push for a ban throughout the \uc2 European Union\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 09:10\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president refuses to hold talks with Russia in BelarusThe Russian government sent a delegation to Belarus, ostensibly to hold talks with Ukraine in search of an agreement that would allow for a cessation of hostilities\par \par \uc2 . However, Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski rejected the offer and said that talks in Minsk might have been possible if Russia had not attacked Ukraine from Belarusian territory\par \par \uc2 .However, the leader left the door open for negotiations in another country.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 04:49\par \par \uc2 Ukraine calls for an emergency special session of the UN General AssemblyUkrainecalled for an emergency special session of the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2  in the face of the crisis generated by the Russian invasion, Ukraine's Permanent Representative to the UN Sergiy Kyslytsya said\par \par \uc2 ."In light of Russia's veto in the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  , I have called on the Council members to take the necessary decision to convene an emergency special session of the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2  , as Russia did not allow the Council to act as required to maintain international peace and security," Kyslytsya tweeted on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 04:37\par \par \uc2 Russian delegation arrived in Belarus to start talks with UkrainiansARussian delegation arrived in Belarus to start talks with Ukrainians in search of a peace agreement, Russian Federation President's press secretary Dmitry Peskov said Sunday\par \par \uc2 . "The Russian delegation, consisting of representatives of the Foreign Ministry, the Defense Ministry and other departments, including the presidential administration, arrived in Belarus to negotiate with the Ukrainians. We will be ready to start these negotiations in Gomel," Peskov told reporters.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 03:45\par \par \uc2 Russia surrounds two major cities in southern UkraineTheRussian military claimed on Sunday to have surrounded two major cities in southern Ukraine, Kherson and Berdiansk, on the fourth day of the invasion of Ukraine ordered by its President Vladimir Putin\par \par \uc2 ."In the past 24 hours, Russian armed forces completely blockaded the cities of Kherson and Berdiansk," with 290,000 and 110,000 inhabitants respectively, the \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin troops had also entered Kharkov, a city located some 20 kilometers south of the Russian border where fighting was taking place in the streets, in the early hours of Sunday.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 03:13\par \par \uc2 Russian troops entered Kharkov, the second largest Ukrainian cityThe head of the Kharkov regional administration, Oleg Sinegubov, reported Sunday that light military vehicles had "stormed into the city."\par \par \uc2 Before his statements, images appeared showing some Russian military cars driving through the streets of the northeastern city.\par \par \uc2 Sinegubov urged residents to stay in bunkers, saying that Russian troops appeared to be in the city center\par \par \uc2 ."Do not leave the shelters! The Armed Forces of Ukraine are eliminating the enemy. Civilians are asked not to go out on the streets," he broadcast.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:43\par \par \uc2 Susana Malcorra criticized the Government's position and called for a firm rejection of the RussianinvasionFormer Argentine Foreign Minister Susana Malcorra said that the Government has no alternative but to reject the Russian invasion of Ukraine. Photo:\par \par \uc2 EFEFormer Foreign Minister Susana Malcorra questioned the Government's oscillating position in the face of the crisis generated by the Russian invasion of Ukraine and warned that Argentina has no alternative but to "reject" the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  promoted by President Vladimir Putin\par \par \uc2 ."Argentina has no other alternative but to clearly define itself with respect to the horror that this invasion represents\par \par \uc2 ", asserted the former Minister of Foreign Affairs of Mauricio Macri when consulted on the varied position of Alberto Fernandez's government regarding the war in Ukraine.In declarations to CNN in Spanish, Malcorra stressed that the Argentine Executive should declare "the rejection of this invasion\par \par \uc2 and the immediate request for a ceasefire and the withdrawal of Russian troops". "Aca hay un tema de principios de la Carta de Naciones Unidas que Argentina ha jugado un rol fundamental alineado con esa carta", fundament\u243\'00\'F3. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.clarin.com/politica/guerra-rusia-ucrania-susana-malcorra-critico-posicion-gobierno-pidio-rechazo-firme-invasion-vladimir-putin_0_sWiRAdTEBC.html27.02.2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.clarin.com/politica/guerra-rusia-ucrania-susana-malcorra-critico-posicion-gobierno-pidio-rechazo-firme-invasion-vladimir-putin_0_sWiRAdTEBC.html27.02.2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 02:40\par \par \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador dijo que sacar\u225\'00\'E1 a todos los mexicanos de UcraniaThePresident of Mexico, Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador, affirmed that no Mexican citizen will remain in the conflict zone between Ukraine and Russia, as his government is working in collaboration with other countries to rescue them\par \par \uc2 ."No Mexican is going to stay in the conflict zone, we are going to get them all out. Governments are helping us, diplomats and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs are helping us", said the President to journalists, during a working tour in the state of Nayarit.\par \par \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador informed that his government was carrying out the procedures and permits "to use the airspace of different countries", in an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  coordinated by the Mexican Air Force. The president did not specify the total number of Mexicans who are in Ukraine, nor how many of them would be repatriated.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:10\par \par \uc2 Six civilians killed in OkhtyrkaThegovernor of Sumy, Dmitry Zhivitsky, revealed Sunday that at least six Ukrainian citizens were killed during a Russian attack on Friday in the town of Okhtyrka, in northwestern Ukraine. Among the fatalities was a seven-year-old girl.\par \par \uc2 As reported by the BBC, "a kindergarten and an orphanage were among the reported targets, which Russia has denied."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:53\par \par \uc2 Ukraine reaffirms its resistanceTheGeneral Staff of the Armed Forces of Ukraine published on Sunday a "guide for the resistance movement", in which it reaffirms concepts to its fighting forces with the aim of diminishing the chances of the Russian army, which continues with its plan to advance towards Kiev, the country's capital\par \par \uc2 .In its social networks, the Ukrainian governmental organization urged its troops to concentrate on the "destruction and dismantling of the enemy's management system and the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its rear".\par \par \uc2 Among the main actions it suggested were "carefully dismantling or drawing road signs, names of settlements to confuse the enemy," being "creative" and "using other engineering skills and tricks," and "destroying key nodes of transport infrastructure," among others.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian forces were holding their positions early this morning and fighting was going on in "the same places as three days ago," Ukrainian Presidential Advisor Mikhail Podoliak said.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:17\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's change of position At the annual congress of conservatives, Trump highlighted the figure of the Ukrainian president. Photo: REUTERS/Octavio JonesDays\par \par \uc2 after praising Vladimir Putin, and considering him "a genius", former US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  considered that the Russian invasion of Ukraine "should never have happened" and that it could lead to a "world war"\par \par \uc2 ."It's a horrible thing. It should never have happened, under any circumstances, and it is what it is," Trump said about the crisis in Ukraine, while highlighting "the great courage" and the "great work" developed by the citizens of that nation in the framework of their resistance to the Russian offensive.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Fox News in Florida after participating in the annual congress of the conservative CPAC, Trump added that "this can lead to (involving) many other countries and a world war".\par \par \uc2 During the conference in Orlando, the former president, who called his successor, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  , "weak and incompetent", praised Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski as a "brave man".\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:50\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Prime Minister, thanked measures of Western "friends "UkrainianPrime Minister Denys Shmyhal thanked the United States, France, Germany, Italy, Canada and Great Britain for the measures taken against Russia in the framework of the offensive deployed by the Kremlin in different parts of the country, with the aim of reaching Kiev\par \par \uc2 .In a publication he made on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  , the official acknowledged these countries for the "removal of several Russian banks from SWIFT", the "freezing of the assets of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2  " and the "ban on Russian oligarchs using their financial assets on Euro-Atlantic markets".\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:36\par \par \uc2 Warns of possible environmental disasterThehead of the Kiev Regional State Administration, Oleksiy Kuleba, warned that Ukraine faces "an environmental disaster", after Russia executed a missile attack on a fuel depot located in Vasilkov, on the outskirts of Kiev\par \par \uc2 ."The fighting over the airport continues. Russian troops have launched a missile attack on the oil base. A huge fire broke out, which can be seen even from Kiev. The fighting does not stop," the official posted on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , where he added that "currently managed to shut off the gas supply" by way of prevention of further disasters.\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:14\par \par \uc2 For Britain, Russia not advancing aspredictedRussian forces in Ukraine "are not making the progress they planned," the \uc2 British Ministry of Defense\uc2  said in a brief intelligence update on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  , which is consistent with Pentagon observations.\par \par \uc2 Britain highlighted Ukrainian "strong resistance."\par \par \uc2 Photo: AP Photo/Efrem Lukatsky\par \par \uc2 ? "They face logistical problems and strong resistance from the Ukrainians," the note continues, where they confirmed that the Russians "have suffered losses and some have been taken prisoner."\par \par \uc2 The London ministry also confirms that the Russian government has restricted access to several social networks "in an attempt to hide details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine from its own population."\par \par \uc2 27.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:00\par \par \uc2 Attacks and deaths in Kharkov and KievThenine-story building that was hit by a Russian missile. A civilian woman was killed there. Photo: State Emergency Service of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 A nine-story building in Kharkov, Ukraine's second largest city, was hit by a Russian missile and one woman was killed and 20 other people were evacuated, Ukraine's state emergency service confirmed.\par \par \uc2 Another 60 residents of the building had taken shelter in the basement and none were injured, but were evacuated after the impact.\par \par \uc2 Separately, according to CNN, a six-year-old boy was killed and several people were injured amid heavy fighting in a western district of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Serhii Chernysuk, a doctor at Kyiv's Okhmatdyt hospital, said that among the wounded were two teenagers and three adults.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:16\par \par \uc2 UN reported 240 civilians casualties in Russian attacks on Ukraine United Nations confirmed at least 240 civilian casualties, including the death of at least 64 people\par \par \uc2 , in fighting in Ukraine that erupted since Russia's invasion on Thursday. The "actual figures are believed to be considerably higher'' because many of the casualty reports have not yet been confirmed.The \uc2 UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs\uc2  (OCHA) released the count Saturday night from the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights (UNHCHR), which has strict methodologies and verification procedures on losses from the conflict.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:00\par \par \uc2 Germany closes airspace to RussiaTheGerman government closed airspace to Russia as part of sanctions imposed from the invasion of Ukraine, German Transport Minister Volker Wissing said\par \par \uc2 .German airline \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  will also immediately avoid Russian airspace due to the war, a \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  spokeswoman announced Saturday. The airline said it will no longer operate services to Russian destinations.\par \par \uc2 All flights to and from Russia were suspended as of Saturday for the next seven days.\par \par \uc2 26.02.202222:45\par \par \uc2 Tense calm in early morning in Kiev as Russian siege continuesIt's past 3 a.m. Sunday morning in Ukraine and there is a tense atmosphere in Kiev after residents were warned of possible shelling.\par \par \uc2 Following the attack on an oil terminal some 40 km south of Kiev, so far no explosions have been reported in the Ukrainian capital, which has suffered some shelling in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Russia's ground advance on Kiev appears to be stalled at the city limits amid concerted Ukrainian resistance.\par \par \uc2 However many expect an air strike and people take refuge in subway bunkers.\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian soldier walks past the debris of a burning military truck on a street in Kiev, Ukraine. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:27\par \par \uc2 From Ukraine believe that the Snake Island border guards are alive and are prisonersThe border guards of the Snake Island in the Black Sea, which was seized by Russian forces, may still be alive, according to a statement issued Saturday by the State Border Guard Service of Ukraine (SBGSU).\par \par \uc2 "We firmly believe that all Ukrainian defenders of Snake Island may still be alive," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Both President Zelensky and official agencies had said on Friday that all the soldiers had died following the capture of the small island by Russian forces .\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:11\par \par \uc2 Russia denounces "unprecedented cyber attack" on institutional websitesRussia confirmed today that institutional websites, with the Kremlin's in the lead, suffered an "unprecedented computer attack" that was "successfully" repelled in most cases.\par \par \uc2 "The Ministry of Digital Transformation is facing an unprecedented scale of cyber-attacks. More than 50 DDoS attacks with a capacity of more than 1 TB were recorded on February 26, as well as a series of professional attacks targeting the utility portal," a statement said.\par \par \uc2 "All attacks were successfully repelled by specialists of the security center," the authorities added, according to Europa Press agency.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:41\par \par \uc2 Gas pipeline in flames after Russian shellingThe pictures, showing the flames after the shelling of a gas pipeline in Kharkov, were made by the Ukrainian State Special Communications Service.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:18\par \par \uc2 Kremlin retaliation: Russia closes airspace to four countries Russia decided on Saturday to close its airspace to companies linked to or registered in Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Slovenia, in retaliation to similar measures taken by these countries.\par \par \uc2 The ban also concerns transit flights carried out in Russia by the same companies, the Russian civil aviation agency \uc2 Rosaviatsia\uc2  announced in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "Due to hostile decisions of the aviation authorities of Latvia, Lithuania, Slovenia and Estonia, the airlines of these states and/or those registered in them are subject to restrictions on flights to points on the territory of the Russian Federation, including transit flights through the airspace of the Russian Federation," the text specifies.\par \par \uc2 It concludes, "This decision was taken in accordance with the norms of international law in response to the ban on all civilian flights of aircraft operated by Russian and/or Russian-registered airlines to/from the territory of these states."\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:01\par \par \uc2 Shocking flames on a gas pipeline shelled by the Russian military 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:42\par \par \uc2 From the U.S. say that with the new sanctions Russia will be "a global economic and financial pariah"The new sanctions that the \uc2 European Union\uc2  , the United States and Canada announced Saturday for Russia for invading Ukraine turned the country ruled by Vladimir Putin into a financial "pariah", a senior US official assured.\par \par \uc2 "Russia has become a global economic and financial pariah," he said, and now its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "cannot support the ruble (its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )."\par \par \uc2 He insisted that only Putin can decide how much additional cost he is willing to bear," and added that a task force "will go after" the "yachts, jets, luxury cars and luxury homes" of Russian oligarchs.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:26\par \par \uc2 A powerful explosion lit up the sky over Kiev A powerful explosion lit up the sky over Kiev in the early hours of Sunday morning. Initial reports indicate that it was a Russian bombing about 20 kilometers from the capital.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:05\par \par \uc2 Cuba blames US and NATO for Russia's invasion of UkraineCuba on Saturday held the United States and NATO responsible for Russia's invasion and attack on Ukraine by pointing out that "the progressive expansion" of those countries toward Russian borders led to this scenario.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. determination to continue NATO's progressive expansion towards the borders of the Russian Federation has led to a scenario, with implications of unpredictable scope, which could have been avoided," the \uc2 Cuban Foreign Ministry\uc2  's statement said.\par \par \uc2 And it adds: "The military movements carried out by the United States and NATO in recent months towards regions adjacent to the Russian Federation, preceded by the delivery of modern weapons to Ukraine, which as a whole amounts to a progressive military encirclement, are well known".\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:44\par \par \uc2 "We will make sure that Putin will no longer use his war funds," warns from the \uc2 European Union\uc2  after sanctions against RussiaEuropean Commission President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  announces sanctions against Russia.\par \par \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  on Saturday took aim at Vladimir Putin as she announced new economic measures against Russia for its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "We will make sure that Putin no longer uses his war funds. We will stop \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions," the EU official said, adding that together with the United States and Canada they are prepared to "ban Russian oligarchs from using our financial markets."\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:29\par \par \uc2 The US, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and Canada applied the sanction that Russia feared most.Russia's removal from the Swift system was one of the most claimed. Photo: Reuter\par \par \uc2 The United States, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and Canada resolved Saturday to slap Russia with more sanctions for its invasion of Ukraine, including the one most feared by the Kremlin.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the leaders of those countries announced that Russian banks will be removed from the \uc2 Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial Telecommunication\uc2  known as SWIFT? the international banking network.\par \par \uc2 In addition, they announced restrictive measures that will prevent \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from deploying its international reserves; limit the sale of citizenship, so-called golden passports, which allow wealthy Russians connected to the Russian government to become citizens of other countries; and launch a task force to identify and freeze the assets of sanctioned individuals and companies. Read more here.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:08\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claims to have killed 1,000 Russian servicemen and captured 300Ukrainian soldiers take positions around a military installation as two cars burn on a street in Kiev. Photo credit: Emilio Morenatti.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claimed Saturday that its army killed more than 1,000 Russian soldiers since the start of the war launched by Vladimir Putin and to have captured more than 300 uniformed men who surrendered.\par \par \uc2 "The Russian army surrenders massively. Even senior officers surrender. Today the commander of a Russian military unit surrendered. The commander of the tank battalion also surrendered. We have already taken more than 300 regular fighters," said Oleksiy Arestovych, advisor to the Office of Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky, at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 As for the casualties suffered in the Russian ranks, the numbers are not definite he assured that there are "more than 1,000 men killed and about 2,500 wounded".\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:53\par \par \uc2 Tension continues in Kiev: sirens sound and citizens flee to sheltersSirens sounded again on Saturday night in Kiev, where a curfew is already in force.\par \par \uc2 Local authorities have urged all citizens to seek shelter in bunkers and dungeons, anticipating "heavy air strikes", according to local media.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:36\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson spoke to Zelenski and took aim at Russia: "It should be isolated diplomatically and financially".British Prime Minister Boris Johnson on Saturday spoke with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky and joined the call for more diplomatic and financial sanctions for Russia.\par \par \uc2 "Tonight I spoke with President @ZelenskyyUa . The heroism of the President and his people in defense of their country is impressive. We are clear: Russia must be isolated diplomatically and financially. I welcome greater willingness to exclude Russia from SWIFT," Johnson maintained.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:10\par \par \uc2 More than 3,000 arrested in Russia over protests against Ukraine invasion Russian police detained those demonstrating against the Russian invasion of Ukraine. Photo: EFE\par \par \uc2 More than 400 people were detained Saturday in various Russian cities in the third consecutive day of protests against the invasion of Ukraine, reported human rights NGO OVD-Info, which raised the total number of arrests since the start of the offensive to more than 3,000.\par \par \uc2 "At least 3,052 people were detained" since Thursday, including 467 this Saturday, in demonstrations that have multiplied across Russia despite being banned, the association detailed.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:54\par \par \uc2 The video published by the Russian embassy in Argentina justifying the invasion of UkraineThe Russian embassy in Argentina published this Saturday a video in which a Serbian woman who survived the NATO bombings in 1999 assures that "the top of the Russian state" is not "celebrating for having opted for military action", and warns that the government of Vladimir Putin "seeks to put a brake on NATO and its imperial arrogance".\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:35\par \par \uc2 Putin's troops are denounced for dropping "toy bombs".A toy in the rubble of an attacked building in Kiev, Ukraine. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 In the context of the violent confrontation between Ukraine and Russia that broke out with the invasion of Vladimir Putin's army, a new strategy to bomb Ukrainian cities ignited more alerts among the inhabitants of the region.\par \par \uc2 "Attention! In the Sumy area, Russian planes are scattering children's toys, cell phones and valuables filled with explosives," tweeted the Verchovna Rada, the Ukrainian parliament, warning about the new action detected in the northeastern town near the Russian border.\par \par \uc2 The denunciation is in line with what President Volodimir Zelenski had stated, who affirmed that Russia was attacking civilian populations, although Moscow affirms that its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are aimed at taking control of military targets. Read the full article here.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:15\par \par \uc2 100,000 Russian troops advance to Kiev and mayor teaches to arm Molotov cocktails to resistUkrainian soldiers walk past the remains of a burnt-out military truck on a street in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 100,000 Russian soldiers are advancing towards Kiev to try to take control of the Ukrainian capital and the mayor of the city, former world heavyweight champion Vitali Klitschko, issued an instruction for citizens to arm Molotov cocktails to defend themselves.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, in the last hours, according to the Ukrainian government, more than 25,000 weapons were distributed among the citizens, in addition to thousands of bullets, grenade launchers and grenades.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian Minister of Defense, Oleksiy Reznikov, assured today that more than 3,000 invaders were eliminated and another 200 have been captured since Thursday. "More than 55 hours of resistance. The number of prisoners of war is growing. They did not expect so much resistance and are