e Russia, expel ambassadors, oil embargo, ruin its economy. stop Russian war criminals!" he completed the message.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 03:52\par \par \uc2 A building in the center of Kiev was hit by a Russian shell A multi-storey building on Lobanovsky Avenue in central Kiev was hit by a Russian shell on Saturday with no preliminary casualties or injuries reported, according to the Ukrainian Emergency Service.\par \par \uc2 "On February 26, the State Emergency Service received information that a projectile hit a multi-storey residential building (17-18 floors) on Lobonovsky Avenue," the State Emergency Service said.\par \par \uc2 The message said, "There are no preliminary casualties and injuries. Evacuation is underway."\par \par \uc2 Members of the emergency services work in an apartment building damaged by recent shelling in Kiev, Ukraine.... REUTERS/Gleb Garanich\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 03:10\par \par \uc2 Ukraine: presidential aide reported that Russia suffered 3,500 casualties as third day of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  beginsThe losses of Russian troops in Ukraine as of this Saturday were estimated at 3,500 killed and about 200 people captured, Mikhail Podolyak, adviser to the head of the President's Office, told Ukrainian television.\par \par \uc2 "As of this morning, 3,500 people were killed and a little less than 200 were taken prisoner. If you show these people that they came to Ukraine to kill, Russia will understand what it is doing in Ukraine," he said.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:46\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  approves $350 million in military aid to UkraineU.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  approved an outlay of up to $350 million in new military aid to Ukraine in the midst of Russia's invasion.\par \par \uc2 As reported by the White House, Biden authorized the State Department to direct up to $250 million in general aid to Ukraine and up to $350 million dedicated to "defense articles and services," including military training and education.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  . Photo: AP/Alex Brandon\par \par \uc2 The announcement came after the U.S. president held a 40-minute phone conversation Friday with his Ukrainian counterpart, Volodymir Zelenski, to address military aid and sanctions issues.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 02:29\par \par \uc2 Situation in Kiev is under control, a senior Ukrainian official assured "The situation in Kiev is under control by the Armed Forces of Ukraine," Secretary of the National Security and Defense Council Oleksiy Danilov said in a message broadcast during Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 However, some clashes were still observed in Kiev. Even, the authorities called on citizens to remain calm, be careful and not to go out on the streets.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:59\par \par \uc2 Australia will impose direct sanctions on Putin for the invasion of UkraineThe Australian government on Saturday announced a new round of sanctions aimed directly on Russian President Vladimir Putin over the decision to invade Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "It is an exceptional measure to sanction leaders, but the situation is exceptional," Foreign Minister Marise Payne stressed at a press conference after returning home from a tour of Europe and Southeast Asia.\par \par \uc2 "Putin has unprecedented personal power over his country and has chosen to go to war against a neighbor who posed no threat to Russia, because he wants to reverse history and take away the freedom and democracy that the Ukrainian people chose for themselves," the Australian foreign minister said.\par \par \uc2 Russian President Vladimir Putin. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:48\par \par \uc2 Two Ukrainian cities on alert for possible airstrikesAn alert for a possible airstrike on the Ukrainian cities of Lviv and Rivne was declared Saturday .\par \par \uc2 "Airstrike in Lviv and Rivne," reads a message on the official channel.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 01:24\par \par \uc2 U.S. says ready to evacuate Zelenski from KievThe \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  says it is prepared to help Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky escape from Kiev to avoid being captured or killed by Russian forces, but the politician has so far refused to leave the capital.\par \par \uc2 According to sources cited by The Washington Post, U.S. representatives have spoken with Zelenski in recent days about security issues, including the safest places where he could take refuge to ensure the continuity of the Ukrainian government.\par \par \uc2 So far, however, the Ukrainian leader would have refused to evacuate, despite being aware of the danger.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:59\par \par \uc2 Fierce fighting" is reported in the Ukrainian town of Vasilkov Major clashes are taking place in the central streets of the Ukrainian town of Vasilkov, the mayor, Natalia Balasyanovich, told the local press.\par \par \uc2 "The streets are completely occupied with battles. Fortunately, there is good information that I cannot express on air," Balasyanovich said in a television interview.\par \par \uc2 As he indicated great help is coming to the Ukrainian armed forces. "And we see that we will win, and our glorious city of Vasilkov will definitely stand firm in this battle," emphasized the mayor, who estimated that there were 200 wounded in the Ukrainian forces.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:49\par \par \uc2 U.S. senator warned that "something is wrong with Putin".U.S. Senator Marco Rubio instantly slipped a very intriguing message warning that "something is wrong" with Vladimir Putin, amid the offensive Russia launched on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Rubio is a member of the Senate Intelligence Committee and, as such, is privy to briefings by U.S. spies.\par \par \uc2 In this context, the lawmaker tweeted that Putin's decision-making skills are not what they were five years ago and that "his problem now is different and significant."\par \par \uc2 "I wish I could share more, but for now I can say that it's pretty obvious to many that something is wrong with Putin," he said\par \par \uc2 "He has always been a killer, but his problem now is different and significant," he added.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:28\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian air force claims to have prevented Russian landing in MykolaivThe Ukrainian air force on Saturday repelled an attack on the Mykolaiv region and Russian troops did not land at the Ochakiv naval base, reported the head of the Mykolaiv Regional State Administration Vitaly Kim .\par \par \uc2 "Mykolaiv was defended. The air defense repelled the attack. The troops did not land in Ochakiv," he specified in a video message posted on the Telegram channel of the Regional State Administration.\par \par \uc2 26.02.2022\par \par \uc2 00:00\par \par \uc2 Ukraine: a Kiev commander claimed that they shot down Russian plane "Ukraine shot down a Russian aircraft, an Il-76 with paratroopers on board," the commander-in-chief of the Ukrainian air force reported in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post.\par \par \uc2 According to the brief text, the plane was shot down in Vasylkiv, near Kiev. The \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allegedly carried out in retaliation for the downing of a similar Ukrainian plane carrying paratroopers at Luhansk airport in 2014.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:50\par \par \uc2 Ukraine reports repulsing an attack on a military unit in KievUkrainian military forces repulsed a Russian attack on a military unit in Kiev on Saturday, the press center of the Armed Forces of Ukraine reported.\par \par \uc2 "The invaders attacked one of the military units in Kiev on Pobedy Avenue. The attack was repelled," the report said.\par \par \uc2 Gunshots, explosions and machine-gun bursts were heard in different parts of Kiev during the early hours of Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 23:30\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president vows to defend Ukraine from the streets of Kiev In a video posted on the social network \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski, promised to defend his country while standing on a Kiev street with other members of his government.\par \par \uc2 "Good evening everyone! The leader of the faction is here. The head of the president's administration is here. Prime Minister (Denys) Shmyhal is here. (Advisor to the head of the president's office Mykhailo) Podoliak is here. The president is here." noted in his message Zelensky.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:49\par \par \uc2 Poland and Czech Republic also close airspace to RussiaPoland and the Czech Republic adopted Bulgaria's decision, and announced the closure of airspace for Russian airlines.\par \par \uc2 The departments of both countries said the restrictions are being introduced from midnight on February 26.\par \par \uc2 "The action is being taken in connection with the escalation of the military conflict and as a sign of solidarity with Ukraine," \uc2 Bulgaria's Transport Ministry\uc2  added as it also announced the closure of its airspace\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:30\par \par \uc2 Shots fired in Kiev and attempts to destroy the thermal power plant.Shooting, explosions and machine gun bursts are taking place in different parts of Kiev as part of Russia's military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's State Service for Special Communications on Saturday reported more than 50 gunshots and explosions, as well as machine gun bursts in the area of Shulyavka and the zoo. Authorities urged the population to rush to shelters.\par \par \uc2 "Kiev. Now they are attacking a military unit in the Beresteyskaya metropolitan area," the Special State Communications Service added.\par \par \uc2 Smoke and flames rise during shelling near Kiev as Russia continues its invasion of Ukraine. REUTERS/Gleb Garanich\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:15\par \par \uc2 Ukraine announced that it is ready to talk about a ceasefire and peace"Ukraine has been and remains ready to talk about a ceasefire and peace. This is our consistent position," President Volodymyr Zelensky's spokesman Sergii Nykyforov assured on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Nykyforov's comments followed a Russian proposal to send representatives to the Belarusian capital to start negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said the Ukrainian side responded with a proposal to meet in Warsaw before breaking off contact.\par \par \uc2 Nykyforov denied what he called "claims that we have refused to negotiate."\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:04\par \par \uc2 Zelenski asked the Israeli prime minister to mediate in negotiations with Russia.It was confirmed to CNN by the Ukrainian ambassador to Israel. "Our president believes that Israel is the only democratic state that has excellent relations with both Russia and Ukraine and could be used to facilitate such negotiations," Yevgen Korniychu assured. - the ambassador even noted that Ukraine would welcome the talks to begin in Israel.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:29\par \par \uc2 UN Secretary General calls for Russian soldiers to "return to barracks".UN Secretary-General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2  on Friday called for "soldiers to return to barracks" after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, at the end of the Security Council meeting where Moscow vetoed the resolution condemning the military action.\par \par \uc2 "Soldiers must return to barracks, leaders need to return to passive dialogue and peace in Ukraine," said a solemn Guterres, who acknowledged that "today, the goal was not achieved" but we must give "another chance for peace"\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:17\par \par \uc2 Zelensky: "The fate of Ukraine is being decided right now"Volodimir Zelenski warned about the possibility of Russia's invasion of Kiev tonight.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski warned the residents of Kiev about the risk of an all-out invasion tonight. "The fate of Ukraine is being decided right now," he said in a recorded message.?"Our main goal is to end this massacre. Enemy losses are very serious: today there were hundreds of dead soldiers who crossed our border and came to our land. Unfortunately, we also suffered losses," he added.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 21:10\par \par \uc2 Cluster bomb reportedly killed 4 people in hospital in UkraineHuman Rights Watch (HRW) on Friday denounced a cluster bomb attack on a hospital in the Ukrainian town of Vuhledar, in the pro-independence area of Donetsk, that left four civilians dead and 10 others wounded, six of them medics.HRW said it had confirmed the information through telephone interviews with a doctor at the hospital and a representative of the facility, Central City Hospital, as well as photographs of two of the deceased. "This vicious attack has killed and injured civilians, and damaged a hospital," HRW weapons director Steve Goose said in a statement, calling on Russian forces to stop using cluster munitions and to "stop illegal attacks with weapons that indiscriminately kill and maim." - The organization explained that an international treaty prohibits the use of such weapons, which explode in the air and send tens or hundreds of small bombs that spread over a space similar to that of a soccer field.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:54\par \par \uc2 Russia, isolated in \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  , vetoes resolution condemning "aggression" against UkraineWith Russia's own veto and the abstention of China, India and the United Arab States, a resolution condemning the Russian invasion of Ukraine promoted by the United States and Albania in the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  was rendered ineffective on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The resolution was supported by 11 of the 15 members, but the right of veto of Russia, one of the five permanent members of the UN's highest body, along with the United States, China, France and Great Britain, left the text dead. The text, which was supported by 60 countries, urged Russia to "immediately cease the use of force" and to "refrain from any illegal threat or use of force against a UN member state".\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:46\par \par \uc2 Ukraine says it shot down Russian military plane carrying paratroopersAccording to a statement from the Army General Staff, the Il-76 heavy transport aircraft was shot down near Vasylkiv, a town 40 kilometers south of Kiev. The Russian military has not commented on the incident so far and the report could not be immediately verified.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:16\par \par \uc2 Paula Lugones\par \par \uc2 Argentina avoided condemning in the OAS Russia's invasion of UkraineLuis Almagro, secretary general of the OAS. Photo: AP\par \par \uc2 Argentina avoided condemning within the \uc2 Organization of American States\uc2  (OAS) Russia's invasion of Ukraine, which was considered by most countries in the region as "illegal, unjustified" and a "flagrant violation of international law".\par \par \uc2 In a session of the OAS Permanent Council convened virtually to analyze the crisis in Ukraine, a declaration was voted that "strongly condemns the illegal, unjustified and unprovoked invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation and calls for the "immediate withdrawal of the military presence and the cessation of any further military action in that country." Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:50\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President calls for resistance: "We cannot lose capital".Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy calls for resistance in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy said that the invading Russian army is preparing a final offensive to take Kiev, the capital, during the early hours of Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 "We cannot lose the capital. I address our defenders, men and women on all fronts: tonight, the enemy is going to use all his forces to break through our defenses in the most vile, harsh and inhuman way. Tonight, they are going to attempt an attack," Zelenski said in a video posted on the presidential website.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the Ukrainian president expressed himself on social networks about a call from France:"Emmanuel Macron just called. I must say that he is a true friend of Ukraine. France with us in the most difficult moments. Supported the disengagement of SWIFT and the introduction of personal sanctions against Putin and the supply of defense weapons. Thanks to France."\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:31\par \par \uc2 France sends military and aircraft to NATO's eastern alliesFrench President Emmanuel Macron\par \par \uc2 France will send 800 military, armored vehicles and four Mirage fighters to Eastern European countriesas part of the decisions taken this Friday at the NATO summit to deploy its Response Force in the region.\par \par \uc2 A tactical group of 500 soldiers and their equipment will be deployed in Romania, the \uc2 French Ministry of Defense\uc2  announced Friday in a communiqu\u233\'00\'E9. Local media assume that this contingent will be equipped with AMX 10 and Griffon armored vehicles.\par \par \uc2 This contingent is part of the "Spearhead" battalion of the NATO Response Force, which will be deployed for the first time for a collective defense mission. In addition, France will send 200 soldiers to Estonia, who will operate alongside British and Danish troops.\par \par \uc2 France previously had a detachment of 300 military personnel equipped with Leclerc battle tanks in Estonia, cooperating with German and British contingents, and regularly deploys fighter aircraft to the three Baltic republics for allied \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to monitor their airspace.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:23\par \par \uc2 Russia limits access to \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , accuses it of censorship, and Zuckerberg's company responds.Limitations on accessing \uc2 Facebook\uc2  in Russia. Photo: Reuters\par \par \uc2 Russia's communications watchdog (\uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  ) announced Friday limitations on logging into the social network \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , which it accused of censoring the country's media and violating the human rights of Russian citizens, while the company attributed the measure to its refusal to stop verifying information.\par \par \uc2 "In accordance with the prosecutor general's decision on the social network \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , as of February 25, \uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  adopts measures to limit its access," the agency itself said, without specifying the nature of the limitations.\par \par \uc2 The Russian regulator reproaches the U.S. giant for having restricted the official accounts on its platform of the Russian channel Zvezda, linked to the Ministry of Defense, of the public press agency Ria Novosti and of the Russian online media Lenta.ru and Gazeta.ru.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  asked Meta's administration to lift the restrictions imposed by \uc2 Facebook\uc2  on Russian media and to explain the reason for their imposition. But the request was ignored by the owners of the social network," he continued, according to the AFP news agency.\par \par \uc2 "The prosecutor's office, in consultation with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, decided to recognize \uc2 Facebook\uc2  as a social network involved in the violation of human rights and fundamental freedoms, as well as the rights and freedoms of Russian citizens," the agency said.\par \par \uc2 Following the restriction, Meta, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  's parent company, explained that the government's decision is due to the platform's refusal to stop verifying information from the media that \uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  claims to defend.\par \par \uc2 Meta's vice president, \uc2 Nick Clegg\uc2 , pointed out that the platform "verifies" the information published by these media outlets. \uc2 Facebook\uc2  assured that an external verifier - authorized by the platform but independent - found dubious information in news and videos.\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday, Russian authorities ordered us to stop verifying and alerting on content published by four Russian state-controlled media outlets," Clegg wrote. He added: "We refused. As a result, they announced that they would restrict access to our services."\par \par \uc2 Roskomnadzor\uc2  's move is part of a series of crackdowns in recent years on major social networks, generally under the guise of protecting minors and combating extremism.\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , \uc2 YouTube\uc2  , TikTok or \uc2 Twitter\uc2  were fined on several occasions, and the authorities also ordered to slow down the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:15\par \par \uc2 Ukraine asks IMF for emergency financial assistanceKiev's request to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  . Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian government has asked the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (IMF) for emergency financial assistance, the managing director of the institution, Kristalina Georgieva, revealed in a statement on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Georgieva, a Bulgarian national, explained that the Fund has held meetings remotely from Washington with the Ukrainian government, with the aim of giving it greater financial support in view of the economic consequences that the Russian invasion is already having.\par \par \uc2 Specifically, the Ukrainian Executive has asked the IMF for emergency financial assistance, and the possibility of granting such support through the $2.2 billion loan program Ukraine already has with the agency is also being explored.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:04\par \par \uc2 Canada supports the most feared sanction against RussiaCanada's Prime Minister Justin Trudeau supports the most feared sanction on Russia. Photo: Reuters\par \par \uc2 Canadian Prime Minister Justin Trudeau on Friday announced sanctions against Russian President Vladimir Putin and said his country supports the exclusion of Russia from the international SWIFT payment system in order to make it more difficult to finance the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Trudeau announced during a media appearance a third set of sanctions against Russia that include not only Putin but also his foreign minister, Sergey Lavrov.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian prime minister declared that the world is witnessing "the horrors" of the war decided by Putin and that Canada is ready to put "all options on the table" to put an end to the Russian invasion of Ukraine. Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:52\par \par \uc2 Bulgaria closes its airspace to Russian aircraftBulgaria has on Friday night closed its airspace to all Russian aircraft, a measure taken "in solidarity with Ukraine" and for an indefinite period, the \uc2 Bulgarian Transport Ministry\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "All aircrafts licensed by the Russian Federation are prohibited from entering the sovereign space of the Republic of Bulgaria, including the skies over territorial waters," reads the text of the official note.\par \par \uc2 A few moments earlier, the three mobile operators in the Balkan country (A1, Telenor and Vivacom) announced that all calls between Bulgaria and Ukraine up to 1,000 minutes will be free of charge.\par \par \uc2 The operators said they took this measure in solidarity with the population of Ukraine and the Bulgarian community in that country, which is estimated to be between 200,000 and 300,000 people.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:39\par \par \uc2 With Kiev under siege, Ukraine agreed to Russia's proposal to negotiate a ceasefireTension in Ukraine on the second day of Russian attacks. Photo:EFE\par \par \uc2 Sergey Nikiforov, presidential spokesman of Ukrainian government communicated this Friday that Ukraine accepted Russia's proposal to start negotiations, and stressed that his country is ready to talk about ceasefire and peace.\par \par \uc2 "I have to refute the claims that we refused to negotiate. Ukraine was and remains ready to talk about ceasefire and peace; this is our consistent position. We responded in accordance with the proposal of the President of Russia (Vladimir Putin)," Nikiforov stated on his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the spokesman remarked that "at this hour," the two countries are coordinating where and when they will move forward with the negotiation process. "The sooner the negotiations begin, the more chances there will be to restore normal life," he augured.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:32\par \par \uc2 Former Ukrainian Olympic boxing champion and brother of the mayor of Kiev fights on the front line Former Ukrainian Olympic and world boxing champion Vladimir Klitschko fights on the battlefront. AP Photo\par \par \uc2 Former Ukrainian Olympic and world boxing champion Vladimir Klitschko fights on the front lines to repel the invasion of Russian troops, as he had promised his older brother Vitali, also a world boxing champion and current mayor of Kiev Vladimir, 45, posted a photo showing him in combat fatigues as a Ukrainian army officer on the front lines at Hostomel airport, some 70 kilometers away from the capital Kiev.\par \par \uc2 The youngest of the Klitschko brothers (he is five years younger than Vitali, baptized as "Fists of Steel" for the power of his punches) was Olympic champion in the super heavyweight category at the Atlanta 96 Games and as a professional he reigned in the heavyweight category in the IBF, WBO and IBO, winning 23 world titles in that category?\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:25\par \par \uc2 Maria Laura Avignolo\par \par \uc2 British fighter jets carry out aerial surveillance in Poland and RomaniaBritain is no longer part of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  but remains an active member of NATO. With a Churchillian air, Prime Minister Boris Johnson did not rule out military action in the Ukraine-Russia crisis as an inevitable option.\par \par \uc2 British participation in NATO at this time is more active than that of the other partners. British fighter jets flew last night from Britain and Cyprus to carry out air surveillance missions, non-stop, in Poland and the Romanian border with Ukraine. Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:18\par \par \uc2 Like Britain, the United States says it will sanction Putin and his foreign minister Jen Psaki, the White House spokeswoman. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 The United States will sanction, like the United Kingdom and the \uc2 European Union\uc2  , Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov, White House spokeswoman Jen Psaki announced Friday.\par \par \uc2 She also indicated at a press conference that an attack against Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelensky would be "an atrocious act" on the part of the Russians.\par \par \uc2 "The United States will join (the \uc2 European Union\uc2  ) in sanctioning Putin, Foreign Minister Lavrov, and the rest of Russia's security team," Psaki said,.\par \par \uc2 Washington's sanctions come after the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) announced on Friday the freezing of Putin's and Lavrov's financial assets on European territory.\par \par \uc2 According to the White House spokeswoman, the option of sanctioning Putin has been "on the table" for some time and, in the last 24 hours, U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made the final decision after talks with his European allies.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions against Putin include a ban on travel to the United States, said Psaki, who insisted several times that details would be released later.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 18:00\par \par \uc2 Former world heavyweight champion boxer and mayor of Kiev assures that