try\uc2  . Photo: EFE/ Sergei Ilnitsky\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian authorities proposed to Russia to talk on Saturday, about possible negotiations between the parties and declined to move forward on that issue on Friday, \uc2 Russian Foreign Ministry\uc2  spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said. "The Ukrainian side refused to negotiate (this Friday). The representatives of the Kiev regime proposed to address that issue tomorrow," Zakharova said, quoted by RIA Novosti agency.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said that Ukraine avoids sitting at the negotiating table after Moscow accepted Kiev's proposal and suggested Minsk, the Belarusian capital, as the venue for talks.\par \par \uc2 According to Peskov, Ukraine proposed Warsaw as an alternative venue for the dialogue after which it "paused" and "broke off communication." "Unfortunately, that pause is accompanied by the deployment of multiple launcher systems in residential neighborhoods, including in Kiev," Peskov said at a press appearance. He added that the Kremlin sees this situation as "extremely dangerous."\par \par \uc2 In turn, Ukrainian President Volodymir Zelensky previously declared his readiness to discuss his country's neutrality in exchange for guarantees for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Russia's main security demands regarding Ukraine concern its demilitarization and that it retains its status as a neutral country, i.e. that it renounces its aspirations to join NATO.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:33\par \par \uc2 US considers Russia's negotiation offer to Ukraine "not real".Ned Price, spokesman for the US diplomacy. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 Russia's offer to hold negotiations with Ukraine is not serious, US diplomacy spokesman Ned Price said.\par \par \uc2 "We see Moscow suggesting that diplomacy be conducted at gunpoint, when Moscow's bombs, mortar fire and artillery are aimed at civilians," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen no indication that Putin is ready for de-escalation. We have seen no indication that he intends to create the conditions for a diplomatic solution," Price responded.\par \par \uc2 The spokesman criticized that "Moscow wants diplomacy to be conducted with the barrel of a gun and rockets pointed at the Ukrainian people" and stressed that those "are not conditions" for a negotiation.\par \par \uc2 "If President Putin is serious about diplomacy, he knows what he has to do: he should immediately stop shelling civilian population and withdraw troops from Ukraine," Price said.\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:19\par \par \uc2 Chinese Foreign Minister spoke about the Russia-Ukraine war: "It is something we do not want to see".Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi referred to Russia's invasion of Ukraine. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi held a telephone conversation with his British counterpart, the EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy and France's Presidency Advisor to discuss the situation in Ukraine."The current situation is something we do not want to see," the official assured.\par \par \uc2 As told byClar\u237\'00\'EDn, the Chancellor's message is in line with the talk held between Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin. Apparently, the Chinese president persuaded him to start negotiations to close the crisis. It is not clear what diplomatic tone the dialogue had. Read more here\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 17:15\par \par \uc2 Britain ordered to freeze Putin and Lavrov's moneyThe \uc2 British government\uc2  ordered on Friday to block the assets of Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov, in response to the Russian invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The British Treasury published this measure which includes the two leaders in the list of Russian oligarchs with assets or bank accounts in the United Kingdom who were sanctioned.?\par \par \uc2 The Prime Minister had already announced before the House of Commons that Britain was extending sanctions to five Russian banks and three Russian millionaires, who are already sanctioned by the United States. They are Rossiya, \uc2 IS Bank\uc2  , General Bank, \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  and Black Sea Bank.\par \par \uc2 The Russian citizens are \uc2 Gennady Timchenko\uc2  , a billionaire who controls the Volga group, Boris Rotenberg, co-owner of \uc2 SMP Bank\uc2  , and his nephew Igor Rotenberg, also sanctioned by the \uc2 US government\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 25.02.2022\par \par \uc2 16:51\par \par \uc2 UN humanitarian chief: "In 45 years of my career I have never seen a situation like this"\uc2 .Martin Griffiths\uc2  , head of the UN humanitarian office. Photo: AFP\par \par \uc2 "I've spent 45 years dealing with conflicts all over the world. (...) I have never seen a situation like this in terms of contingency planning," said \uc2 Martin Griffiths\uc2  , head of the UN humanitarian office at a press conference at UN headquarters.\par \par \uc2 "Contingency plans for what may or may not happen in Ukraine have the highest degree of uncertainty," said the UN undersecretary general, who recalled that he has worked on crises in Iraq, Cambodia, Yemen, Syria or Afghanistan, among others.\par \par \uc2 Griffiths pointed out that for the moment the \uc2 UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs\uc2  (OCHA) is designing a three-month action plan, and explained that as the days go by it will be seen whether it is necessary to extend or shorten that period of time.\par \par \uc2 Although he said that no figures are yet available on the number of people who will need help both in Ukraine and in the border countries to which Ukrainians are fleeing, he did recall that even before the conflict some 3 million people were in need of assistance in the country.\par \par \uc2 "Even before the recent events that have shaken the world this week, there has been a conflict in eastern Ukraine for eight years, and that means that three million people were already in need of help