bway as a war shelter.Tracks, platforms, stations. The subway network of Kiev, Ukraine, is one of the missile shelters set up by the government for civilians against the possibility of bombing in the capital city.Photographers of international agencies portrayed the fear of people who left their homes to go to one of the points that the authorities in a campaign that began weeks before the Russian attack.\par \par \uc2 The subway of Kiev, capital of Ukraine, as a war shelter. Photo Vyacheslav Ratynskyi/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Sleeping in the Kiev subway, the official shelter option in the Ukrainian capital in the face of the Russian attack. Photo Emilio Morenatti/AP\par \par \uc2 Another dramatic image of refugees in the Kiev subway in Ukraine. Photo Zoya Shu/AP\par \par \uc2 The subway platforms in Kiev is one of the bomb shelters set by the Ukrainian government. Photo Emilio Morenatti/AP\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:50\par \par \uc2 Martin Goldbart\par \par \uc2 "All we want is to live in peace": desperate wish of Ukrainians in Argentina.Residents prepare to take the subway, in Kiev, Ukraine, Fears and tensions on the other side of the world. Photo Sergey Starostenko / Xinhua\par \par \uc2 Ukrainians in Argentina call for a march in Recoleta against the war. They will gather this Friday at Plaza Vicente L\u243\'00\'F3pez, in Paran\u225\'00\'E1 and Arenales.The distance, the uneasiness, the fears before the bombings and the community's criticism of Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez's link with Vladimir Putin, in this note.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 22:27\par \par \uc2 Japan's economic sanctions against Russia boosts the Tokyo Stock ExchangeThe Tokyo Stock Exchange started with a 1.38% rebound of its main indicator, the Nikkei, after the imposition of new sanctions by the G7 countries, including Japan, and the European Union on Russia after its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese stock market day on Friday began with a marked upward t