nels and on social networks that the security services control in order to accuse Russia of launching indiscriminate and disproportionate attacks in an attempt to intimidate civilians and create footage for Western TV channels."\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:29\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president promises weapons to all citizens who ask for them Ukrainian President Volodomir Zelensky today promised weapons to all citizens who have combat experience and volunteer to defend the country from Russian military attack.\par \par \uc2 The president made the announcement after shelling began in several cities of the country by military forces sent by Russia.\par \par \uc2 "The future of our nation depends on every citizen of Ukraine. All those who have combat experience and can join the defense of Ukraine should immediately go to the recruitment centers of the Ministry of Internal Affairs," he said.\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:21\par \par \uc2 Postcard from the shelling: a missile in the apartmentA missile in an apartment in the city of Kharkiv, one of the military targets of the invasion launched by Vladimir Putin. (AFP Photo)\par \par \uc2 The Russian invasion left an initial toll of 40 Ukrainian soldiers and 10 civilians dead. AFP Photo\par \par \uc2 The Russian attack not only affected military installations as announced, but also civilian buildings. (AFP Photo)\par \par \uc2 24.02.2022\par \par \uc2 08:10\par \par \uc2 Fire and smoke at the Ukrainian Defense Ministry in Kiev.A photo by Reuters photojournalist Valentyn Ogirenko captured fire and smoke billowing out of the Ukrainian Defense Ministry in Kiev, where Russian shelling took place earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 Photo REUTERS/Valentyn Ogirenko\par \par \uc2 The attack announced by Vladimir Putin against Ukraine in an early morning television message began at dawn today, with heavy explosions in Odessa, Kharvik, Mariupol, Leopoli and in the capital, Kiev, where Russian forces reportedly