 of Ukraine and the government of Ukraine want peace. But if we are under attack that puts our freedom and the lives of our people at risk, we will defend ourselves."\par \par \uc2 23.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:59\par \par \uc2 Argentina called for peace without naming RussiaWithout naming Russia, Argentina made at the UN General Assembly a call for peace in Ukraine. The position was presented by the Argentine representative Fabian Oddone. "Argentina expresses its concern over the development of the situation generated in Ukraine. We are alarmed by the current crisis, as well as by the possibility of its further aggravation. It is necessary to take substantive steps to engage in a constructive and good faith dialogue in order to find a peaceful and concerted way out," he said in his speech, according to the Foreign Ministry statement. Continue reading\par \par \uc2 23.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:26\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president told why his attempt to talk to Putin failed"I initiated a telephone conversation with the president of the Russian Federation. Result: silence," Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said tonight in a message in which he assured that Russia has "almost 200,000soldiers positioned in thousands of combat vehicles" on the border with his country. He thus made public that he unsuccessfully sought a conversation with his Russian counterpart, Vladimir Putin.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy said he unsuccessfully tried to talk to Putin. Photo: Reuters\par \par \uc2 23.02.2022\par \par \uc2 20:21\par \par \uc2 "Leave the country without delay": the order of France for its citizens in Ukraine.France became the latest Western country to call on its citizens to leave Ukraine "without delay" amid growing fears that Russia is preparing a large-scale attack.\par \par \uc2 "In the context of serious tensions caused by the concentration of Russian troops on the borders with Ukraine," as well as Russian recognition of two separatist regions and the Ukrainian declaration of a state of emergency, "French citizens in Ukraine should leave the country without delay," the French Foreign Ministry said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 23.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:58\par \par \uc2 Ukraine calls for an urgent meeting of the Security CouncilForeign Minister of Ukraine Dmitro Kuleba called for a new meeting on an urgent basis of the UN Security Council.\par \par \uc2 On his Twitter account, the official explained that he called for the meeting "in view of the call by the occupying powers of Donetsk and Luhansk to ask Russia for military assistance". He considered that this represents "further escalation" in the crisis.\par \par \uc2 23.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:46\par \par \uc2 White House casts doubts on separatists' request for assistanceThe White House said the request for Russian military aid by Ukrainian separatists in the face of alleged "aggression'' by the Ukrainian government is an example of "false flag'' \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the West has consistently warned.\par \par \uc2 White House Press Secretary Jen Psaki cast doubt on the separatists' request for help. Photo: EFE\par \par \uc2 The United States and its allies have been saying for weeks that Russia will try to create a pretext for an invasion of Ukraine by using such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 White House Press Secretary Jen Psaki said the Kremlin's announcement Wednesday that Ukrainian separatists are asking for help "is an example'' of such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 23.02.2022\par \par \uc2 19:34\par \par \uc2 Another sharp fall on Wall StreetStocks in New York recorded another sharp drop in their prices as a result of investors' doubts regarding the conflict in Ukraine, and due to what several analysts consider to be mild sanctions imposed by the West on Moscow, following the invasion of Russian troops into Ukrainian territory.\p