\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Volatility grips markets: stock markets rise and oil stabilizes amid Russian troops' advance into Kiev\b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Volatility is taking markets that seem to have gone on a roller coaster ride in the wake of the Russian attack in Ukraine. Yesterday the stock markets collapsed with the announcement of the military offensive, but towards the end of the day they recovered while oil prices fell back sharply after having surpassed the US$ 100 barrier.\par \par \uc2 This change in trend was influenced by the speech of US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who, although he reaffirmed tough sanctions against Moscow by the West, gave no indication of sending troops to Ukraine, alleviating an escalation of the conflict.\par \par \uc2 This boosted Wall Street and relieved investors.\par \par \uc2 Europe's stock markets are up more than 1% at the moment, but have shown several oscillations amid the advance of Russian troops into Ukrainian territory, reaching as far as the capital, Kiev.\par \par \uc2 In this context, the Moscow Stock Exchange is up more than 22% after the collapse of more than 33% it suffered the day before, which forced it to close its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden threatened with limitations on the importation of technology, blockades to large banks and punishments to oligarchs close to Putin. However, he was not entirely clear on the energy issue, nor did he remove Russia from the SWIFT system, which allows transfers in dollars and euros to the country.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, soared 2.3% against the dollar to 83.30 units, after touching an all-time low of 89.60. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported by the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2014, when Russia annexed Crimea from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reported CincoD\u237\'00\'EDas The market expects more action from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has to address inflationary risks.\par \par \uc2 What will happen to equities in the immediate?\par \par \uc2 "We lowered our conviction on the recommendation and moved from an overweight in equities to neutral. There was a change and the current status quo, with Western countries decreeing sanctions and Russia being in Ukraine, can be maintained for a while and generate additional volatility," Crist\u243\'00\'F3bal Doberti, \uc2 Sura Asset Management\uc2 's Regional Manager of Savings and Investment Strategies, told Pulso.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices, on the other hand, stabilized and registered practically no variations in relation to the previous day. Brent is quoted at US$ 99.12 while WTI is quoted at US$ 92.68. In any case, both benchmarks are at their highest levels since 2014.\par \par \uc2 Crude oil prices are sensitive for Chile as it imports more than 90% of what it consumes and high hydrocarbon prices have become the engine of inflation in several economies around the world. It should be recalled that in the country, gasoline and gas prices are at historic highs.\par \par \uc2 "War conflicts are difficult to forecast. Historically, when there are rumors of this type of conflicts, the worst day for the markets is the moment when it starts, but then the markets recover, it has happened with Vietnam and the annexation of Crimea by Russia, and in the months following these conflicts the markets have a positive performance. here is the inflation issue. Although here it is not exactly the same, because the issue of rates and inflation is hanging around," Francisco Errandonea, partner of Focus Capital, told Pulso.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2p005o1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
