\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russia ramps up aid to banks,  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market after invasion of Ukraine\b0\par\par\uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par 16:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Russian rouble, assets in free-fall after Putin orders troops into \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Russian c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for first time since 2014\par \par \uc2 * Offers extra \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rouble liquidity for banks\par \par \uc2 * Finmin stops new OFZ bonds offering for the upcoming weeks\par \par \uc2 * Stress-tests show financial market, top companies ready for sanctions, finmin says (Adds details, quotes, background, releads)\par \par \uc2 By Elena Fabrichnaya and Katya Golubkova\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 24 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  beefed up the banking sector with extra liquidity and started to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the rouble fell to all-time lows on the day Moscow sent its troops into Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of denying plans to attack neighbouring Ukraine, Russian forces fired missiles at several cities in Ukraine and landed troops on its coast on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The United States promised harsh sanctions, covering everything from Russia's top banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollars to the energy sector should Moscow invade its neighbour.\par \par \uc2 And as Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bonds and stocks all tanked, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 2014, when Russia annexed the Crimea peninsula from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear how much \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling but the rouble pared some losses and moved away from an all-time low of 89.60 against the dollar and a crucial threshold of 100 versus the euro it was approaching in the morning.\par \par \uc2 "The military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine makes harsh sanctions unavoidable," Raiffeisenbank said in a note. "The rouble crash was stopped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  but its potential for further weakening remains high."\par \par \uc2 The regulator might have spent between $1 billion and $2 billion to support the rouble on Thursday, according to \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  analysts. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to disclose the sum on Monday.\par \par \uc2 It also nearly doubled daily dollar offers under \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with banks to $5 billion, provided another 874 billion roubles ($10 billion) at a daily repo auction and expanded collateral options for its funds to secure its 300 lenders with additional funds.\par \par \uc2 As a precaution before the sanctions, Russian lenders brought $5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank notes to the country in December and increased liquidity coverage of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets last month.\par \par \uc2 State-owned \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  and \uc2 VTB\uc2  both said their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued as usual on Thursday, but the latter urged its corporate clients to refrain from dollar and euro transactions.\par \par \uc2 A number of Muscovites experienced troubles in withdrawing dollars and euros from ATMs in the centre of the city, and a cash machine in Moscow's northeast stopped operating after a Reuters witness withdrew 20,000 roubles.\par \par \uc2 But no big ATM queues were seen in Moscow on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT PLEDGES CONTROL\par \par \uc2 While Russian officials say that Moscow's financial shield is strong enough to withstand both the volatility and sanctions, new curbs would "weaken Russia's economic base and its capacity to modernise", \uc2 European Commission\uc2  chief \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Russia ran a historic high current account surplus of $120.3 billion last year, its gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stand at a record $643 billion and debt-to-GDP level is below 20%.\par \par \uc2 "Russia has financial resources enough to maintain the financial system in the light of sanctions and external threats," the government said on Thursday, adding that the budget has over 4.5 trillion roubles in available extra funds.\par \par \uc2 The government drew up specific plans after conducting stress-tests to assess possible sanctions, saying in the statement that the "financial market and largest companies are fully ready to implement them". It did not provide details.\par \par \uc2 But a Moscow real estate company urged its staff in an email marked 'IMPORTANT' on Thursday to use cards connected to the domestic MIR payment system, set up as an alternative to the western Visa and \uc2 MasterCard\uc2  payment systems after 2014.\par \par \uc2 "We recommend all our staff members to move their salary payments to the cards using this payment system," the letter seen by Reuters said, adding that a decision to open such cards in \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , \uc2 VTB\uc2  and AlfaBank should be taken by the end of the day. (Additional reporting by Andrey Ostroukh, Oksana Kobzeva, Dmitry Antonov, Darya Korsunskaya, Alexander Marrow and Olesya Astakhova Writing by Katya Golubkova Editing by Kim Coghill, Kenneth Maxwell, Emelia Sithole-Matarise and Nick Macfie) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-2-24T16:21:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220224ei2o01meu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
