\par\par \b \uc2 Russia Attack Roils Markets; Defense Stocks Rally -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 1,846 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par 12:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Caitlin Ostroff, Anna Hirtenstein and Quentin Webb \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors rushed for safety, pushing down stocks and lifting the prices of oil, gold and government bonds, after Russian missiles and airstrikes hit Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, and more than a dozen other cities across the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Futures tied to the S&P 500, Nasdaq-100 and Dow Jones Industrial Average fell between 2.5% and 3%. The S&P 500 reached correction territory earlier in the week, and futures are indicating the Dow is on track to do the same. Nasdaq futures are pointing to the index approaching a bear market.\par \par \uc2 The Russian attack -- swiftly condemned by President Biden -- heightens the pressure on a global economy already reeling from snarled supply chains and some of the highest inflation in years, with Europe likely to bear the brunt of the economic impact.\par \par \uc2 "This is what appeared unbelievable to most investors, and this is actually happening," said Slava Smolyaninov, Moscow-based chief strategist at BCS Global Markets. "It's a complete change of everything; we are in a different world right now."\par \par \uc2 The pan-continental Stoxx Europe 600 fell over 3%. The MOEX benchmark for Russian stocks tumbled 30%, putting it on course for its biggest drop on record. Asian stock indexes also fell sharply, with Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index dropping over 3%, and Japan's Nikkei Stock Average closing at its lowest since November 2020.\par \par \uc2 The Russian ruble weakened to a record low, declining as much as 9% against the dollar and trading at 90 rubles to $1, before recovering moderately. The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and banned short selling.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market suspended its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  under martial law measures, according to a statement from its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The country's stock exchange also said it was postponing activity.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, the global benchmark, topped $100 a barrel for the first time since 2014, with the front-month contract rising 8.4% to $104.94. Prices for its U.S. equivalent, West Texas Intermediate, also jumped.\par \par \uc2 Other commodities markets also convulsed. Natural-gas futures in Europe surged 31% and benchmark prices for aluminum and nickel, two metals for which Russia is a major producer, rose to their highest levels in about a decade. Wheat and corn futures also advanced to multiyear highs, since both Russia and Ukraine are major grain producers.\par \par \uc2 "We thought Putin's strategy was largely around negotiation; this was the consensus among investors. We haven't had any serious military conflict in Europe for a very long time so there's no playbook for this, " said \uc2 Gregory Perdon\uc2 , chief investment officer at \uc2 Arbuthnot Latham\uc2 . "A lot has changed since last night."\par \par \uc2 Gold and \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds, which both typically rally in times of stress, rose in price. The most actively traded gold futures contract added 3.3%, to about $1,973 a troy ounce, the highest level since September 2020.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  note declined to 1.858% from 1.976% on Wednesday. Bond yields fall as prices rise. European government bonds also rallied, with the equivalent German bund yield falling as low as 0.111%.\par \par \uc2 The dollar strengthened, with the WSJ Dollar Index gaining 0.8%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  considered to be havens, such as the Japanese yen, also appreciated, while cryptocurrencies tumbled, with bitcoin falling nearly 7% to about $35,000.\par \par \uc2 Investors are building up their cash buffers due to the market stress, said Florian Ielpo, head of macro at Lombard Odier Investment Managers. The funds he manages currently hold the most cash since the market crash in March 2020.\par \par \uc2 The invasion reverberated in markets in Eastern Europe and Turkey. The Polish zloty and the Hungarian forint both depreciated 2.5% against the dollar. The Turkish lira fell 3.7%. Polish bank stocks tumbled, with \uc2 PKO Bank Polski\uc2  falling 13.5%. \uc2 Wizz Air\uc2 , an airline with its key markets in Eastern Europe, declined over 11%.\par \par \uc2 Shares of other European companies with sizable \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Russia also plunged. Austria's \uc2 Raiffeisen Bank\uc2 , which had over 20% of its workforce in Russia at the end of 2021, declined 17%. \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  fell 9% and \uc2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2  slid 11.5%. French car maker \uc2 Renault\uc2 , which also has a large Russian subsidiary, fell nearly 10%.\par \par \uc2 Defense stocks rallied, with \uc2 BAE Systems\uc2  rising 5.4%. U.S.-listed \uc2 Northrop Grumman\uc2  climbed 8.8% and \uc2 Lockheed Martin\uc2  added 3.4% in premarket trading.\par \par \uc2 The Russian attack comes at a time where volatility in markets was heightened, due to looming changes in Federal Reserve monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 "The game-changer for me is, what does this mean for the Fed? Ultimately now, interest rate hikes and aggressive tightening are going to be very difficult," Mr. Perdon said.\par \par \uc2 Amid the chaos, Chinese e-commerce giant \uc2 Alibaba\uc2  and vaccine-maker Moderna are expected to post earnings ahead of the opening bell. \uc2 Beyond Meat\uc2 , \uc2 Etsy\uc2  and cryptocurrency exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  are scheduled to report after markets close.\par \par \uc2 The latest data on U.S. weekly jobless claims are expected at 8:30 a.m. ET. Economists expect the number to edge down amid the tight labor market, after it rose unexpectedly last week.\par \par \uc2 -- Megumi Fujikawa and William Horner contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Caitlin Ostroff at caitlin.ostroff@wsj.com, Anna Hirtenstein at anna.hirtenstein@wsj.com and Quentin Webb at quentin.webb@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 24 Feb 2022 09:32 ET  Russian Attack on Ukraine Roils Markets -- WSJ\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Anna Hirtenstein, Caitlin Ostroff and Quentin Webb \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors rushed for safety, pushing down stocks and lifting the prices of oil, gold and government bonds, after Russian missiles and airstrikes hit Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, and more than a dozen other cities across the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 831 points, or 2.5%, shortly after the opening bell. The S&P 500 dropped 2.5% and the Nasdaq Composite declined 3.3%. The S&P 500 reached correction territory earlier in the week. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cboe\f28 \uc2 \f2  Volatility Index rose to the highest level in over 15 months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian attack -- swiftly condemned by President Biden -- heightens the pressure on a global economy already reeling from snarled supply chains and some of the highest inflation in years, with Europe likely to bear the brunt of the economic impact.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is what appeared unbelievable to most investors, and this is actually happening," said Slava Smolyaninov, Moscow-based chief strategist at BCS Global Markets. "It's a complete change of everything; we are in a different world right now."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pan-continental Stoxx Europe 600 fell 3.7%. The MOEX benchmark for Russian stocks tumbled 32%, putting it on course for its biggest drop on record. Asian stock indexes also fell sharply, with Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index dropping over 3%, and Japan's Nikkei Stock Average closing at its lowest since November 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian ruble weakened to a record low, declining as much as 9% against the dollar and trading at 90 rubles to $1, before recovering moderately. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and banned short selling.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market suspended its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  under martial law measures, according to a statement from its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The country's stock exchange also said it was postponing activity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brent crude oil, the global benchmark, topped $100 a barrel for the first time since 2014, with the front-month contract rising 7.1% to $100.67. Prices for its U.S. equivalent, West Texas Intermediate, also jumped.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other commodities markets also convulsed. Natural-gas futures in Europe surged 40% and benchmark prices for aluminum and nickel, two metals for which Russia is a major producer, rose to their highest levels in about a decade. Wheat and corn futures also advanced to multiyear highs, since both Russia and Ukraine are major grain producers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We thought Putin's strategy was largely around negotiation; this was the consensus among investors. We haven't had any serious military conflict in Europe for a very long time so there's no playbook for this, " said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gregory Perdon\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief investment officer at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Arbuthnot Latham\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "A lot has changed since last night."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold and \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds, which both typically rally in times of stress, rose in price. The most actively traded gold futures contract rose 2.5% to about $1,957 a troy ounce, the highest level since September 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  note declined to 1.893% from 1.976% on Wednesday. Bond yields fall as prices rise. European government bonds also rallied, with the equivalent German bund yield falling as low as 0.111%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar strengthened, with the WSJ Dollar Index gaining 1%. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  considered to be havens, such as the Japanese yen, also appreciated, while cryptocurrencies tumbled, with bitcoin falling 6% to about $35,350.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are building up their cash buffers due to the market stress, said Florian Ielpo, head of macro at Lombard Odier Investment Managers. The funds he manages currently hold the most cash since the market crash in March 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The invasion reverberated in markets in Eastern Europe and Turkey. The Polish zloty, Hungarian forint and Turkish lira all depreciated around 3% against the dollar. Polish bank stocks tumbled, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 PKO Bank Polski\f28 \uc2 \f2  falling 15%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wizz Air\f28 \uc2 \f2 , an airline with its key markets in Eastern Europe, declined 14%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of other European companies with sizable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Russia also plunged. Austria's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Raiffeisen Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which had over 20% of its workforce in Russia at the end of 2021, declined over 18%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\f28 \uc2 \f2  both slid 11%. French car maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Renault\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which also has a large Russian subsidiary, fell over 10%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Defense stocks rallied, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BAE Systems\f28 \uc2 \f2  rising 6%. U.S.-listed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Northrop Grumman\f28 \uc2 \f2  climbed 3% in premarket trading.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian attack comes at a time where volatility in markets was heightened, due to looming changes in Federal Reserve monetary policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The game-changer for me is, what does this mean for the Fed? Ultimately now, interest rate hikes and aggressive tightening are going to be very difficult," Mr. Perdon said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market expectations for a 0.5 percentage point increase at the Fed's meeting next month, rather than a more standard 0.25 percentage point increase, declined Thursday. Market pricing showed the probability fell to 17% from 34% the day before, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weekly U.S. jobless claims came in at 232,000, a decline from the previous week and in line with analysts' expectations amid a tight labor market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beyond Meat\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Etsy\f28 \uc2 \f2  and cryptocurrency exchange \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coinbase\f28 \uc2 \f2  are scheduled to report earnings after markets close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Megumi Fujikawa and William Horner contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Anna Hirtenstein at anna.hirtenstein@wsj.com, Caitlin Ostroff at caitlin.ostroff@wsj.com and Quentin Webb at quentin.webb@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 24, 2022 09:32 ET (14:32 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220224ei2o001mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
