\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Top Russian lender \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  ready for anything as sanctions loom\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Marrow\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Russia's largest lender \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  said on Thursday that it was prepared for any developments as the threat of sanctions grew after Russian forces attacked Ukraine, sending shares in Russian banks crashing.\par \par \uc2 Russian forces invaded Ukraine by land, air and sea on Thursday, confirming the worst fears of the West with the biggest attack by one state against another in Europe since World War Two.\par \par \uc2 A senior U.S. administration official told reporters on Tuesday that \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  and No. 2 lender \uc2 VTB\uc2  would face U.S. sanctions if Moscow proceeded with its invasion of Ukraine, warning that no Russian financial institutions were safe.\par \par \uc2 "We are prepared for any development of the situation and have worked through scenarios for guaranteeing that our customers funds, assets and interests are protected, and also that our functions are fully \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 VTB\uc2  said its branches, ATMs and online services were functioning normally.\par \par \uc2 Both banks previously declined to comment on potential sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Moscow-listed shares of both banks underperformed the wider market, which had lost around 33%. \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  shares were down 49.4% as of 1132 GMT - its lowest in six years, while \uc2 VTB\uc2  shares dropped 41.3%, earlier hitting an all-time low.\par \par \uc2 Online bank Tinkoff, whose London-listed shares fell 45.2%, said its systems were running smoothly.\par \par \uc2 "Tinkoff has sufficient liquidity," the bank, which is not state-owned, but is listed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as one of 13 systemically important banks in Russia, said.\par \par \uc2 "We are seeing increased demand for cash withdrawals and are replenishing ATMs on a reinforced schedule."\par \par \uc2 The rouble bounced off all-time lows on Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered Russian forces to invade \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move expected to trigger new harsh sanctions against Moscow.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alexander Marrow and Elena Fabrichnaya; Editing by Katya Golubkova and Kim Coghill and Elaine Hardcastle) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-2-24T12:54:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220224ei2o02ybt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
