\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russian stock exchange resumes trading with a 45.2% drop\b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Moscow Stock Exchange resumed trading after the temporary pause following President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's announcement on the start of military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which began with a 45.2% plunge according to an official statement.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday morning the Moscow Stock Exchange reported a temporary suspension of all its trading on the trading floor until further notice.\par \par \uc2 The Moscow Stock Exchange has suspended trading on all its markets until further notice," the exchange's management said in a brief statement.\par \par \uc2 The stock exchange had closed the previous session with a drop of 1.84%.\par \par \uc2 The stocks that fell the most at the resumption of the Stock Exchange were Rosneft(58.5 %, EN+ (58.3 %) and \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  (57 %).\par \par \uc2 Measures to stabilize the financial market Due to the military tensions between Russia and Ukraine in recent weeks, the MOEXindex lost 52.13 % in the last month and 55.37 % in the last year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2  announced Thursday that it will take additional measures for the stabilization of the financial market following the 10 % fall of the ruble, the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the announcement about the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia will ensure financial stability and uninterrupted continuity of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of financial organizations," the Russian monetary institution said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  today surpassed the mark of almost 90 rubles to the dollar and 101 to the euro for Russian actions in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Sber guaranteed interest protection The fall of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks began on February 21, after the announcement about Moscow'srecognition of the separatist republics of Donbas.\par \par \uc2 The volatility of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also reached the highest level since the beginning of the covid-19 pandemic and pushed the Turkish lira out of first place.\par \par \uc2 Russia's largest bank, Sber, also assured today that it is "prepared for any development of the situation" and that they have all the necessary resources and expertise to keep the situation under control and ensure the protection of their clients' interests.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220224ei2o004yc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
