\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Kazakh tenge falls more than 2% vs dollar on Ukraine escalation\b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2022\par 12:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds stocks, president's comments at security council meeting)\par \par \uc2 ALMATY, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The Kazakh tenge dropped more than 2% against the dollar on Tuesday, tracking the Russian rouble which earlier came under pressure due to the escalation of the crisis over \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  recognised two breakaway regions in eastern Ukraine and has since ordered the deployment of troops there, deepening Western fears of a major war in Europe.\par \par \uc2 The tenge, which traded at around 438 to the dollar on Tuesday, its weakest in two months, often tracks the movements of the rouble, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kazakhstan's neighbour and former Soviet overlord.\par \par \uc2 "According to our estimates, the rouble may firmly settle in the 75-80 (roubles per dollar) range and we do not expect short-term spikes above 85," said Yevgeny Vinokurov, chief economist at the \uc2 Eurasian Development Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Since Russia is Kazakhstan's key trading partner, this directly impacts the tenge-dollar rates."\par \par \uc2 Kazakhstan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $33 million from its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on the domestic market on Tuesday to ease the pressure on the tenge.\par \par \uc2 The rouble hit its weakest level in nearly two years earlier on Tuesday before rebounding after Moscow said it would only recognise the regions' independence within the boundaries currently under the control of Moscow-backed separatists and Ukraine played down the prospect of a large-scale conflict with Russia.\par \par \uc2 Umut Shayakhmetova\uc2 , chief executive of Kazakhstan's biggest lender \uc2 Halyk Bank\uc2 , said the Ukraine crisis would certainly impact the country.\par \par \uc2 "The question is whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to support (the tenge) at some point but, as we know, you can't support it for too long as you start burning \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves, which are finite," Shayakhmetova said.\par \par \uc2 Halyk GDRs were up 1.3% in London around 1115 GMT, but two other major Kazakh companies - fintech firm \uc2 Kaspi.kz\uc2  and uranium miner \uc2 Kazatomprom\uc2  - were down 3.1% and 1.7% respectively.\par \par \uc2 Kazakh President \uc2 Kassym-Jomart Tokayev\uc2  held an urgent security council meeting on Tuesday where he ordered the cabinet and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come up with an anti-crisis plan on how to react to the international security crisis and sanctions fallout. (Reporting by Mariya Gordeyeva and Olzhas Auyezov; Editing by Kevin Liffey and Raissa Kasolowsky) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-2-22T12:59:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220222ei2m01uz5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
