\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Stock market falls amid China's  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  on ore,  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  crisis and US inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 International pressures on the main basic materials produced by Brazil pushed down in early afternoon this Thursday (17) the shares of the most important companies to the Stock Exchange of the country. The scenario became even more unfavorable for business amid the falls in major global markets, a situation enhanced by investor pessimism about the tensions involving Russia and Ukraine and also about inflation in the United States.\par \par \uc2 At 12:45 pm, the Ibovespa was down? 1.15%, at 113,849 points. Thus, the benchmark index of the Stock Exchange was on its way to interrupt a cycle of seven consecutive daily highs. The dollar rose 0.79%, to R$ 5.17.\par \par \uc2 The\par \par \uc2 American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, remains close to the lowest quotations since the beginning of the second half of last year.\par \par \uc2 A worker in an iron and steel foundry in an industry located in Dalian, China - Stringer - 17.Jul.2018/Reuters The main source of the Brazilian stock market's fall is in the commodities sector, as described by Pietra Guerra, Clear Corretora's stock specialist, in her bulletin to investors on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of appreciation at the beginning of 2022, the prices of iron ore contracts fell rapidly in recent days. China, the main consumer of this raw material, has decided to tighten its grip on values.\par \par \uc2 "The Chinese government is investigating irregular \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid artificial adjustments in prices and, somehow, wants to limit gains from speculation," commented the Clear analyst.\par \par \uc2 Guerra points out that the shares of companies in the mining and steel sector, which represent more than 20% of the trading volume of Ibovespa, tend to respond to the ore price. \uc2 Vale\uc2  fell more than 3%.\par \par \uc2 MORE INVESTMENT NEWS Stock markets, dollar and companies: follow the market live After having surpassed the 115 thousand points on the day before, the Brazilian Stock Exchange would naturally face a technical difficulty to continue high on Thursday, as the recent gains generate a selling pressure. Investors tend to seek the realization of profits made recently, as explained Nicolas Borsoi, chief economist at Nova Futura.\par \par \uc2 Abroad, the continued movement of Russian troops on the Ukrainian border amplified the tension about a potential armed conflict in Europe. Russia is a major oil and gas producer and a worsening crisis could hurt supply and further accelerate global inflation. "It is a challenging combination for Ibovespa," Borsoi said.\par \par \uc2 Despite hovering around the highest quotations in seven years, the barrel of Brent oil retreated 2.35%, at US$92.58 (R$477.93). Analysts attribute the drop to the possibility that Iran will once again be accepted by Western powers as a supplier of the commodity due to advances in negotiations over the country's nuclear program.\par \par \uc2 For Brazil, the drop in oil prices is reflected in the devaluation of shares of \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , which fell more than 1%.\par \par \uc2 In the American market, investors started the day reacting to the crisis involving Ukraine and evaluating the minutes of the January meeting of the Fed (Federal Reserve, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the United States) on the next steps of monetary tightening to control the highest inflation in 40 years.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones, S&P 500, and Nasdaq indices were down 1.33%, 1.38%, and 1.64%, in that order.\par \par \uc2 The Fed minutes showed that advisers agreed that, with inflation extending its impact on the economy and a tight labor market, it was time to raise interest rates and decrease asset purchases in the financial market.\par \par \uc2 They said, however, that decisions would be made depending on the scenario at the time of each group meeting. The January meeting was the first of eight scheduled for this year.\par \par \uc2 Although the U.S. market is still in the period of disclosure of corporate balance sheets for the fourth quarter of 2021, the attention of investors is fully focused on the crisis in Europe and interest rate hikes, said the global head of equities at Federated Hermes, Geir Lode, to Bloomberg.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220217ei2h00852\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
