\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Lira in free fall on fears of lower interest rates, sinks below 12 a dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2021\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Lira could hit 13 per dollar - analyst\par \par \uc2 * Russian, Ukrainian bonds slide on war rumblings\par \par \uc2 * Belarusian rouble at over 3-month low\par \par \uc2 By Susan Mathew\par \par \uc2 Nov 23 (Reuters) - The lira slumped 8% to a record low of 12.49 versus the dollar on Tuesday on intensifying worries about Turkey's unconventional monetary policy, while Russia's rouble recovered but worries about a war with Ukraine kept it at four-month lows.\par \par \uc2 Turkish President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , long demanding stimulus to spur economic growth, defended lower policy rates on Monday, vowing to succeed in his "economic war of independence". The policy rate now stands at 15% while inflation runs at 20%.\par \par \uc2 Speculation that Erdogan might soon replace Finance and Economy Minister \uc2 Lutfi Elvan\uc2  further fanned worries.\par \par \uc2 The lira is now down more than 37% against the dollar in 2021, significantly lagging other emerging market peers, with volatility gauges spiking.\par \par \uc2 "We would have to really start to see strains building in the banking sector before we might get a change in course. So far banks have been weathering this really well. So long as that remains the case, I suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not raise rates," said \uc2 Jason Tuvey\uc2 , senior EM economist at Capital Economics, adding the lira may fall beyond 13.\par \par \uc2 Russia's rouble recovered 0.5% against the greenback after sliding close to 75 last session on Western concerns over possible Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market sell-off hit Russian OFZ treasury bonds. Yields on 10-year benchmark OFZs soared to 8.63% this week, a level last seen in early 2019.\par \par \uc2 The United States imposed further sanctions in connection with the \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2  gas pipeline on Monday, targeting Russia-linked Transadria Ltd and its vessel.\par \par \uc2 "In the event that Russia does try to make an incursion into Ukraine, the risk of sanctions would escalate quite quickly if the rouble does come under severe pressure, we might see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping with interest rate hikes," said Tuvey.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine dollar bonds slumped to one year lows.\par \par \uc2 In Belarus, the rouble hit over three-month lows as a migrant crisis deepened. Austria said Europe must not be blackmailed into accepting thousands of migrants stranded on its border with Belarus, after Belarusian President \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2  threatened war if the crisis goes "too far".\par \par \uc2 Risk sentiment was more broadly hit after U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  picked Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  to lead for another term, raising bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may tighten policy faster than expected, which could pull funds away from EM assets.\par \par \uc2 EM stocks hit six-week lows, with some gains in mainland China, India, Turkey and Russian stocks capping losses.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in developing economies ramping up interest rates will be supportive for emerging market debt, but could spell trouble for equities, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance in 2021, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance in 2021, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX}}}\par \par \uc2 For TOP NEWS across emerging markets\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; Editing by William Maclean) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-11-23T10:43:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211123ehbn01ep1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
