uced cost levels can be delivered.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Post tax nominal Rouble discount rate of 13.5%. This was based on a Capital Asset Pricing Model analysis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Based on the key assumptions set out above YGE's recoverable amount ($90.9m) exceeds it carrying amount of CGU's assets ($89.2m) by $1.7m and therefore YGE's Koshekhablskoye gas field was not impaired.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The impact on the impairment calculation of applying different assumptions to gas prices, production, future capital and operating expenditure and post-tax discount rates, all other inputs remaining equal, would be as follows: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                                                                     Increase/(decrease) in headroom of \par                                                                                           $1.7m for Yuzhgazenergie CGU \par                                                                                                                     $m \par Impact of Adygean gas price:             growth rates increased by 10% annually                                    3.0 \par                                            growth rates reduced by 10% annually                                  (2.8) \par  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------  ------------------------------------- \par Impact of production volumes:                                  Increased by 10%                                   16.0 \par                                                                Decreased by 10%                                 (16.0) \par  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------  ------------------------------------- \par Impact of future capital expenditure:                          Increased by 20%                                    4.0 \par                                                                Decreased by 20%    